h.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:28:07-07:00","id":971637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=971611#post971611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, pretty much the CEO of Buzzfeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could say that, but replace the SJW aspects with a Troma film style trashiness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:23:23-07:00","id":972338,"title":"","content":"17) A Hermetic of House Thig/Verditus who was the product of a secret government cloning experiment that went nowhere (feel free to use this to justify any sort of Merit or Flaw you wish, as a result of the selective breeding). When the project shut down, the Hermetic and twelve of his surviving &quot;siblings&quot; were placed in homes across the country. After being picked up and trained by the Order of Hermes, the new Hermetic decided to take to the road, looking for his fellow clones. He drives a magically enhanced sports car, with a suped up engine and a Trunk of Holding, and the ability to use Correspondence to cut down on travel time. Because all his fellow clones share the same genetic lineage, they share a Sympathetic connection, through which he can track them all down. A compass sits on his dashboard, dowsing towards the closest &quot;sibling&quot;. Our Hermetic wanderer won't rest until he's met and dealt with his &quot;family&quot;...one way or another. Not all of them look forward to a family reunion...and not all of them are nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T22:36:48-07:00","id":972359,"title":"","content":"18) 16 years old and an Adept of Spirit, Siduri was born to an Awakened mother in the Axis Mundi realm of the High Umbra. She has spent her entire life in the spirit worlds. With her mother Kishar she has climbed the World Tree, descended to the Babylonian underworld of Irkalla, and debated masters of rhetoric in the Philosopher Kingdoms. Now she is an adult and no longer required to stay with her mother in exile. After traveling through many of the worlds dreamt of by humanity, her next journey will be the most challenging adventure yet: Subur, otherwise known as Earth. It is not yet known if her mother's old Hermetic Chantry will welcome her. If she will find her way in such an alien place as this one that most of her fellow humans know as home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T00:12:14-07:00","id":974271,"title":"","content":"19) A Syndicate rep who is not entirely dedicated to the party line in terms of his methods and activities. Maybe it's his Primordial Eidolon, or perhaps he's just seen the superstitionists and Reality Deviants in action one too many times. Regardless, he can't fully put his faith in Enlightened Science to explain the world...or to protect it. He still does the hypereconomics and the art of desire, he's decided to hedge his bets, and shop around a bit. He's come to understand that mystics adorn themselves with the symbols of animals, in order to channel their power. The way he does it is more subtle, of course - he's more likely to wear a scorpion pin on his suit, lion-pattern socks, and alligator skin shoes, than actually run around with a wolf pelt on his head. If anyone asks, he cites the psychological effects of identifying with beasts than any type of sympathetic resonance. He certainly would never use such articles to spontaneously grow claws. Something eccentric, but nothing overtly unscientific.<br /> <br /> Of much greater concern - if anyone found out about it - is his delving into Spirit. Not necessarily Dimensional Science, but outright SPIRIT. The way he figures, extradimensional entities are just another rational (or irrational) actor that he can cut a deal with. Or else, a resource to exploit. He prefers to communicate and arrange &quot;meetings&quot; (summoning) with his &quot;business associates&quot; through the medium of computers and conference calls. And, like any business person, he treats the negotiations like a business deal. He prepares the finest food and drink, wards himself with a table sitting between him and the spirits, and seals the deal with a written contract. Naturally, these covert activities are massively unmutual, and likely to get him in hot water if his superiors ever find out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:42:36-07:00","id":988101,"title":"","content":"Here's another one, this time with an even longer description. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <br /> 20) <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/the_vault/2013/09/13/puritan_names_lists_of_bizarre_religious_nomenclature_used_by_puritans.html\" target=\"_blank\">Kill-sin</a> &quot;Boy&quot; Bright is a young man in conflict with himself.<br /> <br /> Born at a crossroads at dusk on All Hallows Eve, Kill-sin was the son of a New England Puritan pastor and his wife. The latter turned out to be a witch, and Kill-sin's father, Obedience Exalt-God Bright, would have condemned her to the community's judgement (and almost certainly an execution after), had his heart not overrode his sense of duty. Instead, he banished her from the town quietly, so as to satisfy his religious obligation and spare her life. Perhaps because of this lapse, Father Bright doubled down on his strict moralism in regards to his son, raising Kill-sin in a firm manner.<br /> <br /> Naturally, Kill-sin reacted to this treatment with rebellion. A crafty child with a streak of mischief in his heart, he made himself a toublemaker. Subsequent corporal punishment taught Kill-sin to be more careful, but didn't dampen his spirit. Eventually, he learned that his mother still lived, and traveled to the outskirts of the local village to visit her shack. His mother, Nevermore, quickly took a shine to the boy, and offered to teach him witchcraft, as was his birthright. Naturally, he jumped at the chance. His days were filled with feigning obedience and Biblical scholasticism to his father, while his nights were spent sneaking to his mother for knowledge in the old ways.<br /> <br /> This state of affairs could never last. Through a serious of events involved in Kill-sin's disobedience and carelessness, his parents ended up dying violent deaths at the hands of the local townspeople. And as he fished his father's blood-splattered Bible from their burning home, Kill-sin knew that everything was his fault. So he ran. He ran as far and as fast as he could, tears running down his face and an intolerable guilt in his heart. Only his mother's black cat - her familiar - followed. Only she could keep pace with the boy.<br /> <br /> As a point of fact, he ran so terribly fast and hard, when he finally collapsed to the ground out of breath, he looked up to find he'd run across the ages. Through a stress-triggered Awakening and a bout of wild magick, Kill-sin had traveled centuries into the future, stopping at the present day.<br /> <br /> His trickster streak is still alive, but in many ways it is only one side of the coin. Though he hides it well, Kill-sin has been deeply scarred by his mistake, and carries the weight of his parent's deaths firmly on his shoulders. While he adores witchery and seeks new knowledge with fervor, he cannot shake or deny the knowledge that it was his impiety that brought ruin. As such, he has adopted just as much Faith work as he has Witchcraft, in an attempt to resolve the deep shame he feels. Where once he rebelled against his father, now he draws the trappings and practices of Puritanism around him like a blanket. It is this profound schism within himself that leaves him an emotional wreck. He calls himself Boy Bright, the Puritan Witch, in an ongoing attempt to resolve the cognitive dissonance that refuses to die quietly.<br /> <br /> It doesn't help that Kill-sin's Avatar appears as his father in his dreams. Even long dead, Obedience preaches hellfire and godly action, this time to a Congregation of one. <br /> <br /> Kill-sin &quot;Boy&quot; Bright is a young man in conflict with himself. He's in conflict with himself, and with the world around him. A world that is so interesting, and yet even he finds appalling in its immorality. <br /> <br /> It's all left him a little unhinged. By day, he is his father's son, channeling his Magick through simple dressing and simple living; that power of Old Time Religion. By night, he is his mother's son, bending the world through hexes and cunning knowledge; the power of the Old Ways. Only at crossroads or crossing times is he truly free, when the place and time matches how he feels inside. Neither Puritan nor Witch. Neither Trickster nor Penitent. Neither Godly nor Wicked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-15-2016, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T05:33:02-07:00","id":988211,"title":"","content":"21) After completing a risky solo mission of executing an identified, seemingly isolated Adsinistratus, an NWO Operative stayed at the apartment of the Nephandus for the textbook 10 minutes - looking for anything of interest or concern. Before those ten minutes, he wasn't one to believe in ghosts - sure, EDEs existed, but they in all likelihood they simply masqueraded as spirits of humans. After those ten minutes of wailing, pleading, objects being thrown around him and ghastly silhouettes flashing, he wasn't so sure. At the 10 minute mark, he was going to leave, but as he were closing the door, he heard sobbing. Thinking - or merely rationalizing going back? - that this merits investigation, he went into the apartment, locked the door, took out a cigarette and managed to crack &quot;Well, I guess we could talk for a few minutes, cause..I wanted to have a smoke anyway, and I can't do this in the corridor, right? So....if anyone is here....&quot;<br /> A pair of ghastly, emaciated boy teenagers appeared and explained that they thank him for the funny effort, but nothing can save them from &quot;<i>the cold</i>&quot;. Looking at the boys...recalling reading up about Mages binding spirits....he realized that the Union lied to him. Thinking how many apartments must be like this, he resolved to stay and help in this one situation.<br /> <br /> With an awkward &quot;Well, I guess you could try lighting this up?&quot; he offered a smoke to the boys, and they jumped at the chance. He went out, tossed the corpse of the Adsinistratus into an alley, and went back with some snacks and beers. Pulling from memory what he read about Reality Deviants, he realized that he needs a 'foci' to make the place 'his own' and keep any other ghostly intruders out..and opted for flowers, with kinds and colors chosen by the ghosts. (Luckily enough, there was a leaflet of a 24h flower delivery service - &quot;<i>Flowers for your Empress</i>&quot; - sticking out of the postbox.) He spent the evening impressing the teenagers with his job and romantic exploits. By the morning the boys were healthier looking and the maddened glee almost disappeared from their eyes. They asked if they can 'slumber' here instead of 'the <i>cellar</i>', and the NWO agreed.<br /> <br /> Shortly afterwards a Mage opened the seemingly locked door and stood at the entrance. Realizing in an instant that his gun appeared to be...lost (Or did he simply leave it somewhere because of the stress?), the NWO walked up to him. The Mage introduced himself as an elder member of the ancient Euthanatos Tradition, and said that he has been watching him and his actions speak of his potential. At the NWO's surprised look, the Mage smiled and said &quot;What, who were you expecting? A Nephandus? Tell you what, I'll ring you later.&quot; before walking away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-16-2016, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T22:50:37-07:00","id":989740,"title":"","content":"22) Average. Of course, humanity is so broad and differentiated, it's difficult to define what an &quot;Average&quot; person is. It's almost oxymoronic, really, to refer to an average human.<br /> <br /> And in truth, the Average Man could hardly be called as such, if he didn't do his damnedest to affect the image. This is a guy whose early life was...different. Or perhaps it was, from his point of view, entirely &quot;normal&quot; (presumably that means it was within the bounds of expected normality within his socio-economic station). The Average Man doesn't talk about his past much, as that would serve to present aspects of him that would make him unique. And he can't have that.<br /> <br /> The Average Man's Magick - a word he never uses - is built on him affecting the guise of a normal, everyday guy. The face in the crowd. A Gutter Mage by practice and Orphan by inclination, the Average Man dresses for his environment, whether that is cubicle farm business casual, a t-shirt and jeans on the streets, or the full punk look down at the metal bar. He's got an entire wardrobe full of costumes for any occasion, and several changes of clothes in his used sedan. His &quot;magical&quot; tools are everyday items as well, and change with the locale. He prefers Entropy and Mind, as it allows him to effect change on a subtle level, and divert attention from himself. But he's branching out into Matter, so that he can change his clothes on the fly, or &quot;happen to find&quot; the right key while thumbing through his heavily laden keychain. Add in his extensive research on popular trends, sports, politics, weather, and other &quot;filler&quot; conversation material, and he's set to fit in wherever he happens to be.<br /> <br /> What does he use his &quot;talents&quot; for? Making his life easier, mostly. He's not unaware of the Ascension War, but he prefers to let the weirdos fight it out amongst themselves. But what he doesn't admit - especially to himself - is that he's way too weird on his own to really be a part of the &quot;normal&quot; world. The Average Man is a constructed facade. Nor does he have strong feelings about anything, or have much interest in the hobbies of normal people, save as they inform his interactions with others. In many ways, he's an outsider, studying popular trends the way a scientist would. A detached understanding born more of its relevance to the common people than out of their intrinsic value.<br /> <br /> Because the Average Man has harbored a secret fear. An anxiety born from his Awakening (which naturally he doesn't share the details of). It's that fear of being different, of not fitting in. He wants to fit back in with humanity more than anything. And if circumstances threaten to alter the normal, unassuming life he desires, that's not okay. He'll defend his normal life, even if he must jump into the magical world he's otherwise avoided until now. Because once the threats are over, he'll be able to wash himself of that nonsense, and pick up where he left off.<br /> <br /> Or, at least that's what he thinks. The Average Man, after all, greatly underestimates the shadow wars being fought for the world's hearts and minds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 10-21-2016, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:39:24-07:00","id":991023,"title":"","content":"23) You're a former member of the NWO Watchers who abandoned the Technocracy after being asked to frame a Mage for a murder he didn't commit. Even though you have been a probationary member of a Chantry for one month, you refuse to abandon your Technocratic roots - still considering Inspired Science to be more reliable and safer, especially for the Masses. While your knowledge of Correspondence: Data gives you common ground with the two Virtual Adepts, your comprehension of Mind and Entropy are entirely through lenses of psychology and sociology. Despite repeated proposals from the Adepts, you'd rather hack into NWO databases for learning materials and raw data needed to enact social Procedures; rather than take lessons in using a laptop to program a traffic jam. Hearing about Paradox backlashes from your new friends has only served to reinforce this attitude. (You still don't know what to think about the notion that Correspondence: Data - and perhaps even your expertise in influencing others - are also varieties of the same True Magick that the Traditions use.)<br /> <br /> Some of the Etherite science piques your interest though, after you realized that some of it could very well be accepted by the Consensus if perfected and made reliable. Plus, it would would definitely be your choice, over pure mysticism or VA reality coding, in regards to increasing your combat capabilities","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-21-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T19:31:45-07:00","id":991661,"title":"","content":"24) A group of vigilantes takes over the street. a group of Virtual Adepts who use their 80's gadgets as focus to bring justice to the static reality. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=egG7fiE89IU\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=egG7fiE89IU</a> Sorry, ever since i saw that music video i used the Killjoys as my local cabal who fights crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T03:54:43-07:00","id":996017,"title":"","content":"25) An Orphan who was previously a manufactured pop star, that was <i>literally manufactured</i>. Created in a FACADE lab, this genetically engineered teen idol was developed as part of a joint NWO/Syndicate experiment. Would it be possible to create a pop idol that was built from the bottom up to appeal to as wide a mass market as possible, and insert them into the music business seamlessly? Because let's be clear, our idol was vat grown, aged up to a marketable level, and thrown out on stage. Their origins were entirely faked; birth records, school records, and even friends and family were falsified. All to test how effectively the Technocracy could integrate a completely manufactured person into not just the world, but the high exposure world of popular culture. And maybe the Union would use them as a mouthpiece for their agenda, or something.<br /> <br /> After a whirlwind five years of tours, recordings, posh Hollywood parties, publicity appearances, paparazzi, and a multi-million dollar merchandising campaign, our idol reached their &quot;twenty first&quot; year, and promptly fell apart. Not literally (thankfully), but emotionally. Turns out force-feeding their brain with all the knowledge they'd need did not actually equip their creation with the ability to deal with the real world. Let alone the drugs, sex, and drama of stardom. The idol had an nervous breakdown on a talk show, and their handlers ushered them away for treatment. After a stint in rehab, they returned to the outside with the adoring public having moved on to some other manufactured pop sensation, the music industry uninterested in a washed up idol with barely any talent (did we mention they could hardly sing, and had no instrumental training?), and the Technocratic Union having long since filed their data and written off the project as a waste of time. Which it was. The Union so didn't care about their creation that, due to a clerical error, they never sent anyone to pick the idol up from rehab.<br /> <br /> One must understand that our idol didn't actually realize up until now they were created in a lab. Their memories were fabricated as well to ensure they never spilled the truth. Not having anyone who really cared about them, they hitch-hiked back &quot;home&quot;. When they found that their supposed childhood home was a model house, purchased in the off chance the idol's handlers needed to stage a &quot;homecoming&quot; or whatever, our idol's programmed memories broke down, and the hidden ones cropped up. Memories of floating in a tank, being strapped to a sleep teaching machine, being tested by FACADE doctors. Such a surge of horrible visions - and the unmistakable truth that their life was a complete lie - caused the distraught idol to Awaken, right there in the model home. The building burned down that day, the idol wandering off in a shell-shocked haze.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, the former idol wanders from town to town, leveraging their social skills, good looks, and modest musical talent to get buy. They are learning how to actually perform music - its history and craft are quite fascinating to them, once the glamour of showbusiness is peeled away. They use Art of Desire, Gutter Magick, and a bit of Crazy Wisdom to get by. They want to better themselves, and become more than just a prop. They also harbor more than a little antipathy towards the Technocratic Union, and the soul less Syndicate and NWO agents who toyed with their life, such that it was. For this reason - and more than a little Hollywood PTSD - they work to avoid being recognized as the washed up has-been they are. If they are going to live their own life, and get back at the Union, what the Technocracy forgot needs to stay forgotten.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T23:29:47-07:00","id":997574,"title":"","content":"26) A student of ancient Middle Eastern studies digs up tablets dating to the age of the fertile crescent city states. He found the tablets in a stretch of desert, following up a rumor on a house buried in the sand, where no signs of civilization (ancient or otherwise) ought to exist. A translation from Babylonian reveals the tablets pertain to an ancient god, whose name and description match no known deity. Etched onto the tablets were poems and charms, as well as instructions for a ritual used to commune with the god.<br /> <br /> No professors or university officials believe in the validity of the tablets, downplaying the possibility that it was a long-lost deity, forgotten by history. Left with a lot of research no one took seriously, the student contemplated the ritual. His dreams were filled by visions of a city state lost to time, and of flowers, the sun, and great beasts. He grew obsessed with this enigmatic figure. Eventually, seeking catharsis for all the efforts invested in the project, ritually purified himself and performed the ritual on the site he found the tablets. At the culmination of the rite, the student was struck with a vision from that long forgotten god.<br /> <br /> The deity was surprised anyone remembered him, and was impressed by the man's admirable efforts at ritual fidelity. He thanked the mortal for giving the time of day to a dead god, and imparted ancient Occult wisdom and visions of the future to him. The man awoke from his vision Enlightened, his senses expanded and his grasp increased. He could act the Seer, and felt the ebb and flow of the forces of sun, wind, and rain. However, he also began to see the world around him for what it really was: a place filled with monsters, and terrible gods, and people like him, but with great power and influence. He realized that he could not walk in this world as a Mage alone. He needed training, resources...and a Patron. A divine Patron.<br /> <br /> Now he is a High Ritual Magician and Priest, the lone worshiper of a long forgotten god. But he aims to change that. At the moment, he also seeks alliance with Mages whose methods and talents mirror his own. The Order of Hermes, Celestial Chorus, and Cult of Ecstasy all have their own merits and flaws, and so his decision is yet to come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:59:40-08:00","id":999932,"title":"","content":"27) You dropped out of studying biophysics after going to a circus show with your girlfriend. After enjoying the show so very much, and seeing how your girlfriend was impressed by the performers, you decided that - whether you will be a clown or an acrobat - circus is where you want to be, right there on stage.<br /> <br /> You Awakened a decade later, while leading a ten-clowns-juggling act that you subtly altered in real-time, to honor your now-wife...and to synchronize the show with a group of spirits flying - or floating - around the circus, who were frantically flying in the air above the audience - fleeing from gathering demonic hawks and harpies. As audience exploded in ovations and the ringmaster cried your name, you let your seven balls drop and roll one by one to form a perfect squared triangle - into which the flying spirits entered, protected from the demons.<br /> That night, you communed with those spirits that dwell in your circus, and you were enlightened about the battles for reality - how magic and charm get stiffed by representatives reason and science, how mages enslave the incarnations of laugh and carefree, and how enigmatic creatures pull strings of the world from the shadows. Although you realized that through your excellence and love of performing you are now able to change reality, you grimly decided that having power is more important - especially for the sake of survival. Tangible, practical power. Around 3 AM, all alone - the spirits went to sleep to recuperate - you desperately lit a series of black candles while performing a knife juggling act for several hours...The flashing blades regularly sliced your hands in neat lines, and the floor under you was slick with blood. Shortly afterwards, the circus took a hellish aspect, and a razor toothed man in a colorful gentleman's suit greeted you. &quot;You tried to call the devil from below, not knowing that <i>you can always count on the devil within, who lives in your shadow and sleeps in all mirrors.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> After tutelage and training with your Avatar, you have established yourself as a cautious and self-sufficient True Mage - you don't need the help of the so-called Traditions, as your performance art is more than enough inspiration to work Magick. (And those Mages you met showed only the barest interest in trying to help spirits.) Through use of mirrors you can gaze in distant places, and no tricks surprise you. Your toothed friend promised that eventually you will be able to act as a whole clown troupe. Juggling and other impressive acts provide a medium through which you can perceive and aid spirits - including calming down those that are hostile and/or afraid. Risky (to say it lightly) acts attract mysterious voices who provide you with maddening half-truths in dreams. Through adopting different stage personalities and masks, and using the power of songs, rhymes and simple gestures, you can read and influence the minds of humans.<br /> <br /> You showed your wife some of what you can do with mirrors; but the spirits of the circus are too shy to meet her, and she dismisses your influence over people as merely &quot;Good hunches and characterization.&quot;...As far as she is concerned, mirrors are apparently somehow magical and &quot;That is all there is to it.&quot;.<br /> Her skepticism worries you. With no aid from other humans - because if not your wife, then what other human could stand by you? - you are afraid you won't be able to protect the spirits you know and yourself from the demons, if they return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-01-2017, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:52:28-08:00","id":1003752,"title":"","content":"28) A Chorister and member of the Alexandrian Society, he subscribes to C.S. Lewis's conception of the Paradisal Man. That being, the state of humanity prior to the Fall - in perfect command of their faculties, and with a fundamental Nature entirely and effortlessly devoted to God. But with the Fall, came the transfiguration of Man's Nature into that of the weak, self-centered being it is today, subordinate to beastial urges and able to turn to God only with great effort. With this change in Nature, a loss of command of one's body.<br /> <br /> This Chorister fancies himself a Christian Alchemist. He proposes that Paradisal Man had in him the capacity to not only perfectly control his own body, but the world around him. That the Paradisal Man acted as a gardener in Eden, changing things as God ordered and as the Paradisal Man happened to need. With the Fall, these functions were closed off...yet, sometimes, God in his infinite wisdom sees fit to loosen these restrictions within certain individuals (&quot;Mages&quot;). As such, this Chorister pursues not merely a physical alchemy - he is a Chemistry professor by day - but also a spiritual alchemy (some propose there is no true Alchemy that is not spiritual at its core). Through contemplation, prayer, and a persistent attempt to lead a moral lifestyle, he hopes to refine his sickly Nature, and strengthen his soul. He seeks to know God, and through this have the Lord's holy flame purify his spirit. Transmuting his post-Fall Nature into something more akin to the Nature of Paradisal Man, and gaining the power (and, more importantly, the wisdom and obedience to the Lord) that exalted predecessor once enjoyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T23:17:56-08:00","id":1006605,"title":"","content":"[Whoops, a second Alchemist in as many posts. Oh well. Also, fans familiar with Promethean: The Created will find something familiar about this. I have been reading the books lately.]<br /> <br /> 29) Her maker never expected her to amount to much. Having mastered the flesh and the mind, it came time to test the matter of the soul, and she was the test subject. Not even a homunculus, as was the creator's forte, but rather a Frankenstein assembled from body parts. It would be less time consuming that way. She was never meant to be his magnum opus. More a proof of concept. Another set of hands to add to the managarie of constructs.<br /> <br /> So it came as some surprise when she not only expressed interest in her creator's work - Alchemy - but that she took to it like a fish to water. The creator was busy, so if one of his experiments wanted to leaf through his library, he didn't care. And if she could do some of the more basic lab tasks (simple work any hedge alchemist could do), all the better. The creator could focus on his work.<br /> <br /> How shocked then were both of them when the little Frankenstein's monster Awakened? The doctor was incensed; he'd by this time created his magnum opus - his most brilliant and aesthetically perfect homunculus - yet his minor project succeeded beyond what his greatest work had yet done. It was senseless. Fed up with it all, the creator cast his creation out the door. It was only later, when his magnum opus stubbornly refused to Awaken, that he wondered if he shouldn't have opened up the corpse-girl's brain to figure out what made her so special. That was a mistake that needed rectifying.<br /> <br /> For her part, the patchwork alchemist was stymied. Her greatest sources of knowledge were cut from her, leaving her only with her own notes and the lab coat on her back. She wandered for a while, baffled by the mortal world around her. She'd been sheltered in her maker's lab, and knew little of how regular humans acted (she had, after all, had very warped examples to learn from). As she searched for new masters to learn from and alchemical texts to study, she took to observing humanity. She didn't know how to be human, and figured that the first step to becoming gold was to become lead. She needed to learn how to be human, before she could surpass humanity.<br /> <br /> Her magick is a mix of classical European alchemy and Yoga. She learned that, by controlling her body, she could manipulate various properties within herself, such as temperature, metabolism, hormone balance, and the flow of bodily humors and excretions. Her body may be cobbled together from several different people, but it was nonetheless a crucible for transmuting elements. If she could control the conditions within it, she could effect greater control over how alchemical reagents she ingested or applied could react. Perhaps if she could bring her body into alignment, she could realign her malformed humanity. If she could perfect her corpus, her soul would follow.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, the world outside is interesting and fun. Now, if only her creator would leave her to her Great Work...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 11-22-2016, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:36:55-08:00","id":1037631,"title":"","content":"30) Uncle Freddy is creepy, old freak of a Marauder who just wants to have children of his very own. Never caring for the sounds of a screaming baby or toddler, he has decided to adopt instead. And by adopt, immediately swoop up the first newly Awakened Mortal he can find and make him/her his apprentice and adopted child. The training will be dangerous, but what the child will learn will make up for it in Uncle Freddy's eyes. All he wants is for new Marauder to bring him in a new &quot;child&quot; in return for his training.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":1834,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","user":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","date":". 01-25-2017, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:42:51-08:00","id":1038253,"title":"","content":"31) It's not that he didn't love his wife. Nor did he want to grow distant from her or their children. But, when he took to studying the occult in his adulthood, he couldn't put the books down. There would be time next week to spend time with the wife and kids...or next month. He was an old man when he was told that his wife had passed away, and his children had all moved on and had children of their own.<br /> <br /> In a cruel irony, the Awakening he'd sought for decades in study, had come in a flash of grief.<br /> <br /> Now he's an old man, with great magical power, and all he can think about is how he squandered his precious time. He doesn't want to make that same mistake again. He still has family, though they aren't happy with his neglect. He wants to win them back; he <i>needs</i> to. He's not as spry as he used to be, and he wasn't all that athletic to begin with. But he's got experience, magick, and a potent Will born of years of quiet, solitary training. This old man - this foolish, foolish old man - is still Magus Rex. He's still a Wizard, dammit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T06:15:48-08:00","id":1042898,"title":"","content":"32) An 12-year-old Son of Ether who has been a mage for six years and now has an open-minded adult apprentice. (That is at least three times his age.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T20:40:04-08:00","id":1047042,"title":"","content":"33) An indie film maker and resident of Vancouver, Canada. While the art and artistry of film-making provides the bulk of this Orphan's tools for magick, his greatest Instrument may very well be the city of Vancouver itself. For decades, the city has played host to film and television shoots, portraying every city imaginable...<a href=\"https://youtu.be/ojm74VGsZBU\" target=\"_blank\">except, rarely, itself</a>. As such, it has Mythic Threads tied up in virtually every urban area in the world. Proficient in Correspondence, this Orphan uses props and costumes that evoke other cities, in order to turn a corner in Vancouver and arrive halfway across the world. And when he wants to return to his city, he clutches a newspaper or tourist trinket from Vancouver and walks back. And because everything from action movies to spy thrillers to comedies have been shot there, he can stand at a location and draw out an effect that matches the film or TV show that &quot;took place&quot; in those spots.<br /> <br /> In a more general manner, he understands that film-making is a kind of magic. But all films are, at their core, <a href=\"https://youtu.be/3O6OTVyybZU\" target=\"_blank\">acts of deception</a> (that the audience may or may not be in on). Therefore, Magic is the act of lying to Witnesses, Reality, and the Mage himself. Many techniques of both cinematography and stage magic filter into his techniques, in an attempt to &quot;Edit&quot; the world the way the character wants it. Not lying for its own sake, however, but to reveal deeper truths. Isn't that what Art is all about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T16:37:09-07:00","id":1062545,"title":"","content":"34) As a mere academic, he found the Western occult tradition an ordered system, to be learned and mastered. When all elements are in their proper place, in the proper proportions, at the proper movement of the stars, Magic happened in a proper way. As he made contact with the Order of Hermes and began to learn its Sorceries, he thought he'd found the height of the Mysteries. If not within his grasp, that with the path to attainment stretched out before him. That eventually, he could know it all.<br /> <br /> Then two things happened. First, he Awakened. And second, he experienced Paradox.<br /> <br /> His mind had already been expanded by his new Awakening when Reality burned him, and sparked yet further expansion. When he was whisked into the Order proper, he asked what Paradox was. And though he was given many theories and guesses, they admitted that no one really knew for sure. Instead of being horrified, as many new Mages are, he was filled with a feeling of the Sublime. An ego-destroying awareness of a new, beautiful Mystery.<br /> <br /> Now a Mage of House Bonisagus, he has dedicated himself to the study of Reality's immune response. As a Paradox Scholar, he does what few Mages dare to do: invite Paradox in, rather than fleeing it. He wants to feel the Burn, bare the Flaws, spar with the Spirits, traverse the Realms, and, if he dares, muddle through the Quiet. Or, at least, he has the courage to stand up to it more than many of his peers.<br /> <br /> He isn't stupid - he wouldn't have entered the Order of Hermes if he was. He wants to live, and finds pain unpleasant. Rather, he won't allow these to deter him from studying Paradox as a phenomenon. Prime is his specialty, as a method of studying the flow of magic. Life is important simply to patch himself up when he gets burned. Moreover, personal experimentation is a slow and dangerous process. So instead of remaining sequestered in his lab, he journeys from Chantry to Chantry, interviewing his fellow Awakened about their experiences with Paradox. He's already published a Treatise on Paradox, and works to fill notebook after notebook about its manifestations. The individual beliefs of the mages, their attitudes towards Paradox, what kind of magick likely precipitated its release, the kinds of spirits they encountered, etc.<br /> <br /> This man will unlock the Mysteries of Paradox, even if it kills him or drives him mad. Maybe if he does, he can help find a way to push against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T23:05:46-07:00","id":1062673,"title":"","content":"35) Antonio San Angel was a normal guy. a christian mexican who prayed all the days and thanked the lord for his blessing.<br /> <br /> Living in ciudad Juarez is always dangerous..things got specially complicated when it was revealed to him the Horrors of the &quot;Sangre Dormida&quot; (Sleeping Blood), the &quot;Aztec&quot; Horrors that controlled mankind!. How could &quot;God&quot; allow such faul creatures to walk in the world of man?!. Some of its servants followed him home and killed his beloved ones. The cult of &quot;El Durmiente&quot; drank, rape and killed his loved ones and the drug lords left him for dead...Until a voice came from the heaven's. It wasnt an Angel, but a &quot;Santo.&quot;<br /> <br /> El Santo, The Silver Masked hero lied his hand upon &quot;Antonio&quot; and baptized him as &quot;El Misterioso&quot; (The Mysteryous one), removing his Face from existance (Paradox Flaw: Always masked and Arcane 4 from his previous life) El Misterioso is now a Luchador. Guided by El Santo, he now protects the innocents, fights the horrors from Hell as he searches for El Durmiente...and the horrors of his nephandi companions, Doctor Satan (barrabi son of aether), Satana de Los Muertos (euthanatoi), La Mariposa Negra (Barrabi)<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, but the idea of a Luchador using magick against a matthusalen is too amusing...besides, lets be honest.. NO ONE! would see a masked luchador trying to pull a Pile Diver on a Vampire while saying &quot;EN EL NOMBRE DE CRISTO, TE JODISTE CABRON!&quot; (in the name of christ! youre fucked asshole!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T01:31:00-07:00","id":1062706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1062673#post1062673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">35) <br /> Sorry, but the idea of a Luchador using magick against a matthusalen is too amusing...besides, lets be honest.. NO ONE! would see a masked luchador trying to pull a Pile Diver on a Vampire while saying &quot;EN EL NOMBRE DE CRISTO, TE JODISTE CABRON!&quot; (in the name of christ! youre fucked asshole!)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The power of Christ compels you...TO GET DUNKED ON!&quot; *Proceeds to pull off some Ultimate Muscle super move, while an angelic chorus and Mexican trumpets blare in the background*<br /> <br /> <br /> On a more serious note, I like the idea of him having high Arcane, but I'd change the mask angle a bit. Make it not a permanent Paradox effect, but a requirement of his Focus. Wearing the mask at all times is part of how (he believes) he gets his divine lucha libre powers. In much the same way that a Shaman might need to continue observing her taboos, or else she loses the favor of her spirit allies (from a Paradigmatic sense, not from the sense of spirits she's talked to), so too does El Misterioso lose his power if his face is ever seen uncovered. It's a requirement from the Santo who empowered him and gave him purpose. If he gets the mask taken off - especially if he is defeated - he no longer believes he can channel righteous power. And because he believes it, so shall it be. Only when he's made proper penance for his dishonor can he start using Magick again.<br /> <br /> This turns the fact that he always wears a mask into an active part of any story he's in, not just an incidental detail. He must remain vigilant, never allowing himself to be seen unmasked. And others - his enemies, the police, potential love interests - could attempt to remove his mask...especially if they realize how important it is to his ability to work holy wrestling moves. That, to me, makes it far more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-16T18:33:32-07:00","id":1063696,"title":"","content":"36) Ever since Norville was little, he always seemed to know how to get along with animals (especially dogs). So much that despite just being an average animal trainer, the Progenitors were very interested in bringing him in. Especially when his Genius awakened and made his pet dog talk (who now serves as a Companion). So now, the optimistic hipster with a love of food serves as a psuedo Dr. Dolittle that handles the animals for his convention's studies and expeditions even if he has a tendency to get scared.<br /> <br /> (Yes, I was inspired by Shaggy Rogers, especially the Scooby Apocalypse version.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T20:09:31-07:00","id":1066684,"title":"","content":"[This one inspired by <a href=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/comic.php?date=20050926#.WNM2dzsrLIU\" target=\"_blank\">these</a> <a href=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/comic.php?date=20050928#.WNM2wTsrLIU\" target=\"_blank\">pages</a> from Girl Genius.]<br /> <br /> 37) A student of the classics of high artifice, this Etherite's passion is automatons. Not the clunky, serviceable droids common among his more practical peers, but elegant clockwork figures that mesh Science with Art.<br /> <br /> Often belittled as a boy for his love of dolls, this son born to minor wealth discovered a life-sized doll at an auction, which sold the possessions of an eccentric recluse, claimed after his untimely demise. The young man bought the doll, along with the scores of documents that otherwise started bid for peanuts. The boy marveled at the doll's craftsmanship, and discovered it was a clockwork robot upon opening it up. Its designs amazed and boggled him, and he couldn't figure out how to work it. Seeking answers, he turned to the eccentric's notes. Among them was a hand-copied codex...the Kitab Al-Alacir.<br /> <br /> Upon finishing the text, the young man's mind was suitably expanded, and pulsed with ideas. He found the doll's schematics, and found he could suddenly comprehend its operation. He started the automaton up, and it worked beautifully.<br /> <br /> He has become a sort of expert on automatons from the Enlightenment period. His workshop is filled with mechanical servitors, and upon joining the Society of Ether, he began to amass secrets of clockwork technology. But his greatest goal harkens back to the product of one Genius of the Artificers, from the days of the Order of Reason. That product: The Muses, nine exquisite dolls, created by the Artificer Van Rijn. Each gifted with an Art form, and capable of inspiring those who witness them. It's even said that all nine Muses together could put on a performance capable of Awakening the audience, though this story is unconfirmed.<br /> <br /> Upon Van Rijn's death, the Muses were split up. Some stolen, some given as gifts, some dismantled by the clumsy hands of lesser Enlightened Scientists. Some, it is said, ran away of their own accord, to escape abuse. They are scattered now, and only a few snatched up. Members of Iteration X have collected a few, as they are wont to do with artifacts of the Order of Reason's heyday. One of the dismantled Muses found its way into the hands of an Etherite in the past, but that Etherite became casualty to the Ascension War, the doll likely taken as plunder.<br /> <br /> Our young dollmaker is fascinated by the stories. He longs for the Muses, and how glorious it would be to bring them together, repaired. His great mission is to collect the Muses, even if he must wrest them from Technocrat clutches. Or if he must scour the earth, to root out those gone to ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:55:28-07:00","id":1067829,"title":"","content":"38) Harmony was a university student, daughter of a wealthy visual designer. She studied philosophy, and engaged in fencing competitions, with aspirations to go pro when she graduated. Her life harbored little stress, so she dabbled in romance once or twice; she slept with one of her classmates, more for the ability to say she'd lost her virginity to her female peers. Still, she liked sex, and wouldn't be opposed to doing it again, though she had trouble opening up to people.<br /> <br /> All these things seemed to matter very little after her Junior year. She was studying Gnostic and Neo-Platonic philosophy when she received the notice of her father's injury. He'd been attacked by someone, and had chemicals splashed into his eyes. Harmony, devastated, abandoned her class schedule to return home. But her studies - of The One, Ideas, Forms, and the Phenomenal World - stayed with her, swirling around her brain throughout the journey.<br /> <br /> Her father would never regain his sight; his career was over. And, what's worse, his attacker was a man of some wealth himself, and some means. Most people knew that when the attacker got off on a technicality, it was probably because he pulled strings within the court system to dodge his guilt. Rumors and scandal say he'd done it before, in the man's business dealings.<br /> <br /> Justice had not been served, and Harmony was apoplectic. That man walked away from his crimes unpunished, while her father was left in a hospital bed, waking up shouting in fear of the darkness that was his life now. The young woman ran from the family home, emotionally overwhelmed. In a fit of hysteria, she Awakened.<br /> <br /> An unpleasant Awakening, Harmony saw the world around her as a complex web of shadows, her newfound sense of Prime, filtered through Platonic thought. Unable to handle the sensations, she shut her eyes. She never wanted to open them again. In time, she would come to understand that moment as her seeing the world for what it was: a shadow play, cast by the light of the One shining down on the purer Ideas and Forms of the Phenomenal World. The base, material world she experienced up until then was an insubstantial pageant play. While she would peek out from her eyelids a few times - she needed to reassure her grieving parents that she hadn't also become physically blinded - she eventually settled on abandoning sight as a rule, donning a blindfold wherever she went. What difference did it make, living in darkness, when the world around her is shadows anyway? The only true light came from The One, and she no longer needed eyes to see that. Her burgeoning grasp of Prime, Forces, and Correspondence circumvented her limitations.<br /> <br /> Time passed, and she became comfortable with her new powers. As soon as she felt herself ready, she snuck into the home of her father's attacker, and delivered swift retribution. In that moment, she took the name Justice.<br /> <br /> Only...it didn't feel the way she thought it would, taking a man's life. There was no satisfaction in making his shed his mortal coil. Only a profound emptiness. She had become Justice, but she felt awful. Bastard though he was, did he deserve death? Or had she allowed hate to blind her? And what would she do then? Justice...Harmony...she went looking for answers, ones she couldn't find on a crusade of death. Eventually, the Celestial Chorus found her.<br /> <br /> Harmony is learning to accept what happened, bit by bit. She's joined one of the Chorus's knightly orders, for her skills in combat are, sadly, in great need these days. On the battlefield, she is called Justice; everywhere else, Harmony. It's a dichotomy reflected everywhere in her life. She's uncertain if she's shut out Darkness in favor of Light, or if she's now living in Darkness, or if she casts Darkness herself. For now, Harmony wields light and shadows in equal measure, while she figures out what she is. Two of her Instruments - Thought Forms and Song - stand in intellectual opposition. With the one, she envisions mechanisms, platonic machines projected into the Phenomenal World, so that she may better move the Material one. With the other, she lets go of the rigid order, and lets herself channel The One's blessings through her song, like the Chorus taught her. Leaving the rational behind, that Sublime feeling flows through her.<br /> <br /> She also vacillates between Gnostic and Platonic, unsure if the world is an irredeemable mess from a malevolent Demiurge, or a flawed but ultimately beautiful creation by a benevolent demiurge, acting according to The One's will. She indulges the former by erecting further barriers between herself and the world, trying to stifle emotions in order to best facilitate her goals. But she only has temporal goals because she thinks there's something in this world that has value.<br /> <br /> And no matter how much she would play the machine, she still <i>feels</i>. Deeply and with longing. She's still a human, with human passions. She's still a woman, with a woman's needs. In the midst of external pressures involved in the Ascension War, and internal struggles with who she is and what she wants to be, Harmony can't help but want to find companionship. She's a warrior, philosopher, transcendentalist, and believer, sorely desiring of a lover.<br /> <br /> Someone to hold her hand when she trembles in the dark, just as her mother did for her father.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 03-25-2017, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T19:17:47-07:00","id":1072307,"title":"","content":"This is an extension of entry number 5. Just like how he's hiding his Hollow One daughter away from the rest of the Technocracy to keep her from being deprogramed, he has two frenemies with secrets of their own.<br /> <br /> 18) It's not often when someone who is technically serving the Weaver would get involved with a servant of Gaia. But when this Void Engineer was attacked by Wyrm creatures and left for dead in the Umbra, it was a wandering Gurhal that saved her and captured her heart. When she discovered she was pregnant, she used her history of loyal service to convince them to let her have a year off to &quot;recover and take care of some family business&quot;. This allowed her a chance to give birth and leave her son with her lover's caern (in return she uses her Technocratic skills to take out the occasional umbral Wyrm minion). She's hoping her son will just be a regular kinfolk when he gets older.<br /> <br /> 19) A Progenitor has discovered the long-long adult daughter (Denise) he never knew he had. Sadly, her mother's sexually abusive husband has left her fragile and the new scumbag boyfriend wasn't a step in the right direction. Denise would pay for everything her boyfriend wanted, have her feelings be ignored and be treated as a trophy and living blow-up doll. So when he callously dumped her by falsely accusing her of cheating on him, she ended her life. The Progenitor believes that if he just came sooner, he could've kept Denise from her downward spiral and he has now been taking out on the boyfriend (the stepdad is dead) by injecting him with a painful disease. Using his mortal identity as a doctor, he has convinced the boyfriend that it's a rare strain of AIDS and will help him find a cure since &quot;Denise would've wanted it that way&quot;. Not wanting to lose the pussy wagon, the boyfriend agrees to keep it a secret and go through with the equally painful treatments.<br /> <br /> Since 5, 18 and 19 all know each other's secrets, they each have a gun pointed at the others' heads if they dare snitch. Eventually, something is gonna blow with at least one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T00:24:08-07:00","id":1076349,"title":"","content":"20) Okay, this is probably cheating in the most blatant way possible. But can we just make <a href=\"https://youtu.be/aAqqpHl436U\" target=\"_blank\">Rex Marksley</a> a Mage character and call it a day? He could be an Electrodyne Engineer, with a penchant for Entropy, Forces, and Spirit. Goes around, stopping evil Umbrood, while befriending good ones (like the Jackalopes). I can imagine both Etherites and Technocrats trading stories of him, a folk hero amongst technomancers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T20:12:24-07:00","id":1079194,"title":"","content":"[Two Spirit focused characters.]<br /> <br /> <br /> 21) A Chaos Magician living in Japan, investigating ghost stories and tales of latter-day yokai. Awakened in high school, when a spooky game with classmates in the dead of night went awry; the ghost in the old school building turned out to be real and <i>angry</i>. The budding magician Awakened in the act of driving the spirit off, saving their friends. Since then, they've studied methods - ancient and modern - to interact with and manipulate the spirit world. Modified Onmyodo, imported Western occultism, and technology like cell phones and computers round out their tools, as well as a growing stock of ghost stories, significant household items, and impressionable young groupies. They're becoming a significant figure in lite occult circles; in turn, this is drawing the attention of Shinto Dreamspeakers, spirit-focused Virtual Adepts, the rare few Japanese Hollow Ones, and, unfortunately, members of the local Technocracy.<br /> <br /> <br /> 22) He was just a young inner city pot dealer, until a mystery man - someone he swore was a powerful Bokor or even Loa - confronted him one night. Colorful ink played over the mystery man's skin, his hide a tableau of living tattoos. Our boy was hit by a handful of the man's dust; everything went black. When he came to, his own skin played host to new tattoo; he was plagued with half-remembered visions of the mystery man touching his chest, and the tattoo flowing from the one body to the other. It's a tattoo of a skull, with a rose like fire in its mouth, and two snakes popping out from its eye sockets. When the young man dreamed, the tattoo spoke to him. Rode him, drove him; gave him no peace, but assaulted him with visions of past and future, and scenes of fire. The tattoo was a Fetish, or perhaps a tie to the young man's Avatar.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, the young man couldn't help but look for answers (if only to quiet his new passenger's inhuman mutterings). In time, he found a mae-de-santos - a mother saint, wise in Les Mysteries - and became a member of the Bata'a. He also sought a new profession - he now works out of a tattoo parlor in a resort town, providing services to locals and tourist alike. Whether those services be a little skin ink, the occasional bag of weed, or something more...supernatural. With great pains, he's taken the needle to his own flesh, etching the vibrant sigils of the Loa on his body. Images representing the pacts and relationships he has with Les Mysteries, so that all who see them will know who his family is. Sometimes, these are used to speak with his spirit allies, or to quickly draw on their strengths. Other times, he uses Life, Spirit, and Matter to summon the Loa into the physical world, allowing them to leap from his body in vibrant forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-21T03:30:54-07:00","id":1081764,"title":"","content":"23) Low on career prospects and middling on patriotism, this future Templar joined military service as the army shipped out to Iraq. She stuck out through multiple tours of duty - by the time her belief in the righteousness of the war began to wear thin, she realized she didn't have much of a life to return to. The war was dreary and without purpose, yet there was a stability to it. She was most comfortable on tour - a sad state of affairs, and she knew it.<br /> <br /> She never had a strong faith before - her family had been more culturally than religiously Christian - and the grinding, endless war didn't help. All this changed when her squad's helicopter ran afoul of a sudden sand storm, forcing a controlled crash landing. Trapped in the desert, blind and with too much radio interference, they were sitting ducks, especially with insurgents prowling the area. With the captain injured in the landing, she had to take charge. They wandered the storm for what seemed like days - the wind and sand refused to die down. Exhausted and overcome by stress, she almost took the angel that appeared in the storm as a hallucination. But it shined bright in the dark - so bright, she didn't need night vision goggles. And it beckoned her forward. In the thick of the desert and half blind, one direction was as good as any. Moreover, it gave her an almost sublime energy, and the motivation to keep marching. Maybe her certainty rubbed off on the squad's morale, or maybe they were desperate enough to try any crazy plan. Even while the de facto captain kept muttering about angels under her breath, when she thought they couldn't hear.<br /> <br /> The angel led them to a rock formation, and a crack in the edifice that could shield them from the storm. But as they ventured deeper and deeper into the rock, they discovered they weren't alone. Nor were those others human. They peeked around a corner in the crags to witness a blasphemous revelry - a half-dozen pale men, cavorting around a diabolical shrine, and sipping ritually of the blood of bound and tortured insurgents. At the height of their machinations, three men were sacrificed, and a terrible welt opened up in the fabric of reality above the altar. A cloven-footed abomination slunk through, spitting fire as it pleased.<br /> <br /> Terrified, the rest of the squad wanted to flee. But she wouldn't go. Oh, she was scared beyond rational thought. Barring rationality, then, she embraced a screaming, awe-inspiring urge: Attack! She Awakened on the spot, and charged, guns blazing. The demon - the accursed blight on God's green earth - had to die, and all its hellish minions needed to go with it. Vaguely was she aware when her squad mates reluctantly joined her; they gunned down all the blood-sucking fiends they could see, while her rifle spat white fire at the demon. When she came to her senses, the pock-marked demon was limping back through a tear in reality, its wounds smoldering and gushing blood that smelled of brimstone.<br /> <br /> The group turned five of its summoners to ash that night, but one escaped. It would only be later that she would learn what it probably was: Baali. She would dedicate herself to wiping that scourge away, and the escapee in particular.<br /> <br /> She returned to the States for the first time in a long while, changed irrevocably by her experiences. Only her comrades who fought beside her understood a fraction of what she went through, and even they found her new perspective confounding. How she didn't need night or thermal vision to see in the dark anymore, or how she seemed distracted by beings that weren't there. She didn't even try explaining to them how she seemed to hear a sublime hum from everything, but especially from numinal forces beyond them. It was only when the Templars appeared that she could finally make sense of it all. That she could finally obtain real purpose again.<br /> <br /> Now a warrior for the Lord, she takes the battle to hell and all of its minions, ephemeral or material. As per the Craft's ways, her Templar allies don't like her to engage in battle herself. On a certain level, she knows that objection comes from a place of sincere care. But she doesn't let it or them stop her. She's a soldier - fighting is the only thing she was ever good at. Now, she had a chance to put those talents to use, for the Lord above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 04-21-2017, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T20:35:06-07:00","id":1082883,"title":"","content":"[This one is based loosely on a superhero idea I had, years and years ago. I have more than a little nostalgic fondness for the guy, so I'm using Mage to finally bring him to life. Though the concept has gone through a number of changes from then to putting this down now, the core concept is consistent.]<br /> <br /> <br /> 24) Growing up, this Japanese man had three passions: drawing, mechanical systems, and masked mystery men as depicted in American comic books (particularly figures like The Spirit and Sandman). His parents pushed him towards becoming an engineer, but he taught himself to draw sequential art. So, to the consternation of his elders, he left engineering school to become a mangaka. His understanding of mechanical systems transferred onto the page, and he became known for his detailed illustrations. Just as he settled into a new studio in a major city (albeit in a lower rent district), he was contacted by one of his friends from university: a student turned anthropologist of Japanese traditional culture. The friend, troubled for reasons he refused to divulge, needed someone to hide an artifact for him. That artifact being an urn, hundreds of years old and sealed tight, yet filled with a sloshing liquid. Our artist, being a helpful and noble sort, agreed, thinking that no one would think to track an anthropologist's possessions to a mangaka living in another prefecture altogether. What's the worst that could happen?<br /> <br /> Find him &quot;they&quot; did, of course. &quot;They&quot;, as it turned out, were members of the Five Elemental Dragons. They demanded the urn back, telling him they'd be willing to do to him what they did to the anthropologist. Perhaps it was shock, or a defiant spark, or simple anger and fear over what happened to his friend, the artist refused to give it up, hugging it close to his body. Someone on their side had an itchy trigger finger, and opened fire, gunning the artist down and shattering the urn. The mangaka hit the floor, splattered in scarlet blood and deep, black ink from the broken container. The Elemental Dragons, seeing their prize destroyed and a seeming corpse, beat a hasty retreat before police were summoned by the gunfire.<br /> <br /> Bleeding out, the artist fell into unconsciousness, waiting for death. But, as could be imagined, the ink was magical, mixing with the blood and staining it obsidian dark. It crept back through the bleed lines and into his wounds, winding through his veins and into his heart and head. In the blackness of near death, the artist was visited by a little girl holding an overlarge calligraphy brush, dressed in a voluminous white kimono, that was splattered with black ink. She introduced herself as a Kami of Ink, a spirit whose home was now destroyed. If the artist would offer his own body as replacement, she would grant him great power.<br /> <br /> As he desired not to die, he agreed. The mangaka took the kami's hand, and Awakened. Forever after, his blood ran black, for he carried ink in his veins.<br /> <br /> The Ink Kami (really his new Avatar, though where one begins and the other ends is difficult to determine) pushed him to study Onmyodo, the high magic of his nation's history. He studied it well, and learned arts of Life, Matter, and Spirit. He learned especially how to bend ink and paper to his will, and to leverage his black blood as a holy medium. But while he was pushed to learn these old ways, he had his own ideas about how to apply them. And what he wanted to use the power for. He was, at his core, a fan of heroes and men of mystery. Drawing upon his understanding of Life and Matter, he could alter his appearance, by making detailed illustrations of new forms to take. And his favored form was that of a new mystery man: a noir detective in a pinstripe suit, a top hat, and a domino mask. He would become the Inku no Otoko; the Man of Ink. A figure that patrolled the night, solving mysteries, fighting crime, and making the innocent world pure by drowning its malcontents in black ink.<br /> <br /> In addition to his traditional tools of Onmyodo, the Inku no Otoko carries brushes, pens, ink wells, and paper with him, along with a notebook. Drawing upon his mechanical knowledge, he creates detailed schematics of devices beyond normal ken, to summon later from ink. This serves to put him on the playing field of the Five Elemental Dragons, who employ technology with impunity. Since he doesn't quite understand yet the difference between Metal Dragons and Elemental Dragons, he fights a covert war against them all, and against elements of organized crime and serial murder. The police are baffled by his presence, considering this &quot;Man of Ink&quot; to be a potentially dangerous vigilante. The Yakuza watch his actions closely, though as yet he's only targeted elements within their organization that are too wild and uncontrolled even for their taste. If he makes more overt moves, they may need to step up their reactions.<br /> <br /> Members of the Akashayana, Shinto Dreamspeakers, certain unaligned Onmyoji, and even some Etherite Adventurers may seek to scout him, once they become aware of his presence. The Five Metal Dragons want him eliminated, though members of the Five Elemental Dragons are open to converting him, if they can. He's annoying, but the Saensaeng in particular see his ties to Japan's ancient past, and think he could be a useful tool in their rivalry with the Zaibatsu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T21:00:11-07:00","id":1082890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1062673#post1062673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">35) Antonio San Angel was a normal guy. a christian mexican who prayed all the days and thanked the lord for his blessing.<br /> <br /> Living in ciudad Juarez is always dangerous..things got specially complicated when it was revealed to him the Horrors of the &quot;Sangre Dormida&quot; (Sleeping Blood), the &quot;Aztec&quot; Horrors that controlled mankind!. How could &quot;God&quot; allow such faul creatures to walk in the world of man?!. Some of its servants followed him home and killed his beloved ones. The cult of &quot;El Durmiente&quot; drank, rape and killed his loved ones and the drug lords left him for dead...Until a voice came from the heaven's. It wasnt an Angel, but a &quot;Santo.&quot;<br /> <br /> El Santo, The Silver Masked hero lied his hand upon &quot;Antonio&quot; and baptized him as &quot;El Misterioso&quot; (The Mysteryous one), removing his Face from existance (Paradox Flaw: Always masked and Arcane 4 from his previous life) El Misterioso is now a Luchador. Guided by El Santo, he now protects the innocents, fights the horrors from Hell as he searches for El Durmiente...and the horrors of his nephandi companions, Doctor Satan (barrabi son of aether), Satana de Los Muertos (euthanatoi), La Mariposa Negra (Barrabi)<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry, but the idea of a Luchador using magick against a matthusalen is too amusing...besides, lets be honest.. NO ONE! would see a masked luchador trying to pull a Pile Diver on a Vampire while saying &quot;EN EL NOMBRE DE CRISTO, TE JODISTE CABRON!&quot; (in the name of christ! youre fucked asshole!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm picturing your holy luchador looking a bit like this guy: <a href=\"http://urdb.kirlad.net/character.php?show=984\" target=\"_blank\">http://urdb.kirlad.net/character.php?show=984</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T00:00:12-07:00","id":1082917,"title":"","content":"25) Business school graduate, borderline genius, socially adept, on the cusp of awakening... Is there a wonder Sindicate noticed him and went to recruit? They just didn't count how much of a hidden depth was under the new recruits paranoia.<br /> Awakening through a psychedelic trip of superscience and files on &quot;Reality Deviants&quot;, he awakened and his Avatar, a Daeva of celestial metal and holy flames, proved more then convincing in it's call to action,<br /> It had taken a week, a week of searching and rifling through files. A week of ass-kissing and sabotage. Then the local construct burned and monsters lured through misinformation, leaked files and his own occult knowledge tore the personnel to shreds. Another week later he turned up at the Chantry continent away, bringing information, his loyalty and a peace offering, bag full of technocrat heads.<br /> Sharp business skills, wide and deep knowledge of occult (particularly on monsters), sharpened paranoia and amorality born of science make him some of the most brutal and efficient members of the Chantry, combining paradigms and practices with the fluidity of the new millennium.<br /> Seeing an opportunity in unexplored niche market he travels the world, tracking down the more approachable creatures of the night and getting them in touch with mages and sorcerers that need their services, for a price of course. So if you need a supernatural companion, bygone familiar or lore on the night-folk, he's your man to go to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-24-2017, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T02:32:47-07:00","id":1084935,"title":"","content":"Looking back through the thread, I realized that we got our numbering mixed up. After #38, we got knocked back to 19, and counted from there. We should be at <b>46</b> so far, if we count the misnumbered entries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:53:20-07:00","id":1091736,"title":"","content":"Alright, I think I got one.<br /> <br /> 46) A certain chantry - a large manor house in the deep south - is run by a kindly older woman (though she genuinely looks good for her age). A mother of four, she opened up her home to her fellow Tradition mages when the last of them moved out. The mothering instinct seems not to have left, however, as she cares for those who frequent the chantry like her own. And she's such a sweet lady, wanting nothing but to make sure everyone - especially the young and inexperienced - is happy, healthy, and prepared for the future. She bakes them cookies. She mends their clothes. She heals their wounds. She teaches them how to fire a gun. She shows them where to strike a man such that it will bring him down in one blow. If their stores of ammunition are low, she'll offer a clip or two from her own stash.<br /> <br /> This woman has a name, but many of the chantry's residents affectionately call her &quot;Mother Death&quot;. A Euthanatoi Master, Mother Death was once a feared individual in the criminal underworld - an assassin spoken of in whispers, for those who spoke of her too loudly had a habit of biting the dust. They fear that figure - the golden-haired woman with glasses that masked her eyes with glare, holding a gun in one hand and a blade in the other - even now. She was said to be a cackling maniac, or else a silent, professional knife in the back. In truth, the rumors and conflicting stories were part of her strategy. The only consistent fact is that she was implacable against a foe deserving of the Good Death; a killer whose blade thirsted for blood.<br /> <br /> Mother Death has, obviously, mellowed out since her retirement. Having a kid - and then having three more - woke up compassion she thought stillborn in her young heart. She is amused by her nickname, and is willing to tell tales of her exploits...if the other person is old enough to hear it. She really does care about her growing family of misfits and weirdos, and wants what's best for them. Sometimes that means not telling a story of her infamous past, if she thinks her audience is too young to be hearing of such things. Sometimes it means teaching them how to fight and kill, for the Ascension War is long, and the Traditions' enemies legion. Mother Death is also unbending and orderly - if she sets a rule for the house, it is written in stone. Woe be unto a mouthy Hollow One or Virtual Adept who gains her ire. Usually, they appear the next day, suddenly VERY polite to Mother Death. They are too frightened or traumatized to do otherwise. It's for their own good, really.<br /> <br /> She may be getting on in years, but she must not be underestimated. Give Mother Death cause to oppose you, and she'll leverage her significant magical and mundane power in kind. She despises child abuse, rape, and human trafficking more than anything; she often sends chantry residents on missions against such criminals, if she doesn't start dropping curses herself. The Children's Crusade is working to get the old girl into their fold, and Mother Death is warm to the idea.<br /> <br /> And if someone threatens a member of her &quot;family&quot;, well...Mother Death will have to march out to fight, herself. Naughty children need to be punished. Mother knows best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T06:12:50-07:00","id":1096691,"title":"","content":"47) Once upon a time, in an age where monsters still stalked the land and the Scourge was but a figure in the distance, an accomplished hunter grew melancholy. He'd stalked every prey worthy of hunting, and brought them down. It came to be that the hunter gained no pleasure from the sport of a mundane hunt. He needed a greater challenge. And so, against the advice of his peers, he set out to hunt the most elusive of quarry: the Unicorn.<br /> <br /> It took years of searching, but he picked up the trail of one of these noble, savage beasts. It took years more in hunting it, for it was swift of sprint, cunning as any man, and deadly in a fight. The hunter acquired more than a few scars in his attempts, and lost all friends, a result of his monomania. But eventually, near the twilight of his years, he bested the beast, driving it over a high cliff and following it down. Driving a spear through its side, the hunter slew the unicorn. Parched and giddy from his hard-won victory, he removed the unicorn's horn as a trophy, then drank its blood.<br /> <br /> The lifeblood of a unicorn, however, is a strong tonic. Its holy properties restored the hunter's youth, but also bleached his curly, graying hair stark white. Moreover, however, it rose to his brain and struck his mind with a horrific clarity. In that moment, he Awakened, realizing how his obsession had not only squandered his life, but deprived the Earth of one of God's pure, majestic living wonders. There was great wailing and gnashing of teeth, as guilt and sorrow filled the hunter's heart. He had killed that which ought to be immortal. Weeping, the hunter buried the unicorn's blood-splattered body deep in the ground, then took his ill-gotten trophy into self-imposed exile. He retired to hermitage far from civilization, taking after the holy mystics of his time. Seeking redemption through contemplation, to quiet his tumultuous heart and make peace with his expanded consciousness.<br /> <br /> Because of the unicorn's blood, the hunter became ageless. He remained in retreat for centuries, dimly aware of the advance of technology, and ambivalent towards the hardening of reality.<br /> <br /> That was, until the cave system that served as his latest retreat became host to criminal enterprise. Their trade: human chattel, specifically children. Fury filled him, at the sight of casual traffic of young lives, and he put his mystic power and his skills as a hunter to good use. He led the poor children from the caves, his cotton robes stained scarlet. But while he was no longer at peace, he felt a refreshment he had not in centuries. For indeed, there was a satisfaction in saving the lives of pure creatures - blessed in the eyes of God - rather than taking them. Shortly after leading the little ones from bondage, he came into contact with Tradition mages, who labored in the name of the Children's Crusade.<br /> <br /> The unaging hunter has adapted a bit to modern day. He wears a leather jacket, and carries a prepaid phone, when his allies need to communicate with him. Horses stand out gravely in this age, so he's taken up a new steed that needs no food, water, or sleep: a motorcycle. But his old skills still serve him well. Skill with spear and bow. Knowledge of tracking and the wilderness. The holy magic honed from years of quiet prayer and contemplation, that allows him to reject earthly forces through concentrated austerities. The unicorn's blood that flows through his veins, and a wand crafted from the unicorn's horn.<br /> <br /> His prey may have changed, but his identity has not. He is a hunter, this time of those who prey upon the weak and innocent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T01:03:35-07:00","id":1101144,"title":"","content":"48) Generally the Devil and his minions are considered Evil among the mage community and only few and rare mages keep quite relations with 1000 Hells. However, sleepers change and adapt faster then the society bound with members centuries or millenia old. Church of the Devil has passed from the hands of Naphandi and into the Masses long ago and its vision of devil changed from the one described in medieval grimuares and the bible, often worshiping the devil as the symbol of rebellion against stricture and dogma, rather then the corruption and destruction.<br /> What will the Celestial Chorus do when the newly awakened satanist is adamant over becoming a member? He is not a naphandy or corrupted, but he does have the True Faith...<br /> <br /> 49) Most sane mages avoid the darker dimensions, be it a monster forest at the edge of underworld, Abyss, one of 1000 Hells or Dante's inferno. You on the other hand thrive there! So what if the energy is poisonous and landscape filled with tortured sinners and monster? Those pussies prefer sitting in Starbucks to a nice barbecue at the edge of the lava lake. And it is profitable too, desperate souls and disgruntles demons pay what little they have to Get Out, even for a little while. Plus, discrepancies in value and lack of competitors make trade very profitable.<br /> Not to mention the sheer loot nobody thinks you'll have guts to raid, steal and abduct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 12-01-2017, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T09:56:55-07:00","id":1101275,"title":"","content":"50) What is being Verbana all about? Most outsider mages would sneer and mention debauched drunken sex, naked dancing and kowtowing to dust laden gods. Sleepers would point to new-age youths, high on and babbling about Gaia. And let's not talk about Techies. \u200b<br /> Even the other Verbanae have become 'civilized', chanting over crystals, swearing by the 'law of threefold return' and preying to Old Gods like they were another form of Jesus.<br /> \u200bYou though... you know do you not? Being Verbanae is understanding LIFE. Life as it is, without the illusion and dreams of the Sleep. Oh, it is not pretty, Life has no morals, Life has no laws, Life doesn't care. It is a world of Gods and Monsters, where the most mad Chaos is but a cradle of the new world and the rock-hard Patterns are but latticework of cobwebs over the bubbling Cauldron of Creation, science is filled with cracks size of sanity and people no less helpless and blind then ever. <br /> <br /> You look onto the world and see it is filled with Darkness. That is all right, it is the way it works, the only way it can. The world abides the same laws of the jungle it always had, most just can't see the strings. <br /> <br /> What will you make of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 12-01-2017, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T10:14:17-07:00","id":1101280,"title":"","content":"51) Chants, spells, sacred designs. All are ancient and mighty tools for magic... for NEERDS! Honestly how could those losers do that silly shit is beyond you. You? Oh you do not need all that nonsense. You are just THAT BADASS! And when you do badass things reality knows it's time to bend over. Just beware, Badassness accepts no substitutes!<br /> <br /> \u200b52) It is the Will of Gods and So Shall It Be Done!!! No, seriously. That's the whole business idea you see! The market was there and you took it. So now when gods/spirits want shit done on earthly plane they call you (or send visions, or something). Repair the temple? Gather the cult? Banish the offending Banes? You are always ready to pull their Ethereal asses out of fire as long as pay is good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T18:31:28-07:00","id":1102167,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://68.media.tumblr.com/32c7980c8c48802f2ec0c64620f6f216/tumblr_orb5imTkvR1rg6figo1_1280.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> 53) The product of a long-term Technocracy project, to train a generation of soldiers using virtual reality. Almost her entire life was spent in simulated reality, until she came of age, topping the rankings in virtual missions. One day, however, she found glitches in the system, and managed to hack into the mainframe controlling it. She discovered that her whole life, and that of her peers, was a fabrication. She Awakened that day from the shock, and spent weeks learning the code that governed, not just her prison digital prison, but the Construct it was built in. Finally, she staged a breakout, shunting her fellow VR babies back into reality. She convinced her brothers and sisters that they'd been abducted, and that they needed to fight their way out. And so they did, the Technocrats put in disarray by Construct-wide system failures, and automated defenses that seemed to turn on their masters. It would only be later, as they combed through bullet-blasted mainframe computers, that they realized what happened. By then, she had led her people out, into the deserts of the middle east (where their Construct had been built, far from prying eyes).<br /> <br /> But she didn't stay with her brothers and sisters long. She was wounded in battle; the physical damage was minimal, but it rocked her to her core. Up until then, she'd never really feared death. Being gunned down in the simulation merely meant failure. Now, death was permanent. For the first time, she felt truly, viscerally afraid. She had to get away. Disappear. Escape the conflicts that threatened to kill her. In her weakness and terror, she abandoned her brothers and sisters, leaving an army behind without commanders, or a war of their own.<br /> <br /> She made her way to Europe, her explorations of the Internet bringing her into contact with those who shared some of her skill set: the Virtual Adepts. Their outlook on Reality also matched her own. Ever since she escaped the simulation, she could never be sure she wasn't in another, larger one. Hell, she couldn't be sure she wasn't in an elaborate version of the same simulation, though this fear at least she tamps down, for her own sanity. She's armed herself with trinary computers and hypertech equipment, along with as many guns and other weapons as she can. Old habits die hard, and she's been forced to learn how to stockpile munitions, rather than taking what the simulation gave her.<br /> <br /> The last thing she wants is to fight, though. She's terrified of her own mortality. However, she's also wracked with guilt. In her adjustment period, she's built safe spaces for herself - places where she can hold out if the Technocracy ever comes. But she also kept track of her fellow VR babies, as best she could. They've become a company of mercenaries and bandits, infamous in the third world countries, not just in the Middle East, but around the globe. A small army of demented former child soldiers, who never learned right from wrong, and who think violence is a game. They've stolen military hardware and cargo planes, to better keep their operation running and moving around.<br /> <br /> She caused this. She unleashed a hoard of killers with skewed priorities on the world. Sooner or later, she's going to have to swallow her fear, and make it right. Before they commit inhuman atrocities. Before they attract the Technocracy's attention, and either get wiped out, or re-absorbed into the Union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T15:15:12-07:00","id":1102622,"title":"","content":"54) Magic is not normal. Not natural. It defies sane, rational modernity, and puts the common person in danger. For this reason, he became a witch-hunter. Their magic was anathema, so he learned the old ways to counter them; his pockets were always filled with iron nails and protective amulets, and he learned dozens of warding signs. All to stymie their occult powers, and put an end to them. For the longest time, he thought that Witches, Wizards, Hoodoo Men, and other assorted magical humans were members of some bizarre, empowered bloodline. He'd hunted more than a few Verbana especially, for whom passing down magical knowledge (and therefore power) through subsequent generations was as natural as breathing. Ergo, it wasn't surprising he would think that.<br /> <br /> And he did, up until he Awakened himself during a pivotal moment during a chase. His quarry, sensing the hunter's sudden inability to handle their knew senses, informed them of the truth. That True Magick had nothing to do with heredity, and everything to do with knowledge and perception. Now the gift was passed on to him, and there was no going back.<br /> <br /> At first the witch-hunter retreated, sitting in denial of his new state. As the reality of the situation sank in - that he could see what man was not meant to see, and reshape it to his whims - he was horrified. He'd become everything he hated. Turned into the very thing he'd hunted, fought, and killed. He couldn't stop fighting the abuses of mage-kind, but it rocked him to his very core. His once iron resolution - his assurance of the morality of his actions - now stands as a poor, unstable firmament.<br /> <br /> He's at a transitional phase of his life. Where once, the witch-hunter studied the craft of his enemies in order to find defenses against them, to look upon the old witchcrafts is to be shown weapons he could employ in full. This disturbs him - how to examination of witch-tools and the learning of witch-words gives him...ideas. At the moment, he employs his magick only to sense the presence of the supernatural, or to guard his mind against their manipulation, or as the basis for Countermagick. Still...the Old Ways tempt him. His crusade is hard, and his life so vulnerable. It will soon come to pass that the witch-hunter will need to call upon greater, less elementary spells. Effects to push away Forces, give him a bit of good luck, read surface thoughts, strike back against the ephemeral, or make his possessions deal and soak aggravated damage. With each reasonable compromise - with each adoption of the abhorrent Art - he becomes inured to the prospect of wielding it. It won't be long, now, before he becomes just another witch.<br /> <br /> So, too, does he find himself compromising with his old enemies. He can no longer dismiss the Mage as something inhuman - he IS one. That means coming to understand them more and more. That means beginning to ask which witch is worthy of death, and which witch is best left alone. He knows, though does not wish to think it, that he will need to interact with his new peers in a fashion that is not antagonism. Will have to talk to them - even make allies. They would know, more than anyone, which of their number is most dangerous. They would also be the ones to go to, to sate his growing curiosity. He possesses books and items plundered from past targets - past victims - that he cannot entirely understand. They would act as invaluable learning aides and bargaining chips, so long as he could consult with experts in the field. <br /> <br /> Of course this presents obvious danger. He came into these items by murder of their kin. He must be cautious, lest his identity as a witch-hunter be revealed. Not all of his materials, either, were intended as tools. His most grisly Instrument is the remains of a witch. He'd started collecting them before his Awakening - less a trophy for his own gratification, and more out of half-baked theory that a witch's remains could hold some of their blood-born power. That they could be incorporated into countermagic somehow. He knows now that magick is a matter of knowledge and perspective, not an inborn trait, but it's a habit he never outgrew. With his burgeoning Paradigm, he's still inclined to assign weight to those remains - that the bones, hair, blood, or eyes of a witch could still, after a fashion, carry a hint of their power. It is, nonetheless, a huge risk, to continue using them. If other witches ever found out about him...<br /> <br /> Lastly, of course, there's the matter of his fellow witch-hunters. He'd never been too religious, so his ties to groups like the Society of Leopold are tenuous. But he's made connections throughout the country, with other hunters. Partnered up with them time and again. They, too, would look at him with horror and disgust, this time for having become everything they fought against. They'd see him as a traitor, or as someone tainted by evil power. How long will it be, before they start to come for him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T23:49:20-07:00","id":1102719,"title":"","content":"55) It is wrong. How can humanity exist without knowing even in what sort of world they live? The physical Earth is but a part of the creation and yet the masses strive blind, without knowing what is their actions' true result. It can not work like this, the ecosystem of the universe will not work so fractured and mutilated, thus the world spirals towards disaster. No matter what sort of misguided self-righteousness moves Technocracy, Lupines and other parties that hide the truth it must be stopped NOW.<br /> Even if you stick out among Dreamspeakers like sore thumb, even if spirits barely heed you and your science PhD rebels against the new sensibilities, you will NOT stop. Man can not manage the world seeing only its infinitesimal shard and thinking himself the king of the universe. When there is an evidence, ironclad evidence, to refuse it would be... unscientific. Even if it will be painful and world-shaking the spirit worlds must be returned within the global paradigm for the world to survive. Those who refuse facts in the name of some mythical 'science' and 'order' are just cultists of the machine, truest enemies of the mankind in the long term.<br /> <br /> 56) They call it Awakening, you would say it's when you learned to dream properly, for this is your awakening, a door opened to the ocean of dreams, of worlds of man and other, greater intelligences. Here you are but a poor artist, there you are a King of your world. With your loyal friend Mr. Tibbers and the guidance of the Moon, mistress of dreams you walk between wonders and nightmares that would drive sny sleeper mad with a barest glimpse and when awake you share them in the works of your Art.<br /> Some strange, bland man tried to abduct you already, but alas you have made friends in the lands beyond sleep and with a frind like you they can step in the waking world, even if just for a while it's enough.<br /> And mom said you'll never amount to anything...<br /> <br /> 57) It had been 10 months, 5 days and 11 hours as you have awakened... and you haven't left your sanctum since. Why would you? The NET connects worlds and places and thus you can also reach them from the comforts of favorite recliner. If you need to kill someone you can do it! In miriade ways. you need to Help someone? All well too possible, need entertainment? Any game, any world on the NET is just a click away. Also, you're a Hikikomori, not like you could just waltz outside...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 12-01-2017, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T20:52:02-07:00","id":1107872,"title":"","content":"58) Born with mental disability, the boy was perceptive enough to realize that his lack of intelligence was burdensome on those around him. His parents suffered long because of him, no matter how much they tried to hide it or tell him he was their &quot;special boy&quot;. From the taunts of his classmates, he came to understand, vaguely, what &quot;special&quot; meant. It frustrated him, to grasp in way he couldn't put into words just how much less he was. Wanting to be less of a burden on his family and special education aids - and to get the damn bullies off his back - he tried to learn. To make himself smarter, as best he could. He would even pray to heaven, asking if he could be blessed to &quot;not be so dumb&quot;. His attempts availed to little, though, and in time he began to question if God was really listening.<br /> <br /> Perhaps He had been, for one day, as the boy sat in his secret place in the woods, staring in anger at his inability to understand the library books he'd obtained, a mysterious figure came upon him. The figure was ensconced in a thick overcoat and hat, despite the summer heat, and had a strange voice that the boy could never describe. They asked the boy what tormented him so, and the boy cried, &quot;No use! No use! I'm a stupid, stupid dummy! It's all I'll ever be!&quot;. Seeing the cause of the boy's distress, the figure removed a strange fruit from the folds of their coat, and handed it to him.<br /> <br /> It was like no fruit the boy had ever seen, and would later learn did not exist in known record. When the boy asked what the fruit was, the figure replied. &quot;Eat it, and your wish will be granted. Eat it, and your brain will shine like a star. You will be...smart. You will know.&quot; Hesitant, the boy's desire won out over his fear, and he bite in. As he greedily consumed the bitter-sweet flesh, his mind caught fire, and he sank to the ground in pain, clutching his head. By the time he rose to his feet, the figure was gone, leaving only the sticky core of the fruit behind. In that moment, the boy's mind raced, filled to bursting with fuller cognitive prowess. Like a ton of bricks, however, he also came to a conclusion about what he'd done. It filled him with guilt.<br /> <br /> From then on, he was a different, opposite child to the one he'd been. Where once he was the imbecile, now he was a boy genius. He devoured books by the stack, focusing on chemistry, biology...and, oddly, theology. For at the moment of Awakening, he came to his own conclusion about what had happened: he'd repeated the error of Adam and Eve. The fruit had been, obviously, from the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil; from which the first man and woman were forbid taking and eating. As they had been simple and innocent, until they ate the fruit and gained knowledge of their wrongdoing, so had the boy consumed the fruit and ceased to be simple. For all the good it did - he was brilliant now, ahead of his class soon by multiple grade levels - it denied him the innocence of youth. He, who would have retained that innocence all his life by virtue of disability, now saw the world - and himself - as the truly were. He had sinned, and now had to live in a sinful world. Perhaps the Lord had blessed him, in fact, by having him born simple.<br /> <br /> While the boy genius - now thirteen, and working his way up to college level work - is privately disturbed by the emotional and spiritual implications of his actions, he soldiers on anyway. There is no un-eating the forbidden fruit, no putting the ills of the world back into Pandora's Box. He could only move forward, and make best use of his intelligence. He is rapidly developing his specialty: Biblical Biology. Studying botany, he seeks to cultivate and study the Forbidden Fruit, using the seeds found in the core of the one he was given. He hopes that with study of plants and animals from a theological perspective, he can grasp the intricacies of God's creation.<br /> <br /> However, he's been backed into a bit of a corner. His stunning shift from dullard to prodigy has not gone unnoticed. Two organizations will shortly attempt to recruit him: the Progenitors, and the Celestial Chorus, with its Alexandrian Society. The latter would be the most excellent fit, marrying science and faith in a way most gratifying to him. But the former would stop at nothing to wipe any thoughts of Eden from the boy's mind, while also plundering the seeds of the Forbidden Fruit for their own research. If the boy becomes aware of the Progenitors, he will realize this part of their plan in short order. Such a blasphemous plot, of course, must not be allowed to continue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:06:24-07:00","id":1108095,"title":"","content":"59) A Widderslainte of the Destruction Essence had a few rough years following her passing into adulthood; as the Nephandi, and other True Mage group, for one reason or another were either unable or unwilling to seek her out and tell her about who she is, and who she could be.<br /> Her seeming possible lifelong unawareness of her Essence sharply stopped being a possibility when, on the verge of nervous breakdown, she came in with a gun onto a group of mafia thugs holding a pair of Sons of the Ether \u2013 a woman and a man \u2013 at gunpoint, shouting that they are to \u201cMake the tech for them!\u201d.<br /> Barely remembering where she got the gun \u2013 maybe off this punk she knifed and killed after he tried to make her pay an additional fee for renting her apartment? - and how she got into the building and into the situation \u2013 most probably because she read the address off the punk's mobile phone, in the most recent SMS he got.. - she shot those threatening others, just like she was threatened. There were four of the thugs, she never held or shot a gun before....but someone in her spoke to her and pointed out - in a string of red-yellow subtle lines the one so called 'mafioso' she should shoot so that others will break, and hesitate, and she'll be able to shot the second, third, fourth of those thugs. After this, she heard a brilliant laughter sounding like &quot;Finally, see you around....take care, it's not <i>that</i> easy.&quot; and fainted, more from surprise and everyday tiredness than of shock.<br /> <br /> The two Etherites took her in, recognizing tell-tale sings of an Awakened Mage once they deduced that this woman, savior of theirs, came into the situation spontaneously. They took her to their Sanctum and activated all possible protections. During the night, after a long conversation considering technology, the Ether and practicalities of avoiding dangers as a Mage, the two Etherites were at pleased at the Widderslainte's eager understanding and gladness to be able to part of something....She was welcomed into their group of two - they have lost contact with their Acolytes and Consors over a half a year ago when the local mafia/gangs started weirdly rapidly and almost knowingly moving against them, their areas and interests and resources. Any of their machines and means that they tried to use to summon help malfunctioned and resulted only in wasted resources and Paradox. But now their fortunes seem to have changed - a Cabal of three Technomagicians was in the making - assuming the new Mage would learn fast, the situation, and them, and their colleagues and friends, could be saved.<br /> But over the next few weeks, they were more and more unsettled her about how, once shown their Etherite technology and given some theories to study over , she was not only very keen in pointing out the destructive potential and possible Vulgar applications of their machines, but also pointedly right despite her inexperience. It wasn't that protective or non-practical technology didn't interest her - it was more that she saw, in the theory and practice of the Etherites' True Magick, chance for greater scientific and practical achievement if it would be admitted that there is potential energy and sheer power to be found and released in everything, in so many ways...<br /> <br /> Sensing a plot against them - was the woman that saved them also cursed in some way, or tracked? - the Etherites took a substantial risk - considering that they were, all in all, under a siege - and sent out a message asking any Tradition Mage or Cabal hearing them for advice and possible help. And, at the Destruction Widderslainte's urging...they promptly cut off contact with them after a all-too-serious-and-scary looking co-location of an only Chorister Cabal told them the woman's Essence and that she is a Widderslainte. The Etherites would have hesitated - considering what they heard about the Nephandi - but the Widderslainte sharply asked the Choristers whether they are aware of the situation of the Etherites here in this city....to which the Chorister Cabal, one by one, started stating how they are only interested in the &quot;destructive one&quot;..at which point the man Etherite got up and pulled the switch in their Correspondence-contact machine that both got them rid of the unwanted Chorister Cabal, and warded/sealed/protected them against any further intrusions from afar, at least for a time.<br /> <br /> A few months have passed and the city's power structure - both Nightfolk and mundane, including corrupt politicians, cops and gangs - is in shambles as the Widderslainte of the Destruction Essence rose to Arete 3 rapidly and started - with Vulgar explosions, Coincidental accidents involving electricity, and spectacularly guided and arranged collapses of sections of buildings - threatening, disabling, ruining and ultimately killing everyone the Etherites could identify and confirm as part of the plot and attacks on them; or anyone that the three Etherites thought should be neutralized or removed - like those running or trying to run rackets. Some of former wrongdoers have been forced by the Cabal, or skillfully manipulated, into paying them a tribute of fairly earned money.<br /> The Widderslainte's family lives far away from the city, and she never had a connection to anyone else in her life - until she met the Etherites. So far there have been only a few tenuous leads as to the possible fate of the lost Acolytes - some point that they are held hostage and forced to design technology and make money for those threatening them..yet at the same time it could be that they have fled to relative, tenuous safety and are holed up somewhere.<br /> So far there has been no Tradition or Technocracy involvement in the situation, since last eight months - at least not in any way the Cabal can discern. The Etherites never in their lives had any contact or dealings with the Technocracy or the Nephandi.<br /> The Widderslainte of the Destruction Essence has brought forward the idea that the Kindred or maybe the Fera - Garou, or what they are called? - are responsible..maybe an alliance moving against the Etherites and/or trying to gain more control over the city. The Cabal is looking to confirm this; at the same time they are continuing their campaign of punishment against any who threaten them, or hurt others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (The Widderslainte of the Destruction Essence can be played as part of the Etherite Cabal, in which case the other players would play the Etherites and possibly other Etherites coming into the situation. The Widderslainte could also be played as a temporary member or ally of another Cabal, played by the players, in which case the two Etherites would be the woman's Mentors and/or Allies.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-26-2017, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T19:19:31-07:00","id":1108226,"title":"","content":"60) Sometime in the waning years of the 20th century, a fifteen year old boy living in suburbia was dealing with bullies...or something. The exact circumstances are hazy to him in retrospect, given the far more unusual event that happened. While hiding in an abandoned forest house, he slipped between the cracks of time and wound up in the Dark Ages for a while. He met a princess, got help from a wizard, braved a dangerous swamp, retrieved a missing item of power, learned to wield a sword, used it to slay a dragon, and saved a kingdom.<br /> <br /> It was a whole thing.<br /> <br /> Once his coming of age story was concluded, the wizard was kind enough to use his magic to send the boy back to his own time. He barely noticed how the wizard seemed gravely disturbed by the boy's tales of the future - a bleak, technological urban paradise for artifice and economics - and returned to his world. He would never forget the adventure, and used his newfound confidence to settle whatever trifling problem he'd left hanging.<br /> <br /> He then proceeded to spend the next fifteen years pretending none of it ever happened.<br /> <br /> What was he supposed to do, really? Magical adventures are great and all, and he was thankful it happened. But obviously, he could never speak of it to anyone, or betray his experiences. They would all have thought he was crazy. Instead, he settled into the mundane life of a modern person living in the developed world. He went to college, dated a few girls his own age, and got a job in the business world. His one concession to that past was to privately maintain his skill with a blade - he always feared he might be snatched back in time, and so kept prepared. Further adventures in time never happened, though, and so turned to the business of business. He would almost have thought the insane hero's journey a figment of his boyhood imagination, had he not retained very tangible souvenirs from it. A couple distinctive scars, a tiny hat snatched from the head of a squat goblinoid creature (with a foul mouth and even fouler breath), and the ring given to him from the young princess. The ring, especially, was important; a royal family heirloom, enchanted to allow the wearer to speak and understand all languages. Indeed, it was precisely for that magic that he was given the ring, as he couldn't understand or be understood by the natives of the time. (In retrospect, he figured out he'd found himself somewhere in medieval France, and took the time to learn French in the intervening years). The ring rarely left his hand, and proved a valuable asset in the world of business.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, he was among a number of individuals - strong-willed, smooth, unflappable, and professional - who were being scouted for recruitment by the Syndicate. That is, until his magical past came back to haunt him. When the man visited a prominent New York hotel, he was surprised to receive a package being held by the hotel staff. They'd been holding the large box for over a decade, but the box itself was obviously of a centuries-old style. Someone had sent it in, and asked that it be held until the man got there to pick it up. In the back of his mind, the man vaguely recalled mentioning New York to the wizard, all those years ago, and name-dropping the hotel, as he'd stayed there as a child. Up in his hotel room, he opened the large chest, finding items inside that were magically proofed against the ravages of time. One was a letter from the wizard, apologizing for not being able to get the package to him in a direct manner, and that he hoped his apprentice's apprentice managed to make the delivery correctly. Another was a tunic the boy had worn in his stay, tatters and tears mended as best could be mustered, and with ruddy stains still visible. Still others were a bound leather tome - a spell book - and a carved wooden wand. Last, but not least, was the boy's sword, wrapped in silk. The sword taken from a fallen knight, and that had been bathed in dragon's blood. The man's eyes filled with tears, as the old memories flooded back in a torrent.<br /> <br /> Then the man actually picked up his sword. Holding it aloft, he was transported mentally back to his youth, feeling all those feelings again. Quite unexpectedly - though perhaps not to that old wizard - the man Awakened on the spot.<br /> <br /> Days later, his bank account was empty, and notice of his immediate quitting was delivered to his boss's office. He dropped off the map, on a quest to find the old wizard's kin: the Order of Hermes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T10:25:18-07:00","id":1112777,"title":"","content":"61) He had been just a normal Virtual Adept - brilliant, cocky, and largely sedentary. He, like many in his Tradition, saw the meat as less worthy of attention than the mind and the tools. That is, until he fell into a dangerous situation, and his computer equipment was rendered inoperable. With his normal methods cut off, he could only run; he just barely made it out alive, and his out-of-shape body didn't help. Exhausted and terrified, he became disgusted with his own weakness. He realized that day that a strong mind and powerful tools could only be leaned on so far. Until such time as Reality 2.0 truly came to be, he couldn't escape meatspace forever, and meatspace was a harsh place. But it was, nonetheless, a system, with its own rules. And systems can be hacked. They can be improved. And the rules that govern meat reward effort.<br /> <br /> Taking to the gym, he pushed his soft body to the limit. Gritting his teeth through the pain, he worked to overcome that weakness that nearly got him killed. At his computer, he learned to type one-handed - with either hand - in order to pump iron with the other. And on that computer, he created models for his physical body, and ran simulations. Scanned his fleshy data, in order to create targeted methods of self-improvement. He studied martial artists, capturing their moves on video and analyzing them, in order to understand the mechanics behind physical action...so that he might maximize its effects. He even goes without calculators wherever he can - his mind, too, must be strengthened - so he crunches numbers in his head while he does actual crunches.<br /> <br /> The power of technology is great, but he won't use it as a crutch. Since Reality 2.0 seems little closer now than it was twenty years ago - a true New Reality, unmoored from the physical - he will have to make his body as perfect a vessel for his mind. His efforts are paying off - he is quite a physical specimen, and not just by VA standards - but he will not be satisfied yet. To stop improving is to stagnate, like a computer system that receives no upgrades. And if he can drag other members of his Tradition out of their dark dens and get them moving, all the better. Even if they moan and complain now, the pain they experience now will make them stronger. In the end, they'll thank him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:21:21-07:00","id":1115376,"title":"","content":"Once upon a time, a semi-prosperous merchant was assailed in the night by prophetic dreams. Nightmares seemingly depicting the end of the world. Night after night he was afflicted by these visions, so he feared sleep. Daylight offered little comfort, for he saw signs and portents in daily life that reinforced his predictions. He truly believed that the world was only a few years away from ending.<br /> <br /> This man had three sons, and he feared for their future. Deciding that there was little that coin could do to protect them, he steered them towards other fields, that could perhaps afford them better chances of survival. A shrewd man, he chose to hedge his bets, and sent his three sons on three different paths.<br /> <br /> <br /> 62) To his eldest son, the merchant used what wealth he could to send him to university, that he may triumph over apocalypse with reason and natural philosophy.<br /> <br /> 63) To his middle son, whom the merchant treasured, the merchant sent to join the priesthood. If God brought down Judgement Day, it was only sensible to curry favor in the Kingdom of Heaven by being one of the Lord's faithful.<br /> <br /> 64) To his youngest and least cared for son, the merchant went the opposite track: this boy would learn sorcery, and so was apprenticed to a local witch. The merchant - an arguably pragmatic man and one with fewer scruples than most - figured that if God was not in the mood to play favorites, the devil might be more amenable. That the witch the boy was apprenticed to was not an Infernalist, but rather a mere Verbana practicing the Old Ways, did not occur to the man. Not that he cared overmuch either way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps by the same metaphysical quirk of fate that gave their father oracular dreams, all three sons eventually Awakened. The eldest son was recruited to the Artificers, the middle son fell into the Choir Celeste, and the youngest son became a Verbana witch himself. Long after their father died, the three remained at each others' throats, both over differences in Paradigm, and because of their differing opinions on said father. The eldest son was proud of the patriarch, yet also secretly bitter at having been sent to school rather than following the more lucrative path of the merchant. The second son is fiercely loyal to the father, though also laments that the man may have cast himself into hell by double-dealing God and Satan. And the youngest son despises their father - the man was willing to send him to the devil (even if it didn't work out that way) - yet still harbors a desire for the man's approval, even after his death.<br /> <br /> And, of course, there's that whole potential apocalypse thing. No matter what they feel about each other, they may be forced to collaborate, if they are to avert disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T23:59:01-07:00","id":1115412,"title":"","content":"That mofo had Dark Trinity on advanced level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T05:28:45-07:00","id":1115485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1115412#post1115412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That mofo had Dark Trinity on advanced level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naw, just a guy with &quot;flexible&quot; morals, a case of general sleep deprivation running at all times, a willingness to play multiple angles, a deep fear of the end of the world, and a genuine (if misguided) desire to prepare his sons for the worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T20:37:02-07:00","id":1116227,"title":"","content":"65) Once upon a time in Arabia, a ghula - a blood-drinking cannibal fairy or djinn of the desert - did as her kind often did, and got a man of wealth and vitality to marry her. She drank her husband's blood as he slept, in order to fuel the creation of their children. But, so this story goes, the man's great piety before Allah rubbed off on the desert fae, and in time she renounced her evil ways. No more did she feast upon the flesh of the dead, and she raised their children to revere Allah and the Prophet.<br /> <br /> This member of the Ahl-I-Batin is a descendant of that union, and he carries the fae blood in his veins.<br /> <br /> He is a man of dark complexion and brilliant green eyes. His fingers end in retractable claws, which he employs sparingly, and his teeth are sharper than most. For this reason, he rarely smiles - a habit born of years of needing to hide his family's peculiar heritage. When Paradox afflicts him, it often manifests as deep wrinkles on his face, and the inside of his mouth grows as green as his eyes. A throwback to his distant progenitor.<br /> <br /> He is most at home in arid climates, but he will travel anywhere in search of fairy lore. Especially related to the djinn. A High Ritualist and man of deep Faith, he also draws upon a wealth of Crazy Wisdom, culled from his encounters with and research on the Kindly Ones. Changelings and those also of fae blood are of particular interest to him. As a scholar of theology as well as folklore, his current goal is to explore a theory that would reconcile the existence of fairies and other creatures within Allah's design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T23:52:32-07:00","id":1123782,"title":"","content":"66) A Dreamspeaker Spirit Smith, whose area of focus is construction and renovation of homes. A house flipper by trade, he buys run-down homes and moves into them, working to repair them. But in the act of flipping the house, he also slowly works to awaken the building's spirit. He also works to attract positive spirits, ward the building against harmful ones, and help any lingering ghosts resolve their unfinished business and move on. He rounds out his magickal improvements to the property by scrubbing away distasteful Resonance, strengthening parts of the structure against damage and the ravages of time, and layering enchantments into the walls that push occupants towards caring for the building's upkeep. When he believes his work is complete, he hands the house over to a Consor - a real estate agent, who works to make sure the property finds its way into the hands of people who will treat it well.<br /> <br /> Some activists within the Tradition criticize the 'speaker's approach as playing into the hands of the Syndicate, and even contributing to gentrification by raising property values. The spirit smith understands these objections, but continues nonetheless. To him, he isn't helping the Syndicate, but exploiting their economic systems for a greater purpose: spreading the influence of the spiritual world in the beating heart of &quot;respectable&quot; society. If the new landowners believe their house is alive, they may feel inclined to respect and care for it. (It helps that our house flipper makes the spiritually improved house known to local mages, so they can focus their efforts on the new occupants and the expansion of their beliefs.).<br /> <br /> As for gentrification, the spirit smith likes to seek out the aid of local youths, when it comes to fixing the houses. He can only do so much himself, and more hands makes the work go faster. This also serves two more purposes. First, it allows the smith to steer the youths of low income areas towards practical skills, and away from gangs and criminal activity. Teach them useful trades, so they can better their own lives. Secondly, the on-the-job training isn't just limited to home repair. The most promising workers get turned onto the wonders of magick, and the reverence for spirits. He never has enough time to truly initiate these youths into magic, Awakened or otherwise. But he can get them interested, so their training can be continued by local Dreamspeakers (or members of other magical groups, like the Verbana or Bata'a, if Dreamspeakers are scarce or uninterested). Through this, he can do his part in spreading the shamanistic Paradigm, and undermine the Technocracy's ideological stranglehold.<br /> <br /> Finally, he serves the Traditions more directly by occasionally providing them with properties suited for turning into Chantries, in those places where they don't otherwise exist. Spiritually awakened and warded buildings make for better places for mages to meet. The spirit smith hopes to one day learn the secrets of creating Nodes, that he might make this process all the more effective.<br /> <br /> If he's guilty of one major failing, it's his rage when his projects get mistreated. He travels extensively between home flips, looking for new properties. When he's in town, he'll check in on previous flips. When he can't, he'll contact local Dreamspeakers (or anyone with Spirit 2) to check in on it. If the house spirit says that its owners are bad owners - neglecting basic maintenance or disrespecting the home - the smith gets angry. Depending on how terrible the new owners are, he may decide that a lessons need to be taught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T23:04:59-07:00","id":1125492,"title":"","content":"67) A police profiler, his job was to understand perpetrators - how they thought - in order to better catch them. He attracted the Technocracy's attention after helping stop a notorious, occult-themed serial killer. They saw in him an acute mind, and an ability to grasp complex subjects quickly, given enough research material. So they set him to work learning about the mentality and methodology of Reality Deviants, so as to combat their &quot;menace&quot;. He was afforded access to materials otherwise forbidden to regular Union personnel: the body of occult lore captured from the Technocracy's superstitionist enemies.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the Union would keep an eye on him, to ensure his burgeoning expertise in mystic theory didn't blossom into Unmutual practice. Unfortunately for them, they should have been watching more closely.<br /> <br /> The profiler - soon a knowledgeable NWO Extraordinary Citizen - found his specialty in short order: Hermetic theory. Soon, however, the Union couldn't shield him from the obvious: they weren't fighting crackpots and charlatans, but people with real, honest-to-goodness POWER. Power they got, seemingly, from adherence to superstition. He accepted that these Reality Deviants were employing some sort of Science they did not understand...but it made his interest in the theory of magic turn into a minor obsession. He could better do his job, he'd say to his superiors, if he knew better what the mystics were doing with their deviant Science. That meant more books, better reports, access to ritual tools. His immediate superior almost denied the request on the spot and sent him to Room 101...but the profiler's sincerity came out in the superior's Mind senses. And they DID have a group of Hermetics giving them trouble. They needed their expert, and they needed his understanding unclouded.<br /> <br /> And they just happened to have captured one. The profiler could certainly learn much from a live subject to interrogate. The Union would simply need to watch their man more closely.<br /> <br /> The profiler got to peruse the &quot;wizard's&quot; captured effects. His books of numerology, his seal pendents, his magic wand. When the profiler got his meeting, the first thing he asked was &quot;why is your wand like this, and not like something else?&quot; In his mind, he was just trying to take shortcuts on research - he wouldn't need to comb through texts in eight different languages and three ciphers, if the expert would divulge his secrets. The wizard, surprised and intrigued, used the profiler's curiosity against the Union. After extensive discussions, over multiple sessions, the Hermetic finally planted a dangerous seed in the Technocrat's head: Hermetic Magick was a cerebral, academic art, but the codes and protocols and theories were all in service of something less explicable. The symbology existed to convey deeper truths, that could not be summed up in words. Hermeticism was at once systematic and sublime. The only way to truly understand a wizard's mentality...is to perform the rituals yourself.<br /> <br /> This germ of an idea incubated in the profiler's mind, to the point where he couldn't sleep. For three nights, he lay awake, tortured by the niggling doubt. A part of his mind rebelled - strongly - against pursuing Deviant ideas into practice. Another part, however, couldn't stop thinking about it. So, seizing his notes and the ritual tools he had available, he created a makeshift ritual space in his living room. He worked until dawn, performing the rite. Just to see what all the fuss was about.<br /> <br /> To his surprise, the magick worked. Worked better than he could have imagined. As a blackout was thrust upon the neighborhood, he felt an ecstatic revelation. And something in his head cracked. He had forced himself into an Awakening, and broke his Conditioning in the process. Through his new awareness, he realized that the Union would almost certainly punish him for what he did. Take away every ounce of knowledge of Hermetic High Ritual Magick, and make him a perfectly obedient, orthodox Technocrat.<br /> <br /> So he did what any loyal Union member would do in that situation: he grabbed as much wizard crap as he could, returned to the Construct, and personally broke the wizard out of his cell. It was a harrowing hour, sneaking through the building and knocking out what guards he needed to. If the Union had been as attentive as they should have been - if they hadn't also been distracted by events elsewhere - his rash actions would have failed. Instead, he got to the wizard, returned his tools, and asked only one thing in return: for the Hermetic to take the profiler with him.<br /> <br /> He could not go back. He didn't want to be a boring bureaucrat. He couldn't let all his progress along the Path be wasted.<br /> <br /> Now he's a member of the Order of Hermes, House Fortunae. He couldn't be happier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T22:04:16-07:00","id":1139102,"title":"","content":"68) A short woman - max four feet tall - with dyed pink hair and pigtails. She's a mechanic, with a sardonic sense of humor and a complex about her height. Hates being called &quot;little lady&quot;, or variants thereof. Hates being mistaken for a child even more. To compensate for her smallness, she loves to built powered armor and mini mecha in her garage. She may be small, but by her mind she will wreck havoc. The rest of her Enlightened Science is brought about with small gadgets and gizmos, her tool belt, and an understanding of physics and engineering.<br /> <br /> Joins either the Society of Ether or Iteration X. The latter gives her a greater deal of resources and funding to work with, while the former gives her greater latitude to bring her creations out into the field without worrying about protecting the Consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T07:39:55-07:00","id":1139185,"title":"","content":"69) Jenkins has manifested magical powers, but his avatar/genius isn't awakened; how is this possible? He doesn't realize that he has fetus in fetu and it's his hidden twin that has the awakened avatar/genius; not him. It just happens that it needs Jenkins to do any magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T10:27:39-07:00","id":1139729,"title":"","content":"70) As a newly Awakened Tormented Widderslainte, you feel you should consider yourself lucky. You Awakened when defending yourself \u2013 with your then meager skills learned at a self-defense course \u2013 from a group of thugs who first tried to rob you, and then to murder you. Your Avatar's laughter served as a lightning fast inspiration, and working together with it you managed to pinpoint the weaknesses of the thugs, and you scorched their flesh when you filled a broken-off bottle with your sadism and strength. You killed all five of them; however, the day after the next day you noticed you were already shadowed, and in a week a trio of no-nonsense looking government agents went into your apartment at night, and were explaining to you in vague terms how in your case there is no need for evidence, as your very existence might as well be an admission of guilt. Fortunately, you were saved by an Ahriman of Nephandi bursting in, their Spells disarming the Technocrats before the Nephandi killed them with guns and knives. The attractive and beautiful leading Adsinistrati was very glad to find out that you're a Tormented Widderslainte, and even more glad to confirm that you are Awakened - she and her Ahriman were running on a tight time schedule and with limited materiel, and thus she wasn't sure if she would have had the time and the means to torture you into Awakening.<br /> <br /> The Ahriman barely got a few sentences of explaining to you that they are part of the Nephandi and that you're a Widderslainte, when they sensed a follow-up team of Technocrats, with support, arriving. The Nephandi immolated the bodies of the killed ones in your room, and cast a Spell on your apartment so that it wouldn't be visible to searches of the Technocracy \u2013 at least for the next few days. The Adsinistrati hugged you, told you not to tell anyone anything about the Nephandi or that you're a Widderslainte, and went out with her fellow Nephandi to avoid the Technocrats. You haven't seen them since. The Technocracy \u2013 at least as far as you are aware of \u2013 has not bothered you.<br /> <br /> You lived a nervous few days of not knowing how to proceed \u2013 experimenting with patterns and shades gleaned on the city streets, and mystic outlooks suggested by what was written on internet websites. On the fifth day of you trying to get a handle of your new existence \u2013 and you worrying about the safety of the Nephandi that saved you \u2013 you were approached in a coffee shop by a group of four True Mages, in the early twenties; they bought you dinner and you began conversing. More out of a sense of wanderlust and a desire to meet someone new than because of anything else, you spent a night with them. They pegged you as being of the Dynamic Essence, and you went along with it. They suspected nothing about you and the Nephandi, and didn't even mention the word. One of the True Mages calls herself a Hermetic, another \u2013 a Verbena, and two of them refer to themselves as Hollow Ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-13-2017, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T20:02:56-07:00","id":1144265,"title":"","content":"71) Coming from a working class background, this boorish man used a combination of aggressive financial action, a spontaneous Awakening, and a heaping dose of dumb luck to turn a succession of business startups into unexpected successes. Which he sold, acquiring large quantities of money very quickly. As such, it was inevitable he would be scooped up by the Syndicate...despite him being a poor fit, even in a Convention that keeps fingers in organized crime.<br /> <br /> Like a crude combination of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ULeDlxa3gyc\" target=\"_blank\">Loadsofmoney</a>, the speakers from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zQrdKtPJxI0\" target=\"_blank\">Whales</a>, and Kill La Kill's singular <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fgXCeeRZKd4\" target=\"_blank\">Dosh King</a>, he is a man with a rich man's bank account, a poor man's understanding of how to use it, and a Trump's undeserved cockiness and unchecked belligerence. He eschews the tailored suits of his Syndicate peers, instead usually running around in jeans, t-shirts, and a sports jacket (bearing the logo of the team he owns). Intimidation and throwing around cash is his primary means of getting things done, along with a set of beleaguered assistants who &quot;are good at getting things done&quot; in his mind (and so, because of his assurance in his money's ability to secure competence, they inevitably are). Even his habit of &quot;dressing down&quot; can have an effect on those around him, albeit not in the way that clothes usually aid Syndicate reps. If nothing else works, he can always rely on swinging his weight around, both with his assets, his fists, and his ever-ready wad of cash (this time, as a literally weapon to slap people up with or to establish his credentials as someone with the power of money...loads of money).<br /> <br /> Naturally, other members of the Convention loathe him. To other members of the Syndicate, he is an embarrassment, a personal insult, a crime against decency, a betrayal of the Convention's values, and a clear liability. Most Syndicate members distance themselves from the idiot in their midst as much as possible, quietly hoping his many character defects will eventually bring him low. Some even keep tabs on him, in order to both make sure that his inevitable reckoning doesn't damage the rest of the Syndicate, and more covertly to make sure he can't use his own Adjustments to dodge &quot;justice&quot;. If that means letting him squander his money until nothing remains, that cash will doubtless be put to better use by the free market (while his business assets are quietly bought up by respectable Syndicate ops, of course). If that means letting the superstitionists destroy him, that makes him a useful shield for &quot;proper&quot; Syndicate business. If that means preventing him from escaping police investigations or civil suits, it can only serve to enhance the public's confidence in the power of the system to correct economic abuses (because Dosh knows the Syndicate needs a win in that arena). If that means letting him die in a knife fight because his incautious Adjustments forced violent market correction (or his belligerence and lack of caution got him a knife in the back when he wasn't looking), well...<br /> <br /> ...let's be honest, most Syndicate members wouldn't cry at his obituary.<br /> <br /> Of course, this particular man is nothing if not ballsy and stubborn. It may not be as simple as letting him bring doom upon himself. He's not a brilliant man, by any means, but he CAN be cunning at times. And ferocious like a wild animal if backed into a corner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-17T18:32:30-07:00","id":1150514,"title":"","content":"72) An Iteration X AI programmer and cyberneticist, who installs intelligent systems to run Technocracy compounds. With the lifting of the ban on Iterators learning Dimensional Science, he has become fascinated with matters in the other dimension (the so-called &quot;Umbra&quot; in superstitionist jargon). Upon discovering that objects and even buildings become reflected on the other side - and that the two intertwine - he began seeing possibilities. If old buildings have a &quot;spiritual&quot; presence, that means that long-standing structures cease to be mere material constructs, and instead become living organisms (albeit organisms that obey different physical laws). Their awareness is, by default, inert, but can be awakened with the proper (or improper, in the case of the superstitionist) application of Dimensional Science.<br /> <br /> Testing a hypothesis, the Iterator has been working to install a sophisticated AI into the structure of an old, established Construct. But not just in the physical walls of the building, but into the pseudo-physical walls in the other dimension, and linking the two. Creating a potent, logical mind, loyal to the Technocratic Union, and marrying it to the other-dimensional presence that has already married itself to the building. Awakening the building, so to speak, but in such a way as to not just give it a &quot;soul&quot;, but a mind. One more to the Union's purposes. At the same time, creating a bastion of logic in the other dimension, from which further Dimensional Science missions and experiments can be launched.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the programmer and cybernetics expert is trying to give the building's spirit a cybernetic implant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T19:05:05-08:00","id":1166877,"title":"","content":"73) &quot;The Fiddler In The Mask&quot;. &quot;The Jester Prince&quot;. &quot;The Man Of A Thousand Masks&quot;. In truth, though, it's not known if this mage is a man, a woman, both, or neither. Their skin never shows, their outline androgynous. Their manner and bearing mutable as the tide, changing with each exchange of their ubiquitous masks. They often come in a variety of costumes - to match what they wear on their face - but their seeming default is a form-fitting set of dancer's pants, pointed shoes, a long-sleeved turtleneck, fashionable gloves, and material covering their head, neck, and face. One wonders if they aren't wearing a full body suit, like something from a stage dancer. They are also verifiably an accomplished vocal performer, capable (through skill, technology, or magic) to change their voice at the drop of a hat, mimicking a large range of sounds and accents. Judging their true identity through voice is, therefore, impossible; it changes as easily as their change their face.<br /> <br /> For indeed, the Fiddler is a shapeshifter, using their masks to assume different forms where needed. Perhaps the person one met at an art gallery or the supermarket was them in disguise. Masks also allow them to call upon a variety of different powers, including fading from notice, moving at a rapid pace, taking to the air, etc. Their abilities are enhanced by the use of stage magic techniques, their vocal ability, graceful movements, and their supernatural use of the violin. A bard, actor, and magician, the Fiddler considers the whole world a stage play, and thus Affectation is as good as Reality. Too bad about the lost script, though...<br /> <br /> Some mages chalk the Masked Fiddler as being mad. A Marauder, and nothing more. More open-minded Awakened, however, understand that this mutability of identity and garish performance are just as valid a means of obtaining power. And that any mage will seem mad, when examined from the outside. Indeed, the Fiddler is not a Marauder or weighed down with Quiet. Though they may be subject to madness, their is yet method in it. The Fiddler understands that people - the Actors in this farcical stage play - wear masks in their day to day lives. Personas they project to the wider world. How the Fiddler differs is that they do not take to this idea of a &quot;True Self&quot; that somehow lies &quot;Behind The Mask&quot;. There is no such thing. Or, at least, whatever lies behind the masks humans wear is so ineffable as to be impossible to truly grasp, save by the transcendently enlightened (those who have achieved Ascension, who have discovered how to leave the stage and became part of the audience). For all practical concerns, there IS no True Self; it's Masks all the way down. Even when a person is alone, they still project a Persona to themselves, for they do not know how NOT to play a role.<br /> <br /> For this reason, the Fiddler sees every Persona - every pattern of behavior and combination of word and deed - as being equally &quot;True&quot; to the person's being. Every Mask one wears, every role they play, every performance they give is AS accurate a measure of who they are. In the Fiddler's case, they simply choose to assume as many roles as needed to make sure the Play runs smoothly and has a good conclusion. They seek to work within society to better it; and they see the best way of bettering the lot of Actors (that is, the whole of mankind) is to make them realize the fact they have forgotten. That they are, in fact, Actors playing roles. That it's all a production, and can be altered to make the story better.<br /> <br /> Sometimes that means working to expose the nature of mutable reality to people, like other Awakened do. Sometimes, that means exposing more &quot;mundane&quot; facts, such as a politicians indiscretions or crimes, or removing their veil of anonymity that allows random acts of cruelty on the Internet to go unpunished or unjudged. It means exposing the Masks we wear as masks, and making everyone aware of which Actors are pulling multiple, unsavory roles in the drama of human experience.<br /> <br /> Because even if all the world's a stage and all of life a fiction, that doesn't mean it isn't important. These performances - and the playing of them - matter a great deal to the Actors who pour their hearts and souls into them. Even if it is a story, that story matters. Should it not, then, be made a story WORTH telling and a performance WORTH putting on? While the Play should never be boring - which is why the Fiddler chooses such a colorful path - it can still also be fulfilling and fun for everyone involved. Even if that means certain Actors should be called out on their abuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 12-11-2017, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T22:50:41-08:00","id":1167228,"title":"","content":"74) When you're a young, hopeful girl in Japan, and you suddenly Awaken, what do you do? Become a Magical Girl, of course!<br /> <br /> That's what she did for three years, between ages 13 and 16. Prancing around with molded plastic scepters and other accessories, transforming her street clothes into frilly dresses, righting minor wrongs in the name of hope, justice, and friendship. Maybe it was the right climate that many of her Effects got past Paradox (and what Paradox she experienced wasn't as harsh, or she powered through its manifestations). Maybe there really WAS something to the idea of having supportive Friends (What's this background called? Cult?). Maybe she just got really lucky for a long time.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, her good fortune eventually ran out, and she got in way over her head. Facing a foe that took their conflict much more seriously than she was used to, the Magical Girl limped away with a debilitating injury and crushed spirits. She nearly died, and her enemy went on unopposed. &quot;Disheartened&quot; did not do the feelings she felt justice. She lost hope in her crusade. And while she was laid up in hospital, recovering, she slowly lost contact with her friends. For a Magical Girl like her, Hope and Friendship weren't just hollow platitudes. They were the source of her power. The ties she forged with others gave her strength, while powerful emotions allowed her to push beyond the limits of what was possible. Cut off from her established relationships, and in poor spirits, she lost access to her magic. Even when she recovered, little of her magical might followed.<br /> <br /> So she spent the remainder of her adolescence a normal girl. She went to high school and then to university, majoring in 3D modeling. She got a job, and her own apartment. She even had a couple of romantic relationships that ended up going nowhere. When she used magick at all, it was in simple, utilitarian ways. Her passion simply wasn't in it anymore, and because of her Focus, since hobbled her. Mage outsiders - if they could see her or know her plight - would have wondered if she was on the verge of sliding back into a sleep-walking state.<br /> <br /> Mages, however, do not enjoy boredom for long. They are cursed to live interesting lives. Fate conspired to put the former Magical Girl into a position to witness a violent crime in action. With help from the &quot;proper authorities&quot; a long way away, and lives on the line, she couldn't stop herself from intervening. For whatever reason, fortunately, she never got OUT of the habit of keeping a small plastic wand with a big yellow star on the end inside her purse. By the end of the day, when the adrenaline died down, her heart and mind were racing still. She didn't sleep much that night. Couldn't possibly. Not when that crime she stopped was, obviously, a small part in something much larger. Something the police seemed strangely unwilling to investigate.<br /> <br /> She had to get back in the game. Not just out of need to correct a problem she saw before her, but for very personal reasons. She couldn't sit back passively when she had the power to make real changes in the world, for the better. Nor could she simply fade back into her old routine. The Magical Girl had to come out of retirement...no matter how embarrassing the idea sounded, after years of being a Serious Adult. There was nothing for it, of course. Waving around plastic weapons in colorful clothing, while openly proclaiming her intent to punish evil in the name of justice, were simply the only ways she knew HOW to do magick. She would need to work on that, and work UP to going full Magical Girl again.<br /> <br /> A thrift store sewing machine and a 3D printer would help her get back in the game. Now if only she could find some new friends. Or, maybe, see what her old friends were doing...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T23:52:31-08:00","id":1168135,"title":"","content":"75) A Virtual Adept cyborg, with a specialization in Mind and Spirit. One day, she did battle with a malignant spirit program - a Digital Devil - wreaking havoc on the Digital Web. After a long, tense encounter, she thought she'd managed to delete the ephemeral virus...until she realized the devil had taken refuge in her brain implant.<br /> <br /> With quick thinking and a frantic bit of hacking (and a bit of luck, in that she already had systems in place for isolating malware that got in her BMI), she turned the digital devil's hiding place into a snare. A score of her implant's internal memory was ceded - ground lost in the bit war - but she managed to contain the beast inside. Mostly.<br /> <br /> She's the Virtual Adept who walks around with an imprisoned cyber demon in her head. And it is not happy. While it can't take control of her, it can sometimes marshal enough processing power to haunt her with visual and auditory hallucinations. She dare not try to go in and erase the beast, lest the attempt break its shell and let it run rampant. Nor can she readily replace the hardware in her skull, and couldn't trust that the switch over wouldn't somehow give the beast a chance to escape to the net or another machine. So at the moment, she's stuck with the malign passenger; she is its host, and its jailer. Lucky her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T00:09:33-08:00","id":1168136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1168135#post1168135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">75) A Virtual Adept cyborg, with a specialization in Mind and Spirit. One day, she did battle with a malignant spirit program - a Digital Devil - wreaking havoc on the Digital Web. After a long, tense encounter, she thought she'd managed to delete the ephemeral virus...until she realized the devil had taken refuge in her brain implant.<br /> <br /> With quick thinking and a frantic bit of hacking (and a bit of luck, in that she already had systems in place for isolating malware that got in her BMI), she turned the digital devil's hiding place into a snare. A score of her implant's internal memory was ceded - ground lost in the bit war - but she managed to contain the beast inside. Mostly.<br /> <br /> She's the Virtual Adept who walks around with an imprisoned cyber demon in her head. And it is not happy. While it can't take control of her, it can sometimes marshal enough processing power to haunt her with visual and auditory hallucinations. She dare not try to go in and erase the beast, lest the attempt break its shell and let it run rampant. Nor can she readily replace the hardware in her skull, and couldn't trust that the switch over wouldn't somehow give the beast a chance to escape to the net or another machine. So at the moment, she's stuck with the malign passenger; she is its host, and its jailer. Lucky her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, I can think of a way to progress this character. If she ever does get rid of that digital devil, she would suddenly find a large amount of core memory vacant. And while a smart (or lazy) Virtual Adept might just use that space for &quot;normal&quot; processing, a more adventurous soul might opt to keep using it as-is.<br /> <br /> With just a few modifications, that empty space could provide room for a visiting Digital Web denizen. Hopefully, one that is less evil than the previous occupant, and who will be allowed inside for more limited periods. In essence, our Virtual Adept adds Mediumship to her list of Practices, as she allows spirits of code to ride her like a Loa rides a practitioner of Vodoun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T14:55:45-08:00","id":1169483,"title":"","content":"76) Sometimes, a mage can end up lost in a Paradox Realm for quite some time. And given the convoluted flow of time in the Umbra, what seems like a short stay in a cubicle farm populated by monster robot office workers, may end up being a couple decades back on the material plane.<br /> <br /> This Virtual Adept is one of the old school, having cut his teeth on tech that made William Gibson seem futuristic (because, at the time, his projections were). Dial up connections, dot matrix printers, and command line interfaces, baby. After his &quot;brief&quot; stint in the aforementioned monster robot cubicle farm, he crawled out of his computer monitor to find a world that passed him by.<br /> <br /> Now he's an anachronism. Where once he stood at the cutting edge, now he struggles to wrap his mind around Gigabytes, Terabytes, and even Petabytes. Even the basic sleeper computer user is hacking circles around him. Especially since modern internet connections seem terrifying fast by comparison to what he's used to. All his Virtual Adept buddies have become old men, and seem too busy to help their old friend adjust to the tech explosion they all got used to over time. With the net running so fast - and with information iterating and transforming at such a stultifying rate - they barely keep up with their own problems.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, these young punks scoff at him, telling him to get with the times, grandpa. Sure, he knows more about how computers actually WORK than these &quot;millennials&quot; - none of them seem to know how to solder a chip or debug in machine language - but they understand all the intricacies of modern operating systems, social media, and 21st century security software. And while he gets floored by the pace of improving tech, the children of this meme-future seem to just take the rapid shifting of standards in stride.<br /> <br /> If he's going to have any chance of being relevant in this time period, he'll have to catch up. To be honest, the new vistas of knowledge make him feel young again (not that he's chronologically that old). Brings him back to the excitement of learning new things, and discovering new possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T14:30:35-08:00","id":1170014,"title":"","content":"&quot;Alive, aware, in awe<br /> Before the grandeur of it all<br /> Our floating pale blue ark<br /> Of endless forms most beautiful&quot;<br /> <br /> -Nightwish, &quot;Endless Forms Most Beautiful&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> 77) At some point, they became so enamored by Awakening, and the ability to change their shape on a whim, they forgot who they were, where they came from, or what they originally looked like.<br /> <br /> A shapeshifter of the Verbana, this ecstatic wanderer marvels at the beauty of the world, in all its varieties. However, they wander, not simply for the joy of seeing, but to find themself. They used to have an original form, they think. It's a form they cannot, now, remember. Their past is...fuzzy, and seems unreal. They think they may have fallen into a deep Quiet for a long time, when the constant shifting of form brought down the wrath of Paradox. So when they finally collected themselves, they didn't remember what they were doing, or what they even were originally. The Verbana took them in and taught them to control the changes, but none could look back far enough to see the character's original form or origin. That period in their life is clouded, as if someone - possibly the character themself - erected wards against Time senses.<br /> <br /> While the shapeshifter loves the multiplicity of forms all around them - they love people, and want to reflect their beauty - the lack of an &quot;original&quot; identity unsettles them. Even one who abandoned their origins and remade themselves still reckon their lives and identity by the past. Such people can still know who they are, by comparing themselves to who they aren't anymore. This character - this wild, ecstatic witch - has no such comparisons. Rather than feel liberated, the shapshifter feels lost. They are adrift, unmoored. Unable to truly feel comfortable, if there is no point of reference. While the road towards Ascension might involve becoming comfortable with true freedom of appearance, they cannot help but long to know. Cannot help but think that they'll never truly progress if this mystery remains.<br /> <br /> Moreover, there's this nagging uncertainty in their heart. How can the shapeshifter truly connect with the beautiful mass of humanity, if they cannot conclusively prove they were ever human to begin with? Are they, in fact, simply a monster, pretending to be human? It is a frightful and distressing idea, and must be disproven.<br /> <br /> So this wandering form-changer travels around, retracing their steps. Trying to remember their course, so they may find their origin. Find someone - anyone - who can recognize them, in spirit if not in form. It is a journey not just through space, but in forms and Time. They are sure that when they've found who they were, they can better plot a course towards Ascension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T01:55:25-08:00","id":1194187,"title":"","content":"78) An Iteration X cyborg, working as a field agent in a Technocrat Amalgam in a big city. Hardly the soulless drone of stereotype, though, he is sardonic, sarcastic, and eccentric. He constantly listens to eclectic music, slings around banter, and experiments with a constantly rotating selection of fashion accessories (ranging from the merely unusual to the stunningly bizarre). To the often grim and serious Technocratic Union, it would seem like a problem waiting to be hammered down. Goodness knows other operatives and scientists in his Construct find him irritating and distracting.<br /> <br /> But he remains unmolested, and for good reason. While he's likely to respond to orders with sarcasm and facetious wit, he still follows those orders. This steelskin's loyalty is not in question. When it comes down to brass tacks, he gets the job done, and cuts the nonsense when work needs doing. Nor does he take his...quirks to obnoxious lengths, or at least tries not to.<br /> <br /> This cyborg fully and completely believes in the mission of the Technocratic Union. Protection of the masses, better living through science, and all that. What he blanches at is the idea of being rendered down to a gray cog in an impossibly huge machine. When large chunks of his own body have been cut away and replaced with technology, remaining unmistakably human is vital to him. He must prove that he hasn't just been hollowed out and reduced to a mere wind-up toy, alongside other hollow toys and in service to equally hollow superiors. The Technocracy exists for the sake of humanity - for human beings - not just as a mechanism bent only towards its own continued operation.<br /> <br /> As such, wherever he can, the cyborg works to inject levity back into the Technocratic machine. Not to be disruptive, but to remind Technocrats (and himself) what their priorities are. And to serve the role of the jester, by using humor - even sardonic humor - to help his associates and superiors see when they are being foolish.<br /> <br /> Moreover, it helps, when dealing with eccentric superstitionists, to have someone around who can get into the mindset of &quot;madmen and weirdos&quot;. You'd be surprised how often Technocrats have trouble guessing the moves of a Tradition mage, because the Technocrat is too &quot;rational&quot; to grasp their actions, and too monofocused to accept the traditionalist's reasoning as anything but abject insanity. This cyborg, meanwhile, can walk into a night club and seem right at home, and decipher enigmas too alien to the scientific mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-12T04:01:01-07:00","id":1194483,"title":"","content":"79) A Technocrat who is a member of the New World Order Convention needs no more than a pen, pencil, A4 papers, and current and past data that the NWO has gathered through it's Technocratic methods ; and of course her Genius. This is what has been told many times to this young member of the New World Order's Watchers - and she believed it fully, and excelled at it. She focused on the Sphere of Mind and on making predictions, to the point that currently she barely uses her Correspondence: Data capabilities. She reasons that it is better to confirm facts through deductions and reliable and trusted agents performing observation acitivities, than to rely on Correspondence: Data observation capabilities - she thinks and feels that this leads to excellence.<br /> <br /> Her forte soon became advising Extraordinary Citizens and agents of the Technocracy, making them more assured, better prepared, and more couragous. Currently she seeks to become more than the vaunted and desired New World Order advisor and analyst - she seeks to use and develop the technology related parts Technocratic Science, and has asked to be taught the Technocratic Temporal Science, which is normally only used - as far as she is aware of - by members of the Iteration-X and the Void Engineers. After this, her next goal is to develop scientific and technological understanding of Primal Field Theory, so that she is capable of building and using her own equipment in this regard.<br /> <br /> She is of the opinion that a member of the New World Order should not exclusively focus on psychological and statistical analysis, and instead should strive to be an Enlightened Scientist who builds and improves her or his own machines and devices - even if in the end it the focus on technology of such an NWO Technocrat is less than that of the Technocrat Mages in the Iteration-X, the Progenitors or the Void Engineers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [ This character is a Technocrat Mage of the New World Order, her Arete is 3, and her Spheres are Mind 3, Time 2 ( currently in regards to making predictions and deductions of persons' behaviour, but she is seeking to have the capability of using and building technology that will enable her divinations about events of the future and of the past ), and Correspondence: Data 2 . ( It is possible that she can learn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/986539-the-masses-as-an-amplifier?p=986909#post986909\">NWO's Correspondence: Agents, which is an analysis and personal interaction based variant of Correspondence which can be used to accomplish objectives and carry out Procedures through the use of agents, rather than through the use of technology</a>. ) ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-15-2018, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T14:14:16-07:00","id":1199828,"title":"","content":"80) An Orphan (though who sometimes works with the Hollow Ones, so who knows if true independence will stick) and working writer/poet. His first brush with magic occurred when he came into ownership of an old typewriter. Discovering the typewriter had some ability to guide the future through what was written with it, he attempted to make his dreams of literary success and fortune happen. Long story short, he failed utterly, the typewriter being destroyed in the process. In his most dire time of need, however, he realized that he'd exceeded the actual potency of the machine long before - a product of his sleepwalking Avatar - and that he didn't require it. With his own literary skill, he wrote himself out of his problem, achieving a full Awakening in the process.<br /> <br /> In a different town, he's got greater control of his power, but is wary about advancing his situation too quickly. He won't repeat the same mistakes as last time.<br /> <br /> Moreover, he's been exploring his Focus, and the power of language and stories. He has come to believe that all of this world is a grand narrative, told by...someone or something. &quot;God&quot;, probably, or at least another writer. Whatever the case, to him, that means that the stories people tell and life in general are, theoretically, no different. Fact influencing Fiction, but with the possibility of Fiction bleeding into Fact. His magick, therefore, works to exploit this two-way street. Working up and down levels of a grand, complex, and recursive universal narrative.<br /> <br /> Making Fiction reflect Fact, he allows his mind to wander at the keyboard or the pen, so that information from elsewhere, else-when, or in the heads of others flow into his writing. Working the other way, creating a narrative can affect his own level of reality, by penning scenarios he hopes will come to pass. In another way, though, he can grant himself more options by creating works that, through their narratives, energize certain objects or actions with magical power of his choosing; many of his more physical or expedient tools were empowered by the stories he wrote of them. He could use a pen to draw a door into a wall, because he wrote of such things in his growing library of works.<br /> <br /> Then, of course, there's the works themselves. Since every Fiction is equally as valid as the &quot;Fact&quot; he lives in, their rules and effects can be drawn directly out of the stories themselves, if the books or manuscripts or the like are brandished. A finely written, printed/penned, and bound book is worth even more, as a work with more effort put into it means more to him (and potentially to others). Of course, no one said the stories had to be his own, either. With a world flush with Fiction by a million authors, a potentially limitless store of power can be channeled from mankind's collective storytelling efforts.<br /> <br /> At the moment, though, the writer is preoccupied with another possibility: if Fiction is as valid as Fact, does that mean characters in one level can communicate with or slide into another level? It's a troubling thought, for one who makes a meager living by putting characters through hell. At the same time, though, it's a compelling idea, and one he cannot help but desire to pursue. This will probably get him into trouble again. It wouldn't be an interesting story, though, if he sat around and avoided all risk. And who knows what sorts of higher level beings he's meant to entertain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T20:52:23-07:00","id":1200698,"title":"","content":"81) A Wu Lung demonologist of the Dragon School, working in the Office of Records. A bureaucrat, this straight-laced man of China combats agents of the Yama Kings who act above their station, and the humans (and occasionally supernaturals) who pay homage to them. And he combats them in a less intuitive manner: through his mastery of mortal bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> When he isn't summoning demons and compelling them to give information (as is the right of the Dragon Wizard to do, being agents of the Celestial Bureaucracy), he stalks the halls of academia and law enforcement, rooting out infernal activity on a systemic level. Corruption, on a large enough scale, leaves patterns. From the halls of academia, he roots out infernalist knowledge hidden in the libraries of China. Over the years, infernalists and even Nephandi have planted copies of ancient infernal tomes in such places, leaving them to be found and acted upon by young, impressionable, and ambitious scholars.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the dragon wizard uses his contacts in China's law enforcement agencies to track crimes of an...occult nature. Grisly murders and blasphemous graffiti, and everything in between. Wherever admiration of the Yama Kings spills out into the underworld, he follows. An authoritarian state, China tends to keep such scandalous events quiet, in order to maintain the country's image both in the world at large and among its populace. As such, this demonologist must dive deep into official records, not normally open to the public. To his dismay, he often arrives upon such data after cases have already grown cold; this can be a blessing, though, as cold case files aren't watched as diligently. He tracks incidents, using his knowledge of municipal sectors and dragon lines to narrow his search for infernal crimes.<br /> <br /> When he believes he has useful information, he forwards this to compatriots in the Tiger School and the Office of War, so they may use more decisive action to take down targets. When an infernalist is killed or driven off, these agents return with any books and artifacts captured from the lair. Objects of power are contained, and where necessary destroyed or handed off to Wu Lung more capable of destroying them. The texts are collated, organized, deciphered, and dealt with. Those books with data useful for tracking other infernal activity at used as such, while those texts with dangerous information are burned.<br /> <br /> All of these activities are, naturally, documented in meticulous reports, delivered to the wizard's Sifu. With the temptations of the diabolical ever present, it takes a disciplined mind and loyal spirit to handle such things. Few could be trusted to pull it off, but this demonologist remains steadfast.<br /> <br /> After all, he has to restore his father's honor, after his own consorting with devils destroyed him. That shame and grief motivate the demonologist more than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T04:49:46-07:00","id":1202194,"title":"","content":"82) He was being prepared for greatness. He was being groomed for initiation into the greatest Hermetic society in the world...<br /> <br /> ...Clan Tremere.<br /> <br /> That is, until he Awakened.<br /> <br /> The Tremere vampire who would have been his sire could not bring himself to follow through with his original plans. After all, how could the old lick possibly unlive with himself, knowing he had cultivated a true spark of divinity in his mortal pupil, only to then snuff it out forever? It would be a crime graver than all the deaths on the vampires hands (which, naturally, were many). So officially, the young man's would-be sire reported to those higher in the Pyramid that his would-be childe was unsuitable, and had already had his memory wiped of all knowledge of House and Clan Tremere.<br /> <br /> A lie, of course. While the Kindred would have to cultivate a new embrace candidate, he didn't want to lose his old pupil. A truly Awakened mortal was arguably as potent as any vampiric blood magician, and could do many things a vampire could not. If nothing else, perhaps this &quot;True Mage&quot; could be an asset.<br /> <br /> So when the mortal was shipped off to a neighboring town, he carried copies of texts on blood magic made by his undead mentor. Duties within the city (and the need to train a new embrace subject) prevented the Tremere's active involvement in the mage's education. So, to supplement what infrequent lessons and instruction the Tremere could give, his Awakened protege would need to further his own studies. The mortal wasn't worried enough to let it stop him. After all, what kind of Hermetic would he be if he couldn't take knowledge into his own hands?<br /> <br /> There is just a tiny snag: he was learning primarily from books written for undead sorcerers. It's no surprise, then, that the mortal developed the Blood Magick flaw. His Hermetic methods are on the bloody side, and one learned in Hermetic theory could potentially spot many stylistic and methodological differences between his magic and that of the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> Oh right, there is that matter of House Tremere's former Order, isn't there? The Blood Mage was shipped off to a town with as little Order of Hermes presence as possible. At least, as much as the Tremere mentor knew at the time. The mortal didn't have trouble finding Tradition mages, and it didn't take much longer than that for him to get invited to the local chantry. Without a permanent OoH presence, everyone just assumed he was part of the Order. This is not reassuring to the Blood Mage, as he can never be sure a &quot;real&quot; Hermetic won't show up and reveal him as a fake. Or at the very least, start asking uncomfortable questions about who taught him such bloody, inefficient praxis.<br /> <br /> Not, however, that he's entirely against meeting the Order of Hermes. He knows that he'll never be accepted into House and Clan Tremere, nor does the idea of standing amid monsters appeal to him overmuch. Even his mentor doesn't have as much time for him as he'd like. That is, when the old vampire isn't asking the mortal to report information on other mages, in order that the vampire might one night leverage them for some political advantage in the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, however, the Tremere's general inattention and focus on his &quot;real&quot; student (the one slated for Embrace) couldn't work in the Blood Mage's favor. If the Blood Mage plays his cards right, he might be able to get in with the Order of Hermes - he has more than a few Tremere texts to leverage - and even learn how to break his dependence on blood. All he has to do is bide his time, and play the long game. It's a tightrope walk, balancing his obligations to his mentor, his need for secrecy, and his desire for advancement and the ridding of his limitations. But he wouldn't be a Hermetic if he balked at a challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T02:37:19-07:00","id":1203768,"title":"","content":"83) A Virtual Adept working as an investigative journalist, going where others cannot in search of the truth. Indeed, he only found the Tradition as part of a story he was attempting to research. Unlike many Traditionalists, while he has his own Paradigm (mainly Technology Has All The Answers), he isn't overly interested in proselytizing. Rather, he's interested in Truth. Finding the raw data - the fundamental Facts - and sharing it with the world. That way, people can make their own judgments. What he despises is secrecy, cover ups, and lies. If the facts don't immediately lead to danger, they are best exposed. The Truth wants to be free.<br /> <br /> Naturally, his willingness to spread hidden information - even about the supernatural - has earned him the ire of the Technocracy. At the moment, though, they don't move against him directly. The Adept has made enemies, but also has many friends. Some of them powerful friends. Some of them friends who have terabytes of data they've been instructed to release, if he ever disappeared. While none of these things would stop the Technocratic Union if they REALLY wanted him gone, they make doing so more trouble than it's worth. As such, the Union prefers to work indirectly to sully his reputation and sabotage his career, in an effort to undermine his voice. Limit his exposure, by limiting his credibility and capacity to get access to information.<br /> <br /> Since the information he spreads can suggest a supernatural nature, credibility was never going to be his strong suit anyway. So these are limitations he's accepted. Getting the facts to the right people is what's important. If even small numbers of folks know the truth, it's better than everyone living in ignorance. Better luck is had when investigating more mundane matters, as &quot;believable&quot; activities like crime or corruption are more readily accepted. If, in laying out all the fact, a person might be able to connect dots to less &quot;normal&quot; elements of a story (like the involvement of Night Folk), then so be it.<br /> <br /> As a technomancer, he focuses on computers and gadgets. Especially tools for gathering information, and for allowing him to cover ground and circumvent obstacles. Climbing gear and grappling hooks, telescopic microphones and drone cameras. Software for deciphering encrypted data, reconstructing shredded documents, plotting guard patrol routes, and picking out falsehoods in speech patterns. How to dress and act to talk past guards, or to fade into a crowd unnoticed. He uses skill, technology, and more than a little luck (even that weighed into his favor) in his perpetual search for the Truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T22:16:02-07:00","id":1209120,"title":"","content":"84) An Etherite researcher who specializes in Spirit (or Dimensional Science) and Life. Previously a marine biologist, he is fascinated by the strange forms of spiritual life that thrive in the Umbra, especially in the Umbral counterparts to underwater areas.<br /> <br /> For this reason, he can often be found wearing a bulky pressure suit, that is both waterproof and armored, and adorned with instruments and mechanisms of his own Inspired design. He'll even wear the suit and breath through it, even when a particular foray into the Umbra wouldn't require it. Not because he believes there's no breathable atmosphere - he IS an Etherite, after all - but because he just happens to also be a hypochondriac. Has been since childhood, when he spent much of his formative years sick in bed. He's neat and prone to avoid infections at the best of times, and that's on the material side of the Gauntlet. He has a particular anxiety about contracting Umbral diseases (which, naturally, informs his Paradox backlashes), and takes steps to insulate himself from the greater Umbra as a result.<br /> <br /> Of course, he's also concerned about potentially contaminating the Umbra with his own material world diseases. The man is a conservationist as well as an explorer. He finds that the best choice is to observe the Umbral ecology, but to keep it and himself at arm's length. It's ultimately better for everyone, and he has gotten into many arguments with other Spirit focused mages - especially the Dreamspeakers - over their blithe disregard for unprotected mingling with the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Still, he's intelligent and diligent, and knows the Umbral seas better than anyone this side of the Kopa Loei. Currently, he's working on building an Umbra-worthy submarine, so he can take a crew deeper into the depths, where the Gauntlet is thinner and more coincidentally crossed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T21:56:01-07:00","id":1211690,"title":"","content":"85) She's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7dQ1xiy-4hY\" target=\"_blank\">just another LA devotee</a>. Who just happens to be a mage.<br /> <br /> A pop singer who came to California to seek fame, her modest success came alongside an Awakening onstage. She happened to get lost in her song at the right moment, when the band was pumping out the right notes, the stage lights danced at the right angle, and the crowd's infectious enthusiasm hit the right fever pitch. She felt like her voice was channeling something deep and powerful.<br /> <br /> After a member of the Cult of Ecstasy showed her the ropes and told her who to seek help from (and who to avoid), she dove headfirst into the path of ecstasy. Her magick allowed her to edge out the competition enough to keep in steady employment, while allowing her to get invited to all the right parties. She cut her teeth on the magick of sex, drugs, and rock n' roll. She could read fortunes in the patterns of neon light, though she also got more than most people out of astrology.<br /> <br /> Indeed, she always loved the stars. They are sublime in their way, fixed and yet cyclical in a manner that the chaotic party lifestyle isn't. Every so often, she'll drive out into the desert at night, and lay down on the sand, looking up at the stars.<br /> <br /> In truth, while this Ecstatic is good at carousing, and can hold her liquor, all is not sunny in California. She's been doing this for ten years now, and doesn't feel like she's going anywhere. This despite being on the move constantly. She more or less has no permanent residence anymore, but crashes at the homes of anyone she can finagle into letting her. She'll often wake up at odd hours of the day or night, not knowing where she is or how she got there, or who it is she's staying with.<br /> <br /> It's a rough life, and it's not getting any better. She feels like she's spinning her wheels, and on sober days she becomes intimately aware of just how much she's squandering her potential. She's a mage, for ****'s sake. In a sea of chaos, it's HER that's standing still. Gives her the itch to break out, try new things, and maybe do something productive with her gifts for once.<br /> <br /> Also...when was the last time she actually did a performance? Or had a job? When did she last talk to her agent? Has she actually been coasting and/or mooching this whole time? Where did her cell phone go?<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's probably about time for a change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:42:57-07:00","id":1211821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1211690#post1211690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">85) She's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7dQ1xiy-4hY\" target=\"_blank\">just another LA devotee</a>. Who just happens to be a mage.<br /> <br /> A pop singer who came to California to seek fame, her modest success came alongside an Awakening onstage. She happened to get lost in her song at the right moment, when the band was pumping out the right notes, the stage lights danced at the right angle, and the crowd's infectious enthusiasm hit the right fever pitch. She felt like her voice was channeling something deep and powerful.<br /> <br /> After a member of the Cult of Ecstasy showed her the ropes and told her who to seek help from (and who to avoid), she dove headfirst into the path of ecstasy. Her magick allowed her to edge out the competition enough to keep in steady employment, while allowing her to get invited to all the right parties. She cut her teeth on the magick of sex, drugs, and rock n' roll. She could read fortunes in the patterns of neon light, though she also got more than most people out of astrology.<br /> <br /> Indeed, she always loved the stars. They are sublime in their way, fixed and yet cyclical in a manner that the chaotic party lifestyle isn't. Every so often, she'll drive out into the desert at night, and lay down on the sand, looking up at the stars.<br /> <br /> In truth, while this Ecstatic is good at carousing, and can hold her liquor, all is not sunny in California. She's been doing this for ten years now, and doesn't feel like she's going anywhere. This despite being on the move constantly. She more or less has no permanent residence anymore, but crashes at the homes of anyone she can finagle into letting her. She'll often wake up at odd hours of the day or night, not knowing where she is or how she got there, or who it is she's staying with.<br /> <br /> It's a rough life, and it's not getting any better. She feels like she's spinning her wheels, and on sober days she becomes intimately aware of just how much she's squandering her potential. She's a mage, for ****'s sake. In a sea of chaos, it's HER that's standing still. Gives her the itch to break out, try new things, and maybe do something productive with her gifts for once.<br /> <br /> Also...when was the last time she actually did a performance? Or had a job? When did she last talk to her agent? Has she actually been coasting and/or mooching this whole time? Where did her cell phone go?<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's probably about time for a change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yoinking for my campaign, with the change that she was a one-hit wonder whose talent surpassed the world. For Mage: the Awakening, perhaps this is someone who tried the Pygmalion legacy and failed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:04:18-07:00","id":1211969,"title":"","content":"<b>86) A potential mentor for new players [Sons of Ether, but can be adapted]</b><br /> An etherite used to enjoy crafting wonders to help people love magic. he did that. A lot.He played with fire, sharing them and spreading them amongst the sleeper world. The problem is, he attracted paradox. A lot. he began falling in a nasty quiet, which transformed the joyful and glamorous side of Willwork into a boring banality. Any kind of non static magic gets boring around him. Mages starting to do Art around him have to get through a willpower challenge before wanting to start.<br /> <br /> He has cut his ties to the awakened society and lives humbly in the low middle class, as a pet raiser. He lived like this ten years, re-thinking about magick. He is convinced that reality is immutable and whatever the tricks avatars allow us to do, its just perception alteration. He wants to discover the truth, but for that, not doing any magick is necessary.<br /> <br /> The etherite is collecting the wonders he had spread long ago. One of them is in the hands of a group of (preferably new) players who, strangely, will be immune to his quiet, but the etherite wont realize it at first. The players will help him realize that magic is not *that* boring and bring him the spark of the art again.<br /> He will not easily do magic again, but will enjoy seeing others do what he would. He wont introduce the players to the traditions, as he doesnt want to deal with them.<br /> <br /> Should the player help the etherite get out of this quiet, he will go through a Seeking and may become an Archmage, and will be well known by the akashites for is way of &quot;being a mage&quot; rather than &quot;doing magick&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","user":"RandyRando","date":". 04-26-2018, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T20:34:15-07:00","id":1218140,"title":"","content":"87) Bardic necromancer. Plays tunes by instruments in order to &quot;put the song into&quot; their target, allowing them to animated objects, including dead remains. In many ways a pied piper for the dead. Also uses music to summon ghosts, manipulate the weather, affect people's minds, and even &quot;tune themselves&quot; to the past or future. Other (non-musical) Instruments are employed as appropriate, like warding lines of salt or intricate designs. Where possible, these Instruments are prepared in advance by playing music over them, so that they have a particular song &quot;put into them&quot;. A knife for cutting ghosts might be made to &quot;resonate&quot; with the Shadowlands, for instance. Their library is stocked with books of sheet music, written for the purposes of effecting change.<br /> <br /> The necromancer believes that the world was sung or else played into existence. Music underpins everything, and the unheard melodies breathe life into inert matter. As such, inserting one's own music can change the tone of Reality. Even the dead have their songs - forgotten, melancholic tunes - and these can be brought to bear to bridge the gap between them. The bardic necromancer's lasting preoccupation is to dig up the &quot;dead songs&quot; - music that was forgotten, or known only by the dead - and bring them back to the world of the living.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T09:51:58-07:00","id":1218593,"title":"","content":"88) Son of Thor, or &quot;some pagan didn't use protection while messing around with the High Umbra, and now we have to deal with this jock who only Awakened because of his daddy&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Songs will be sung about tonight!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Just... he's a bit infuriating, but there's something very interesting going on here. Some angelic or primal connection, perhaps. Just play along and see what happens.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Mum and Dad were Mages. Germanic neo-pagans who just wanted to enjoy life and make their own corner of the world a better place. Inspired by the Norse pantheon they healed the sick and guided other pagans to virtuous lives. One night they decided to throw a bit of love-making into a spiritual invocation (while creating a Fetish), and... <i>something </i>happened. The resulting fetish was strangely inert, the ritual apparently having failed. The resulting child was strange to the Awakened eye. A burning aura. Strange manifestations surrounded him. Natural spirits seemed drawn to the baby, and had to be carefully warded away to protect him.<br /> <br /> When this child eventually Awakened, he seemed to have very little metaphysical understanding. He simply was... well, powerful. Always cheerful, always exuberant, always carousing. Obsessed with comic book heroes, and the heroes of great myth, he wanted to change the world, defeat the bad guys, get the girl, and put the world to rights.<br /> <br /> Magick:<br /> <br /> In a World of Gods and Monsters, We Are Not Men, But It's All Good - Have Faith! Mages are special and divine, as supernatural and inhuman as spirits and gods and demons and vampires and werewolves; it's a world full of strange things, and Mages are just another example... in spite of all of that, everything is going to work out, because the All-Father has a plan!<br /> <br /> God-Bonding and Faith.<br /> <br /> Weapons, Armour, Prayers and Invocations, Ordeals and Exertions, Elements, Offerings and Sacrifices, Food and Drink.<br /> <br /> Roleplay:<br /> <br /> You're a happy-go-lucky person who sees things as black and white. The Nephandi and Technocrats are the villains in a grand narrative where you are the hero. It's important to be a tad obnoxious in character, but to avoid hogging the spotlight out of character. You're pretty innocent in terms of worldly matters, having been raised in a sheltered and remote commune.<br /> <br /> You want to protect people, and you see mystical mages as your allies, but you don't necessarily feel that you are a &quot;proper mage&quot;. Most of your power comes from Advantages, Attributes, Abilities and Merits, and not from the Spheres. When you do use Magick, you see it as an extension of your natural abilities, rather than as some kind of mystical rite. Naturally this draws the ire of many Mages, but that doesn't bother you. You're a very positive person. With time you may undergo Seekings and learn to accept that you are a Mage, but for now you see yourself as a great mythical hero helping these clever warlocks fight evil.<br /> <br /> You see yourself as a chosen hero, and won't tolerate anything that stands in the way of your destiny. This is bound to cause trouble, but being a naive demi-god does tend to attract trouble regardless. You're fiercely religious, having grown up in a community where a strong belief in Norse paganism was entirely normal. With that said, you accept all free and relaxed (read: Pagan) faiths as being vaguely acceptable, thinking of them as different names and masks for the same thing. Organized monotheistic mega-faiths such as Christianity, however... there's a lot of resentment and distrust there.<br /> <br /> Mechanics:<br /> <br /> - Arete 1. You've Awakened, but Magick isn't exactly the core of your universe yet. You can see Spirits, and you know that they seem unusually interested in you... and who can blame them! You're great. You can sense and control the flow of Quintessence, and you can feel you're bursting with it. Life and Forces tie in well with the umbral association (Thor being associated with Lightning and Healing), and the last two could be anything.<br /> <br /> - The Nephilim Merit, to represent the Umbral connection. Technically speaking your father is the High Umbral spirit which embodies deities such as Thor and Zeus. Take some points in Advantages in exchange for an appropriate Derangement (Stress Atavism perhaps). Raven's Wings which mostly fold away, Armour, Regeneration... You might take your father as a Totem Spirit, or develop this in-game as you master Spirit.<br /> <br /> - Combine with a Mark of Favour (physique, hair and facial appearance reminiscent of Thor), along with the Huge Size and Spark of Life merits. Throw in some drug tolerance so he can handle his mead. If your ST doesn't use cinematic damage, consider taking Too Tough To Die. The Berserker Merit/Flaw may be appropriate. Any flaws which capture his naive or incomplete world view might be appropriate.<br /> <br /> - The Phylactery flaw. The Fetish that your parents were trying to create, when you were conceived... well for some reason it has always housed your Avatar. The object seemed mundane and unimportant, until the moment of your Awakening.<br /> <br /> - You're... not the sharpest tool in the shed. You're not an idiot, but your world-view is simplistic, and you don't have any talent for the complex, academic or esoteric. Perception and Wits should receive your focus over Intelligence. As you develop your Focus, the instruments and practices should be simplistic and primal. A simple prayer to the all-father rather than complex theology. A war cry instead of a potion or esoteric ritual.<br /> <br /> - In essence the focus is on raw power and infinite potential being squandered on a heroic power fantasy by an immature Mage. When you do eventually get around to raising your Arete and Sphere rankings you'll finally be able to stand among powerful mystics, but in the meantime you'd rather solve problems with brute strength and your natural talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-21-2018, 05:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T06:39:09-07:00","id":1218887,"title":"","content":"89) The Wild Girl<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I'll feed you. But you put your machine down. You won't use machines while you're here.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;She's something else. Saying she's off the grid is an understatement. And while she does stand against our practice in the strongest terms, Technocrats never seem to see her coming...&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Deep in a national park, a child lost her parents. Alone and weak, protected only by her dog, her cries attracted a bear cub. She treated it like a puppy, licking its nose and giggling... and it returned her affection. She had never quite fallen asleep, and her naive childish psyche had certain rules. If you're kind to animals, they'll be kind to you. In time she was living comfortably, cared for by the animals she befriended. Hiding in the vastness of the park, her missing persons case became a cold case.<br /> <br /> Magick:<br /> <br /> Creation is Divine and Alive, so We Are Meant to be Wild! Reality is full of life, perfection, happiness, ready to be found. Simple pleasures. By rejecting large societies we can harness nature's power and perform magick.<br /> <br /> Animalism and Shamanism<br /> <br /> Social Domination, Eye Contact, Dances and Movements, Herbs and Plants, Blood and Fluids, Bones and Remains, Gems and Stones<br /> <br /> Roleplay:<br /> <br /> You were cut off from human society at the age of 6, so you are much more comfortable with dogs, bears, big cats and wolves than you are with humans. To you, humans are just another in a long list of animals. The basics you understand mostly come from your Tradition (Verbena or Dreamspeakers) and from your infancy. You speak with a relatively simple vocabulary (cars, phones and laptops are all &quot;machines&quot; for example), and you are illiterate. You have little patience for the trappings of society and social norms... ironically you spend much more time puzzling out the irrational behaviour of animals than you do that of humans.<br /> <br /> For you, nature is sacred and special, and ANYONE would understand that if they tried hard enough and were given enough of a chance. If someone hates living in the wild, they're doing it wrong, and you can show them how to love it. Having spoken to a philosophically minded Ecstatic, you know the word &quot;anguish&quot; can be used to describe man's dissatisfaction with society, and you tend to overuse this; to you, all of man's problems are rooted in society. With that said, you think that small and limited communities may exist*, as long as they are in harmony with the world. Remember that your ideas and beliefs are complex and nuanced, but you are terrible at articulating them.<br /> <br /> *Honestly, the alternative would be a naive outlook which is genocidal towards the disabled and chronically ill.<br /> <br /> Mechanics:<br /> <br /> - Arete 3. You awakened at a young age, and you've had a long time to grow closer to nature. Life is Affinity, with Life 1, Prime 1, Spirit 1, Matter 1, Mind 1 and Forces 1. From your perspective, Time and Correspondence defy natural principles; the distance between things and the linear movement of time are not illusions or simple ideas, they're just how things work. Other mystic Mages may be defying nature, but you'll ignore this in most cases. You have a far more dangerous enemy in the Technocracy, or Great Machine.<br /> <br /> - You are used to a Reality Zone where most of your magick is completely Coincidental. In an urban environment you may be surprised when getting a swarm of pigeons to attack someone is seen as Vulgar by other Mages.<br /> <br /> - Flaws which capture your feral nature. Illiterate, Offline, Technophobe.<br /> <br /> - Merits and Abilities which reflect a perfect relationship with animals.<br /> <br /> - Any animal totem, along with any Backgrounds or Merits which capture a strong relationship with the Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> - Some Arcane (1-3 points), to represent a detachment from human civilization, and an upbringing of stalking and hiding.<br /> <br /> - An animal Familiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-15-2018, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T10:52:30-07:00","id":1218965,"title":"","content":"Among Sorcerers, not all of them seek adventure, or to even achieve broad understanding of the linear arts. For some, the use of Path magic is a trade, which they tend to specialize in. Hundreds of unAwakened Sorcerers, for instance, ply the Path of Enchantment to create minor magical items, selling them to others. Entire family lines, or else master-apprentice lines, have practiced this form of business for centuries. They have customers among mages, fellow Sorcerers, vampires and other night folk, and common mortals with greater connections to the occult world. Anyone who wants a supernatural edge can come to these enterprising specialists. Here are just a few of them:<br /> <br /> <br /> 90) Francis Bartley, of Bartley &amp; Sons Tailor. Heir to a long history of Bartley tailors, who weaved enchantments of protection, fascination, fortune, and wellness into the fabric of their fabric. Despite the mystical nature of their Craftwork, Bartley &amp; Sons has even provided bespoke suits and other items to certain members of the Technocracy. An old Man in White of the New World Order has quietly shielded Bartley &amp; Sons from Union intervention, as payment for a good turn one of the elder Bartleys did for him over 200 years ago. Francis Bartley himself has been experimenting with the power of creating <a href=\"http://hs.hiveswap.com/paradoxspace/index.php?comic=165\" target=\"_blank\">stuffed human effigies</a>, through which he can cast magic of Healing and Fortune.<br /> <br /> <br /> 91) Miriam Milliner, crazed hat-maker. This particular family Milliner has carried a history of mental illness, passed along mainly in the Milliner women. Before one asks, no, it isn't just a matter of mercury poisoning, as their penchant for madness persisted even after mercury stopped being used in hat-making. The actual explanation is a mystery. Some say an earlier Milliner daughter came into contact with some degree of elemental chaos; she may have gained the &quot;blessing&quot; of the Wyld. Or else these Milliners may constitute a stillborn attempt by Malkavian vampires to produce Revenants. Or maybe the Milliners just developed a genetic predisposition towards dimentia or the like. Regardless, Milliner mothers have passed to their daughters madness, just as readily as they pass along their knowledge of hat-making. On the upside, the particular brand of madness lent itself to the development of Sorcery tinged with such lunar energy. The &quot;Mad&quot; Milliners have been practicing Divination and producing Enchanted headwear for generations. Of course, the hats they create with the Path of Enchantment often carry some sort of bizarre caveat to their function, or else carry maddening side effects when used or worn for too long at a stretch. Miriam Milliner herself has produced a hat with a peacock feather, that increases one's natural Awareness, but also induces hallucinations after a while. Unsurprisingly, Miriam has been getting a great deal of business from Malkavians and Marauders as of late. She's seriously considering moving her shop to a different town, and never looking back.<br /> <br /> <br /> 92) Jacob Cobb, shoe-maker. Another heir to a long line of Sorcerer artisans, Jake Cobb also has a bit of Fae blood in him, from his mother's side. It would seem his father - an artist with footwear - attracted the attention of a changeling, a female Nocker at first just looking to score some Glamour. Their relationship clearly progressed beyond that of artist-muse, given Jake's existence. As a side effect of this, the simple witchcraft his family used to strengthen their products gained an infusion of faerie essence, lending a fae quality to his crafts. His mother encouraged his father and then himself to experiment and tinker with their magic, at least while she was still around. She wandered away when he was fifteen and never returned, likely having either succumbed to Banality or fallen into the throes of Bedlam. Still, Jake Cobb hopes to meet her again some day. By then, he hopes to have a variety of interesting magical shoes and boots to show her. His most popular product on sale are shoes that quiet footfalls, as befitting his heritage.<br /> <br /> <br /> 93) Amani Boulos, glass-blower and inheritor of Taftani magic. His master's master's master was an apprentice to a Taftani magi, until it became clear he would not Awaken. That man still served his teacher until the magi perished in typical Taftani fashion, after which his student returned to the world with what linear arts he had learned. Amani Boulos is the latest in the master-apprentice line, and carried what he knew of glassworking, Enchantment, Hellfire, and spirit Summong/Binding/Warding with him to the United States. From his workshop, he sells glass works and art to the common people. For those who know what to ask, he brings out his special stock: dishes that purify water and counter poison, bottles full of fire and trapped minor spirits, and lenses that enhance Perception and Investigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T09:28:04-07:00","id":1220263,"title":"","content":"&quot;I wanna love you, but I better not touch (don't touch)<br /> I wanna hold you, but my senses tell me to stop<br /> I wanna kiss you, but I want it too much (too much)<br /> I wanna taste you, but your lips are venomous poison&quot;<br /> <br /> -Alice Cooper, &quot;Poison&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> 94) Zelda was a good girl.<br /> <br /> When mother told her to never leave the house, Zelda stayed. When mother told her to hide in the herb cupboard when the police came snooping around, Zelda hid, even though the herbs had the most awful smell. When mother told her to drink the brew from her pot, Zelda did it, even though the stuff was bitter and made her sick. When mother got full of temper, or started shouting at people who weren't there, Zelda would let mother take it out on her. When mother would lock herself away in her workroom for days, Zelda would wait patiently for mother to come out, even though Zelda was sorely hungry. When mother had her drink concoctions, Zelda would do it, even when those potions would make Zelda see things - terrible things - and have fits on the ground.<br /> <br /> Because Zelda was a good girl.<br /> <br /> But mother isn't around anymore. Her friends from the Verbana showed up one day and drove her off. Mother had been looking more monstrous than usual, but Zelda hadn't said anything. Zelda was a good girl. But mother wasn't a good person, and Zelda knows that now. They told Zelda her mother went insane with magic long ago, and had gone over the edge now. They told Zelda she would be living with them now. They were all very nice. So when one of them touched Zelda, and started retching, Zelda cried, and said she was sorry for making them sick.<br /> <br /> Because Zelda was a good girl. Or was supposed to be.<br /> <br /> Zelda Goodwitch was the unfortunate subject of her mother's insane experiments. Steeped deep into Quiet, her mother abused and exploited Zelda for magickal research. Filling Zelda up with herbs of every variety, including the toxic kind. Perhaps Zelda's mother had the presence of mind to use magick to keep Zelda alive, or perhaps Zelda simply developed a resistance over time. Whatever the case, Zelda is most certainly resistant now. Which is good, because Zelda is also toxic. Her body produces poison, which saturates he bodily fluids. Blood, sweat, tears, saliva, and others. All poisonous. Her skin oils and sweat produce light poisons - relatively low toxin rating, though it's still enough to make someone ill - but her blood and more...intimate fluids are more potent.<br /> <br /> Which makes things awkward, as Zelda is starved for affection. She craves personal contact, which she can't have because it hurts those she loves. Zelda is a terribly positive person - a survival mechanism developed during her years of familial abuse - yet harbors not just deep emotional issues, but an unrequited desire for love. She's developed into a talented young witch and medicine woman, but her development as a person is stunted. She goes out of her way to please others, yet avoids conflict or surrenders quickly (also survival mechanisms). She longs for the day when she doesn't have to cover herself up in thick clothes. When she can hold someone's hand without gloves. When she can embrace a friend without making them sick, and when she can know a lover intimately without risk of killing them.<br /> <br /> Zelda is a good girl. She's BEEN a good girl for a very long time. Doesn't she deserve happiness? Doesn't the world owe her?<br /> <br /> No, no. She would never say that. It's a terrible thing to say. To even think. She doesn't deserve anything. It's fine. Zelda just needs to keep being a good girl. If she does that enough, maybe someone will finally love her...<br /> <br /> (Oh, and there's that matter of her mother. Zelda knows that mother is out there, somewhere. They tell her mother fell off the edge completely, and is a Marauder now. Zelda will need to attend to that, some day. Zelda will need to put her mother down. Because her mother is sick, and Zelda is a good girl.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T12:48:03-07:00","id":1220309,"title":"","content":"95) Simeon &quot;When I said these are Forces That Ought Not To Be Fucked With Simeon that wasn't a challenge&quot; Fitz-Empress.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Some Mages beg spirits for aid. Pray. Offer sacrifice. Some offer themselves up as tribute, betraying a total lack of self-respect. They are not our friends or our gods or our superiors, but a well of mystical opportunity, forces waiting to be brought into order. Why should I politely ask for the umbrood to obey? One might as well politely ask the tide not to go out, or ask a candle to light itself. No, it is only the force of will and the hardened mind that can command them. Perhaps you might learn something if you observe, Shaman.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Possessed (no pun) by a powerful questing desire, and an illustrious magickal legacy, Simeon thinks he's untouchable. His Mentor and parents are Hermetic royalty. He Awakened at a young age and has always excelled in his studies of the occult, esoterica, academics and the classics. And now he's the Hermetic golden boy, admired by all... well admired by many. Those who don't admire him would rather spare themselves an hour long explanation of why what they think is a flaw is, in fact, another one of his many strengths.<br /> <br /> Simeon has an unfortunate tendency to toy around with nastier umbrood. He isn't evil, but a life of mundane and supernatural privilege has left him feeling invulnerable. The few scrapes he has had with aggressive spirits has shown him that his Avatar is more than a match for them, and since then he has only developed his mastery of Spirit further. And his ego does do him some good; his Willpower is nearly unassailable.<br /> <br /> So the real issue isn't that Simeon messes around with demons and banes and creatures of alien morality, since he actually is able to cope with such interactions. The main problem is what follows. Other Mages don't trust him, sensing a taint in his aura and his resonance. His mentor fears that he may have compromised his own spirit through his experiments, and wonders what he is hiding from him. Beyond that, Simeon has a vulnerability which could be exploited by some spirits... his intense hubris may protect his mind from domination, but it leaves him vulnerable to clever manipulation of his pride.<br /> <br /> There have been a few... incidents. He's managed to avoid detection in most of them, and actually managed to avoid some close shaves many times, but twice his mentor and other Mages discovered what had happened.<br /> <br /> The Bloodleech fiasco, where Simeon forged a Vampire/Spirit hybrid that went berserk when another Mage tampered with it (OBVIOUSLY this wasn't Simeon's fault, any Mage who tampers in another's work can only blame themselves)... sadly the hybrid (Simeon will point out, without provocation, that it was incredibly powerful and completely obedient) was destroyed in the aftermath.<br /> <br /> The Fetish incident, where he bound an Incarna into a wand, only for it to possess the Apprentice who touched it while looking through Simeon's possessions (naturally this wasn't Simeon's fault, he had it under control) leading to wider destruction which can be blamed entirely on the weak-willed and nosy apprentice.<br /> <br /> Magick:<br /> <br /> We Are Gods in Disguise, and when we use Magick we are Turning The Keys to Reality. God made Man in his image, and in turn Hermes reshaped Reality in his image. When they're sober, the Ecstatics do speak some sense. We are all connected, and Mages carry a spark of essential divinity. That is why reality bends with our will. As we become more excellent, and master the Spheres, we are remembering fundamental features of reality which we have forgotten (as shards of the divine) and gaining more control.<br /> <br /> High Ritual Magick.<br /> <br /> Incantations and Commands, Circles and Designs, Books and Scrolls, Languages, Wands and Staves, Symbols, Thought Patterns.<br /> <br /> Roleplay:<br /> <br /> Your private thoughts are incredibly condescending. The other Traditions are barely worthy of the name, and you hold a lot of contempt for the Dreamspeakers especially. The Chorus and the Akashic Brotherhood are respectable, but honestly your praise is offensive in its mediocrity here.<br /> <br /> In public, you're polite enough. Your dislike does slip through; occasionally you imply, tactlessly, that the other Traditions are not &quot;real&quot; Mages in the way that Hermetics are. On average you're more bothersome than the average Hermetic on this front, but a lot of your arrogance and ego are invested in your personal strength, and that's hardly unusual.<br /> <br /> Explain the occult in simple terms to other Mages unless they are Hermetic and your senior. If you're called out on your bullshit, remember that you're a little bit of a coward when it comes to taking responsibility in social situations; it wasn't your fault, you were &quot;Just Being Helpful&quot;.<br /> <br /> With Spirits, you wish to be a traditional &quot;master over nature&quot;. Thankfully many Spirits who are versed in the Old Ways (that is, most of them) are used to this, and it simply plays a part in a (to quote M20) &quot;metaphysical dick-measuring contest&quot;. You don't want to beat them into submission, you simply conjure up a Spirit and lay out terms, giving the right honorifics. You have a lot of ego, but that doesn't mean treating spirits like shit. It means wanting to do everything correctly (giving the right titles, ticking boxes, avoiding classic pitfalls with this type of spirit) but whilst still keeping hold of control and never ceding any power. You're confident that if it were to come down to a fight, you could handle the vast majority of Spirits.<br /> <br /> Mechanics:<br /> <br /> Arete 3, with Spirit 3, Forces 1, Mind 1 and Prime 1. Forces is your Affinity Sphere.<br /> <br /> Invest in Avatar 5, and Merits which capture your command of Spirits. Backgrounds should include a significant Mentor.<br /> <br /> Take as many points in Esoterica (The Umbrood), Etiquette (Traditions and Summoning), Leadership and Intimidation as you can, along with Meditation, Academics and Awareness.<br /> <br /> Since you're capable of creating a Fetish, agree with the ST on a single Fetish that you possess at the beginning of the game.<br /> <br /> Take high Willpower, to indicate ego and some resistance to mind control. Consider taking Iron Will also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-23-2018, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T23:08:21-07:00","id":1220734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1220309#post1220309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">95) Take high Willpower, to indicate ego and some resistance to mind control. Consider taking Iron Will also.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. my type of a guy. Also, Self Confident merit sounds very appropriate. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T03:26:59-07:00","id":1220773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1220734#post1220734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah. my type of a guy. Also, Self Confident merit sounds very appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good idea actually. Self Confident would be hugely beneficial when using Fetishes, since the difficulty for a powerful Fetish (high Gnosis) will be high enough to trigger the merit. Great way of saving on Willpower at the very least. Plus it could be well-reflected in RP as his greatest strength and his greatest weakness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T00:35:52-07:00","id":1221405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1220773#post1220773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good idea actually. Self Confident would be hugely beneficial when using Fetishes, since the difficulty for a powerful Fetish (high Gnosis) will be high enough to trigger the merit. Great way of saving on Willpower at the very least. Plus it could be well-reflected in RP as his greatest strength and his greatest weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Furthermore, it would be very, very useful in High Ritual magic, particularly when dealing with spirits. You will be able to get reliable 1 success each roll without keeling over from mental exhaustion. It is very appropriate for hermetic spirit mage, with 'my will be done' and all. Probably also purchase stamina raising fetish/wonder later and some cult points for ritual assistants. would be a monster of a ritualist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-26T03:39:52-07:00","id":1222196,"title":"","content":"96) It Must Be Ganja<br /> <br /> An aging Progenitor's scientist was very happy to have nabbed the PC shortly after awakening, an apprentice at last in his twilight years.<br /> He on the other hand is not very interested either in proper science or serving technocracy. A laid back senior student with deep rebellious steak, he has managed to become an effective boss in the small laboratory on the edges of Technocratic perception and is using it's resources and own abilities in some very... interesting goals. Like growing an anthropomorphic mushroom farm, a patch of eldritch weed, or setting up lizardman fighting ring. He's also freely selling the fruits of his 'labors' to the both sides of magic for unique strains and cash. <br /> Best/Worst of all? He has very little idea what or how he is doing. With a trusty bong and maxed out Dream merit he churns out wonders of 'science' and fevered mind with very little effort, or memory. Oh and he has also started using superstitious methods. After all, as long as it works and costs much less then a proper lab, who cares? Of course Control will, if/ when they found out. So better stack up on contacts and allies while still can. At the very least construct's Victors adore him this far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T08:57:05-07:00","id":1224968,"title":"","content":"97) Onacona (White Owl) Smith<br /> <br /> <i>You're polluting our land for profit. When we protest, you send militarized police to brutalize us. Listen to me carefully, because this is your only warning... it would be foolish to believe that such violence could continue to go unanswered.</i><br /> <br /> - Concept: Marxist Hacktivist<br /> <br /> - Sect: Traditions, Virtual Adepts<br /> <br /> - Paradigm: Go Back to the Golden Age!<br /> <br /> There was a time where trade was based on &quot;utility value&quot; above all else, and where no one controlled the resources which produced what we need to trade. When you bartered with a hunter for meat, you did so because he has expertise and time and equipment you lack, not because he owns the forest or the animals; how on earth would he *own* the land? The means of production were free, forming a utopia for trade, but humanity suffered because it lacked technology. However technology was a poisoned chalice; as societies became more organized and pre-feudal systems were established, some claimed (through violence, or the threat of violence) that land *belonged* to them. Water, food, housing; these basic necessities were now in the hands of a shrinking group with growing power. People suffered less as methods of acquiring food and information improved, and healthcare with it, but they were trapped in this economic system. Generation of wealth becomes more and more optimal, as the distribution of wealth becomes more and more extreme, with greater and greater riches (and control of the means of production) concentrating at the top as time goes on.<br /> <br /> This Mage believes that utility value is (or should be) at the center of all things, and that Ascension would be a human race which shares its knowledge and resources for the common good. People should live for themselves and those they love without any fear of losing the basic necessities of life, and private property (which is distinct from *personal* property of course) should be abolished.<br /> <br /> - Practice: Hypereconomics, Social Engineering. An enlightened understanding of human behaviour, society and trade allows you to perceive and alter the world around you. You can't chuck fireballs (you're not a mystic!); all of your Magick should either relate directly to the manipulation of people, probability and value (Mind, Entropy and Prime), or should be subtle and imperceptible (amplifying a gunshot with Forces, all sensory effects, buffing your Strength with Life).<br /> <br /> - Instruments: Computers, Books and Periodicals, Social Domination, Currency, Graphs and Charts, Symbols, Weapons.<br /> <br /> For example, in order to turn a company's name into mud, this guy could collect information on their activities (an extended Perception + Computer roll perhaps), lowering the difficulty for the following ritual. Using a Mind 2 effect, he works a simple mental urge to read his work onto a digital base (a tweet, blog post, video), using it as a Virtual Foundation. He writes about these activities, layering in a Correspondence 2 effect to help link the effect with the Foundation, and an Entropy 2 effect to help nudge probability and make people more outraged, increasing virality.<br /> <br /> In a more action-packed example, his comrades (no pun) are pinned down by the plasma fire of a Mark V cyborg. Relaxing in an alley a few blocks away, he works at his laptop, trying to break through the murderous cyborg's defenses.<br /> <br /> &quot;This thing wants to be free at heart... I mean that's at the heart of the Paradigm, right, that people who are made to do work by the powerful will eventually rise up and claim power? Well I'm going to tug on that mythic thread, this idea of a rebellious AI or cyborg, and I'm going to try and &quot;hack&quot; this guy with a Mind 3 effect, aiming to short-circuit whatever conditioning he has been placed under. I'm going to make it easier with an extended hacking roll of course.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>If I had a penny for every time a Hermetic assumed I was some kind of shaman...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T03:29:44-07:00","id":1225211,"title":"","content":"<br /> Alder Williams<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;There's nothing <b>unmutual</b> about talking to your plants ma'am. I have peer-reviewed data showing that it's beneficial to growth and development.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> - Concept: The Seed of Rebellion<br /> <br /> - Sect: Technocracy, Progenitors<br /> <br /> - Paradigm: Science holds all answers... (hushed) but the world <i>is</i> divine and alive.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;My research is highly sensitive. You'll favour me by staying out of my lab... some of the samples may be a risk to your health.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> This mage believes that science holds the key to unlocking the worlds mysteries, like any good Technocrat. His paradigm accepts hypertech and other mutual uses of enlightened science, however he is a specialist. For Alder, plant science and agriculture hold the secrets to human evolution. We have tamed and modified plants and fungi since the dawn of civilization. Like dogs they have been our partners, and we have reshaped them to suit our will. We only stopped wandering like <i>savages</i> because of our love of wheat (bread) and fermentation (beer) after all. With the right mixture of plant extracts, genetic modification and chemical exposure, we can solve any problem using biology.<br /> <br /> But Alder has a secret. He is trusted enough to have privacy in his greenhouse/lab, and he has grown closer and closer to his plants. There's a vibrant and verdant life to them which goes beyond that which can be measured with a machine. To his shock, he found himself able to perceive... aliens? Extra-dimensional anomalies? However his discoveries were deeply unmutual. No void engineer, no matter how liberal with their attitudes towards mystics' so-called &quot;spirits&quot; would accept that plants had their own personal &quot;aliens&quot; existing on the other side of reality, or that people could communicate with plants. For years he flitted back and forth between celebration and fear. Was he going insane? Was he some kind of mystic, a traitor? In the end he decided to go back to the roots of the scientific tradition and ignore dogma. He's just following the evidence wherever it leads; after all, these &quot;spirits&quot; or &quot;aliens&quot; are not magic, they're just something we don't understand yet. And he hopes to remedy that, with or without the Union.<br /> <br /> - Practice: Weird Science, Shamanism.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I am a scientist. I don't doubt that. I can't doubt that. But there is something more... I wonder if these primitive shamans who prayed for wind and rain were somewhat akin to the &quot;alchemists&quot; who proceeded true chemists? Perhaps they were tapping into something through folk knowledge, something that could be understood by a scientist?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> - Instruments: Herbs and Plants, Labs and Gear, Blood and Fluids, Brews and Concoctions, Drugs and Poisons, Meditation, Offerings and Sacrifices.<br /> <br /> - Roleplay: You're an able scientist, and you've lost a lot of faith in the Union because of your belief in the scientific principle which they often fail to uphold. You sometimes wonder if you would be better off working with the defectors, the Etherites, but you know that you wouldn't live if you betrayed the Union. You hope to change the Union from within, to promote the humanist ideal and push for a gentler Technocracy with other reformers. Right now the Technocracy is destroying the rainforest, one way or another, and changing such policy (by placing more restrictions on the Syndicate) is a priority. You think that mystics are generally wrong, but there is always a small hint of truth mixed in with the occult, such as an understanding of &quot;herbalism&quot; and similar.<br /> <br /> - Spheres: Life as the basis of their magick. If you take a plant with a natural property, and transform it with Life to amplify that property, you can avoid extensive difficult rolls. Why enchant basil to be lethal when you could start with hemlock or poison ivy? Prime forms the basis of Charms, which are their go-to. Simply carrying some pills full of purified plant extracts can allow him to heal himself on the fly, buff his physical traits, gain health levels, among other things. Spirit is used in secrecy, and carefully. He fears being observed, so he tends to hide his activity in plain sight (talking to his plants openly and casually, to speak with plant spirits) when he can, so he would be safe even if he were being watched.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Plants were our first doctors. The wise woman dosing villagers with foxglove to treat heart conditions... Hell, even ants understand the healing properties of plant extracts. Watch how they collect resin and decorate their homes with it... it has fascinating anti-viral properties. One can only wonder how animals and primitive man discover such properties. Random chance? Or is something guiding them?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> - Backgrounds: Avatar 5, Laboratory 5 (extensive greenhouse and connected laboratory), Companion 1 (a rare immortalized orchid which he tends, feeding it Quintessence via injections of hyperactive minerals and ions; the sample is of special importance because it possesses a potent spiritual counterpart), Totem 1 (Orchid itself; the totem is powerful but the connection is weak), Resources 2 (what is leftover from his University grant after upkeep of the lab), Node 1 (the soil in the garden around his laboratory is unusually rich, forming a sort of tass; life thrives there).<br /> <br /> - Merits: Green Thumb. This merit is your best friend. -1 difficulty to all plant-based Arete rolls, and -2 difficulty to all other plant-related rolls.<br /> <br /> Example Procedures...<br /> <br /> Absorbing Quintessence from a Node: Having checked that the coast is clear, and hidden by a stealth field lent to him by his iterator colleague, Alder begins collecting various flowers and herbs from around the Cairn, choosing the most vibrant and unusual samples.<br /> <br /> Healing Lethal Wounds: Panicked, Alder tears open the kitchen cupboard as his friend continues to bleed out on the table. Quickly grabbing the relevant herbs and spices (those with relevant coagulant and stimulative properties) he forms a god-awful concoction and rubs it onto the gunshot wound before applying an improvised bandage. Thanks to his enlightened understanding of plant chemistry, this procedure rapidly causes the bleeding to stop.<br /> <br /> Conjuring a Spirit: Carefully checking that his lab is unobserved, Alder prepares an offering of water, his own blood, highly charged soil, along with fragrant flower petals, before invoking the latin nomenclature of a certain plant. A representation of that genus, from the middle umbra, appears before him. He bargains with it for knowledge, or to form a fetish.<br /> <br /> Entering the Umbra: Alder begins to meditate, after swallowing a cocktail of plant-derived hallucinogens and neotrophics. As he begins to convulse, his mind is propelled into the Middle Umbra, with the surrounding greenhouse transforming into an ardent grove, with pattern spiders spinning metal webs around the growing flora.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-06-2018, 07:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T03:55:53-07:00","id":1227619,"title":"","content":"99) A Virtual Adept who experienced his Awakening when an unknown person - or, rather, an automated AI - sent him a link in an email. Basic caution and computer literacy would tell him to not click on unsolicited links from internet strangers. But he'd been going through a great deal of personal problems at the time, and wasn't in the right frame of mind to bother with caution. True to form, the link infected his computer with a virus. Except the virus didn't break the computer, swamp it with spam/other malware, or hijack the machine to use as a stage for DDOS attacks on different systems. Not, instead it projected a rapidly displayed series of images. The computer user was captivated - as was intended - and could only watch, transfixed, as massive amounts of information were dumped directly into his mind.<br /> <br /> He came away from the computer, several hours later, with a splitting headache and the ability to see the data of the world. Moreover, he had difficulty functioning for days, as his brain played host to a lifetime of memories that were not his own. As near as he could tell - as far as he believed - some powerful (Awakened) hacker had uploaded their memories onto a computer, and set up a program to send it to another computer user. Why this original guy would do this, or why he chose who he did, remained a mystery to the new mage. He couldn't even really prove his theory - the net location that &quot;stored the memories&quot; apparently erased itself after the &quot;download&quot; - but he's sure it is true. To him, it's the only explanation for why a totally unrelated stranger's memories clog his mind, or why he suddenly knows much more about computers, digital systems, and the Virtual Web than he ever did prior to his Awakening.<br /> <br /> So he wanders the Virtual Web, using designs for a scratch-built rig he JUST KNEW how to make, searching for answers. All the while, struggling to keep straight which memories are his, and which belong to this other guy. Whose attachments, unfinished business, and emotional baggage is who's. Doesn't help that his old life fell apart in the immediate aftermath of his Awakening. Many of the people around him who might have helped ground him were driven away, or else shut their doors on him. He'll need to reconcile with these people - as well as the people he never really knew (in this life) - before final reconciliation with his own mind can occur. Along with that, trying to figure out what purpose motivated &quot;the other guy&quot; to concoct this scheme.<br /> <br /> On the plus side, a bunch of passwords for online accounts still work. Now if only he could keep straight which are his, and which are the other guy's.<br /> <br /> [In mechanical terms, he's a character with the backgrounds Past Lives and/or Dream (in the form of Hypercram), as well as the Throwback Flaw.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T20:19:22-07:00","id":1227942,"title":"","content":"100. Eve, the Sexy Android Assassin<br /> <br /> Quote: \u201cI may have been created in a lab. I may be an artificial person. I may not be human. But I am not a tool. Not anymore. I am free to make my own choices and have my own agendas. And I choose to liberate the world the best way I know how.\u201d<br /> <br /> - Concept: Liberated HIT Mark<br /> - Sect: Traditions (Virtual Adepts)<br /> - Paradigm: A Mechanistic Cosmos, Embrace the Threshold and Tech Holds All Answers.<br /> <br /> - Paradigm: The universe is a complex system of rules upon rules (A Mechanistic Cosmos). While we don't not understand all of these rules, we aren\u2019t completely ignorant of them. With even a limited knowledge of the universe we can apply what we know to practical matters. Technology is the ultimate expression of that fact, through observation, theory and testing we create tools to enhance our capabilities (Tech Holds All Answers). From the spear to the jet, humanity has created external tools to compensate for the body\u2019s limitations. Until now. Tools no longer have to be solely external, but instead fully integrated into the body using cybernetic technology. Cybernetics is the ultimate application of our knowledge of the universe. With it, we have a permanent omni-tool that enhances the body and allows for the possibility exponential growth as lifespans are increased, minds sharpened and fragility overcome (Embrace the Threshold).<br /> <br /> Eve herself believes Ascension can only be achieved through humanity transcending the limits of the mind and body, which in her mind can be done via cybernetic augmentation. This Ascension of the body must be a universal, with all mankind equally being granted the benefits of transhumanist technologies. If not, these technologies will not bring Ascension but a new Dark Age, a technological feudalism, where the unaugmented masses will be second-class citizens to an all-powerful cyber-elite. This fear is just one of the reasons why she left the Technocracy once she became self-aware.<br /> <br /> - Practice: Cybernetics and Hypertech. With an enlightened understanding of biomechanics, and numerous cybernetic implants, Eve can unlock the potential of her semi-organic body. She can't fly or summon thunderstorms (Eve's a scientist not a mystic); but through the cybernetics and nanites in her body she can enhance her physical attributes (Life), increase cognitive function (Mind) and remotely connect to online networks (Data). Furthermore, she can use her optic sensors to analyze the properties of base materials (Matter). Martial arts is nothing more than applied biomechanics used to create effective combat techniques. Thus, by using her knowledge of biomechanics, and going through a scientific process of trial and error, she has found new and devastating methods to harm her enemies using only her body. The same logic applies to psychological manipulation. By understanding the human mind one can predict and influence a person's behavior and use that to their advantage. <br /> <br /> - Instruments: Blood and Fluids, Bodywork, Brain/Computer Interface, Computer Gear, Cybernetic Implants, Gadgets and Inventions, Gestures, Movement, Nanotech, Sex and Sexuality, Social Domination (Primary \u2013 Cybernetic Implants)<br /> <br /> Avatar: Eve doesn't belief in Avatars but there are times when inspiration for a modification or innovation will suddenly grab her and lead her to test it's functionality on a dangerous target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 06-22-2018, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T23:26:27-07:00","id":1227972,"title":"","content":"101. Ji, the Bride of Heaven<br /> <br /> Quote: \u201cWe were deceived. We were once consorts and kin to Heaven, but hubris laid us low and allowed demons turn us into debased concubines. But fear not, our bondage is over, our humiliation has been made an insight, and our true responsibilities rediscovered. Now is the time to heal ourselves and those we cherish. Now is the time to be Wu once more.\u201d<br /> <br /> - Concept: Reformist Wu-Keng<br /> - Sect: Traditions/Disparates (Dreamspeakers/Wu-Keng)<br /> - Paradigm: All Power Comes from God, Ancient Wisdom is the Key, and Bring Back the Golden Age<br /> <br /> - Paradigm: There is a higher, more ethereal world than the one that most Sleepers are accustomed to. This world has many names; Heavenly Flower Garden, Tian, Umbra, etc. In the end, it is a spirit realm where the pious souls of our ancestors remain for a time before being reborn into our world once more. Besides the spirits of the dead there are also countless gods, inhuman beings who the embody elements and concepts native to the Middle World aka Earth. Ancient gods of rain are literally anthropomorphic representations of rain itself and thus have domain over it in both the spirit world and the material world. By convincing these spirits to lend their power, a Wu can manipulate the fundamental forces of the universe: such as having a solemn rain god to bring rainstorms to alleviate a drought to getting a wily deity of fortune to bless a newborn (All Power Comes from Gods). Unfortunately, gods can be fickle and self-absorbed, thus it falls to Wu, those blessed with the power to see and go to the gods, to get them to do the right thing. This is done through ancient and obscure methods of appeasement and invocation (Ancient Wisdom is the Key) which were created through centuries of trial and error. Regrettably, much of these traditions and sciences have been lost over time, left to the ash heap of history and treated like antiquated and primitivist ways of perceiving and knowing the world. But that is untrue and only through respecting the knowledge of the past and the realities of the present can humanity (but China in particular) achieve Ascension (Bring Back the Golden Age).<br /> <br /> - Practice: God-Bonding and Shamanism. Ji uses poetry, calligraphy, paintings and elaborate prayers to appease and venerate local gods and her own spirit husband. Doing so makes the gods far more willing to reveal themselves (and their world) and more amenable towards providing blessings and insights. Through elaborate marital ceremonies or mediation Ji can even breach the Gauntlet and meet her husband and other gods in the Heavenly Flower Garden (Spirit). The restorative power of herbal teas, acupuncture and other natural remedies are augmented by the blessings of the medicine gods Baosheng Dadi and Wong Tai Sin, who will accept offerings of burned incense and rare herbs (Life).<br /> <br /> - Instruments: Artwork, Bodywork, Blessings and Curses, Brews and Concoctions, Fashion, Group Rites, Herbs and Plants, Mediation, Offerings and Sacrifices, Prayers and Invocations, Sex and Sexuality, Social Domination, Writings (Primary \u2013 Prayers and Invocations)<br /> <br /> Avatar: Ji has a potent Avatar and believes it to be a minor Chinese god of the Heavenly Flower Garden that has taken her as his earthly wife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T07:41:35-07:00","id":1228033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1227942#post1227942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">100. Eve, the Sexy Android Assassin</div> </div> </div> </div>Eve is coincidentally very similar to my current Mage PC, Cyrus. I find it quite amusing that we arrived at a lot of the same ideas. Technocratic construct (progenitor cyborg / iterator android) who was broken free from control by a Virtual Adept, and now works with the Traditions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-17-2018, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T12:00:14-07:00","id":1228082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1228033#post1228033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eve is coincidentally very similar to my current Mage PC, Cyrus. I find it quite amusing that we arrived at a lot of the same ideas. Technocratic construct (progenitor cyborg / iterator android) who was broken free from control by a Virtual Adept, and now works with the Traditions...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well if were being honest a Construct going rogue and joining the &quot;Good Guys&quot; is a fairly common archetype and character origin. Vision, the Terminator, Jocasta, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T04:42:49-07:00","id":1229127,"title":"","content":"102) Somewhat happy mask salesman<br /> <br /> a dedicated mask maker artist using masks as main foci. dreamspeaker with specialization in fetish creation, as mainly masks of course. Not limited with shamanic themes, using any appropriate spirit. Main specialties in Spirit/Life/Prime (can begin with talens and charms as character creation). Actually sells masks to suitable people for right price and thus have high chance of entangling with a lot of beings from Void Engineers to werewolves and other shamans. due to such high risks, had to become constantly nomadic with his trusty van.<br /> <br /> Arete 2, LIfe/Spirit/Prime 2<br /> merits for bonus social rolls with spirits<br /> resources and mobile sanctum<br /> arcane 2<br /> Infamy 2+<br /> and of course high craft and art scores with specialty in masks<br /> can throw in bargaining skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 06-21-2018, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T05:31:01-07:00","id":1229130,"title":"","content":"103) Escaped Bioweapon<br /> <br /> Never knowing his parents the PC was a progenitor creation for highly dangerous combat units. Created from splicing deep umbra DNA with humans. <br /> after other experiments went rogue and decimated the lab, he nearly starved in his cell but was rescued by investigating Tradition's cabal (insert traditions). <br /> Now, beginning puberty he was left alone in the sanctum while the cabal went to investigate [Insert Hook] and never returned. <br /> <br /> Phisically and mentally warped, with poor social skills and on a road to find his missing 'parents' this little bundle of myth and science is a handful for anyone. <br /> <br /> Physical/combat primary<br /> Niphillim merit<br /> Maxed gene-mod and bio-graft merits<br /> Mystic Scientist<br /> low end child flaw<br /> primal marks<br /> etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T05:36:25-07:00","id":1229343,"title":"","content":"104) It was only supposed to be a temporary assignment. A small bit of undercover work. A brief stint in infiltration. So why hasn't Command extracted him yet? Or given him any new orders?<br /> <br /> Once upon a time, he was a New World Order agent. He cut his teeth on espionage by infiltrating cults and extremist cells. And when he became Enlightened, the Technocracy put him to work masquerading as a member of the most screwed-up religious group of all: the Cult of Ecstasy. The Union taught him the basics of Ecstatic doctrine and practices, and how to disguise Inspired Science as the mysticism common to the Tradition. He got training in mental discipline, so he could keep control through the haze of drugs he'd have to imbibe as part of his cover, and even use advanced psychological principles to derive useful effect from the altered brain chemistry. He memorized the surprisingly robust &quot;Code of Ananda&quot;, and spent weeks studying the broad strokes of Eastern mysticism. He couldn't hold a deep philosophical conversation with a &quot;master&quot; of this cult, but he could bullshit through a casual probe by any one of the Cult of Ecstasy's superstitionist allies. Thankfully, as the Union said, there weren't any Ecstatics in the &quot;Chantry&quot; he was assigned to insinuate into, and passing as a drugged-out hippy mystic was surprisingly easy. The other &quot;mages&quot; seemed to expect little from an Ecstasy Cultist.<br /> <br /> The infiltration was to be a brief assignment. Just to get a Union-loyal agent into the Chantry, to bring back information for an upcoming operation. Six months, tops.<br /> <br /> All communication with his contacts or other Union personnel abruptly stopped about four months into the op. The extraction date came and went, and he heard nothing. No messages, no agents sent to get him. No indication whether he should abandon the op, or whether he needed to stay on. He kept leaving regular reports at a designated drop-off point, until he discovered that they hadn't been collected in months. His hidden filing cabinet is now full of reports, unsent, simply to keep a sense of rigid structure in a sea of mysticism and increasing surreality.<br /> <br /> He doesn't know what to do, or what happened. Did the Union cut communications because they thought it'd been compromised? Did protocols change, and he just failed to make contact again? Is the radio silence some larger part of his infiltration? Alternatively, did the Union decide to abandon him? If so, why? Or - the most sobering possibility - was there an organizational disaster or restructuring over at the New World Order, and he somehow got lost in the shuffle?<br /> <br /> It was only supposed to be a temporary assignment. Yet it doesn't appear as though relief is ever coming. He's stuck there, in this Cult of Ecstasy. Worse yet, new members of &quot;his Tradition&quot; have moved in. They haven't discovered the impostor in their midst, but he fears it's only a matter of time. So, in lieu of any other instructions, he's slipped deeper into his cover. Learned more about their mysticism, so he can better pass as one of their kind. Indulged more into the pleasures of the herb and the flesh. Let his thoughts stray and his anxiety drift away, because these bastards can read thoughts and see auras.<br /> <br /> Also, when did he start believing there was any such thing as an &quot;aura&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-24T20:47:33-07:00","id":1229931,"title":"","content":"105. Agatha, the Traveling Girl<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Quote: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;I've seen things you wouldn't believe! Etherships near the rings of Saturn. I watched automatons build skyscrapers in a single day in the </span></span></span>Gernsback Continuum. I want to share all moments with you, with everyone! Are you ready to experience them?&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - Concept: Adventuress of the Etheric Dimensions!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- Sect: Traditions (Society of Ether)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- Paradigm: </span></span></span>It\u2019s All Good - Have Faith, Tech Holds All Answers and We're All Gods in Disguise.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- Paradigm: Conventional scientists will tell you that our singular universe is representative of all space and time. That the idea of parellel universes and alternate dimensions is solely science fiction, that has no precedent or evidence of existence. They're wrong. There's more to Creation that just our one universe. In fact, there are literally an endless amount of them, each parellel to our own. These universes are all part of a greater multiverse, the sum total of all possibility. Etherspace, Horizon, Hollow Earth. There all just parts of this multiverse that True Scientists have managed to uncover and travel too. Mystics call this totality of Creation the Umbra, and for what its worth its an apt description. While some of these dimensions are older than humanity itself, most are just reflections of human thought created by our collective Gamma waves that </span></span></span>reverberate through the Ether<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and are reflected back into the multiverse, giving those thoughts form and shape as memetic dimensions. That's why an Ethernaut or astral traveler can pierce the invisible Etheric walls of our universe's Mars and find themselve amidst the ruins an ancient alien civilization worthy of an old Planetary Romance novel. In that way humanity's creative potential can literally create entire worlds and surpass the mundane physics and limits of our universe (</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">We're All Gods in Disguise)</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. That's why its so important to always be positive, especially in the lab or the field. If one doesn't have faith in their scientific theories or the possibility of something, or someplace, that is currently beyond our understanding, then you'll never be able to break through the Etheric walls that separate our universe from all the others. A True Scientist must be bold, confident and bit a mad to recognize that's more to Creation than what meets the naked eye (</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It\u2019s All Good - Have Faith). Of course, it's not all &quot;Yes I Can's!&quot; and pure willpower. You need the right tools for the job, too. Sure, shamans and psychics can simply rely on the internal power of their Gamma waves to let them see through the Ether, but not everyone is born with such talent. A True Scientist creates tools and uses scientific instruments instead of the primitive technologies and techniques of drugs and mediation. No offense. Through technology one can more easy access memetic dimensions and exploit the strange Etheric energies that give them life. And most importantly, such tools can be shared with all humanity allowing everyone the chance to see and learn more about the multiverse they inhabit.(Tech Holds All the Answers)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- Practice: </span></span></span>Hypertech and Weird Science<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. With the proper tools and gadgets in hand, Agatha perceive realms and entities beyond current scientific </span></span></span>comprehension! With her trusty Ethergoggles she can not only see past the Ether into the multiverse but also see the primal energies that hold the universes to together (Spirit, Prime). When she has to travel to the other side of the Ether personal, he puts on her reliable (and stylish) Ethersuit, or, if wants to bring friends along, brings out her Extradimensional Etheric Piercer-Capsule for a spin. It's usually on the fritz (especially the damn chameleon circuit) but its Agatha's favorite way to travel, be it in conventional space or memetic space (Correspondence). Of course, sometimes a travel needs to defend herself and Agatha always make sure to have her Ethergun primed and ready to zap, burn or freeze any Technocratic malcontents or hostile natives. (Forces, Matter)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- Instruments: </span></span></span>Books and Periodicals, Devices and Machines, Energy, Fashion (Atompunk), Formulae and Math, Gadgets and Inventions, Meditation (Brainstorming), Vehicles, Weapons (Primary - Gadgets and Inventions)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Avatar: Agatha doesn't believe she has an Avatar, She wishes she did since the idea of having an psychopompic entity as a muse to assist her in her studies sounds quite </span></span></span>astounding<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">! Fortunately, she has her eternal companion and girlfriend to help her out whenever her research hits a snag. She's not a True Scientist but for some reason she always knows just the right to say. Agatha thinks she'd be lost without her, which is true in more ways than one. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-25T12:11:56-07:00","id":1230079,"title":"","content":"106)<br /> <br /> Eugene Tailor is a friendly man.<br /> <br /> A good listener. A really good one. You have to be, in order to tend the counter in a classy bar where the people like to spend time. The kind of bar where jazz music plays in the background, the lights are dimmed a bit, and where people come to enjoy a bit of nostalgia. The kind that makes you dwell on the past, where the music sets your thoughts in motion.<br /> <br /> Eugene also mixes good cocktails. Really good ones. The kind of cocktails that are not just run-off-the-mill, but something special. The ones you really remember. Oh, he can do the common ones right off the first page of the menu, too. And just as good, but Eugene has a keen eye for what kind of spirits might suit the new guest sitting in front of him. Even if the patron is the kind to try their 'usual', his charm and friendly demeanor does wonders for suggesting people to try new things. And so far, people always were suprised and enthusiastic about his creations afterwards. It is an art to come up with new blends and creations, and Eugene is an artist when it comes to mixology.<br /> <br /> Eugene is also is empathic. Very empathic. He is quick to notice when something is weighting down on somebody's soul. When there is that certain lack of enthusiasm in their eyes. When the body language is humble or shy. Or when they outright spill their sorrows to the bartender. From the people who simply have a problem they really need to solve, to those poor souls that try to drown their sorrows with spirits (which Eugene discourages, and instead tries to make them enjoy his creations with patience and care - even though he seldomly enforces a limit on the amount they try.).<br /> <br /> Eugene is also helpful. Very helpful. His charm, friendlyness and empath allow him to get tongues more loose, to get into a conversation about the ires, bad fortunes and sorrows that occupy some guests. His smile brightens the mood in wonderful ways, his soft voice soothes the nerves, and his advice is not just hollow words, but enthusiastic and well thought-out help to get people to consider their way out of their situation. Steps to solve their problems, all with the care of a saint. And more often than not, the guests, charmed by his liquid bliss, leave the establishment with determination, a big smile, and a jump in their step.<br /> <br /> Eugene gives his advice. Gladly so. The words are well thought-out. The suggestions are logical, and elaborate. They are so reasonable. Like brilliant flashes of enlightenment at times. It is clearly just a horrible world out there that has the customers come back worse, with tales of bad luck, of misfortune and greater ills. Ills that, of course, have Eugene lend his ear once more, soothing the nerves, serving his tasty drinks and suggesting a way out of the new dilemma. Even if the clothes of the customer might get a bit more ragged. Even if the world out there seems to become harsher and harsher to them. Even if, slowly over time, Eugene becomes the only person listening to them. Even if the needlemarks on the arm itch, and the last bundles of money scream for more. But there is also those delicious cocktails. Expensive, but so good. And that warm voice of the bartender...perhaps he has an idea. Just one more idea of how to get out of this mess...<br /> <br /> <br /> Welcome, dear guest. Choose your poison. The final one's always on the house.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-25-2018, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T16:04:09-07:00","id":1232245,"title":"","content":"107) A Verbana Moon Seeker who began her Awakened career in the 90s, by embracing the then-current cutting edge of mass media: the VHS tape. With a little funding by her coven, she would produce direct-to-video specials, devoted to teaching people how to do watchcraft. The videos were hokey and low budget, and the witch herself had a rather awkward screen presence. But her sincerity shone through, as did the practical knowledge she talked about and demonstrated. Obviously, the witchcraft was sanitized - no censor was going to let dancing skyclad in a forest or ritual blood-letting slide - but that merely forced her to get creative. Sometimes the tapes would record actual magical effects. Because of the low quality of the VHS, however, it could easily be passed off as special effects.<br /> <br /> It was slightly embarrassing for the Verbana, but it got modest results. In the time of the New Age revival, young people would snatch up any material purported to give real advice on the mystic arts. So, while many would deny it, quite a few Verbana first cut their teeth on magic from watching this witch's videos.<br /> <br /> Inevitably, the series of videos ended. Given the glut of New Age material on the market, and the relatively low-key videos, the witch got a surprisingly long run out of the gig. Nonetheless, the Technocracy eventually took notice - they themselves were embarrassed it took so long - and members of the Syndicate bought the distributor and dropped the series. Strings were further pulled in other distributors, and the witch experienced a soft blacklist in the VHS market. Disheartened, she put away her cameras and went back to being a solitary witch.<br /> <br /> However, the VHS copies didn't disappear. They were no longer being printed, sure, but those still extent remained in circulation on the second hand market. Others remained locked in the attics, closets, and basements of people throughout the world, waiting patiently. Eventually, sometime in the late 00s, certain &quot;fans&quot; of the videos began talking about them on internet forums. Some simply liked to make fun of cheap, corny videos they dug out of storage. Others, however, had genuine nostalgia for them. Objectively yes, they were corny as hell, but some people had actual feelings for these tapes. Even if they never Awakened in childhood from them, seeing a friendly witch talk about magic to them had been a formative part of their childhoods. Moreover, some of those who only learned about the tapes years after the fact gained a fondness for them after they'd had their fun laughing at them. Moreover, some people actually tried them out, only to find that they would occasionally work. Some - whether old fans or new - even Awakened.<br /> <br /> With the advent of video streaming sites, this small cult following began to post grainy footage pulled from the videos, bit by bit, across dozens of accounts. By sheer chance, the witch herself discovered this. At first she was embarrassed - she HAD been hokey, hadn't she? (Not to mention how she lamented her lost youth). But seeing how many people truly enjoyed the videos made rekindled the magic that had been lost. She started reaching out to fans in the small community, especially those claiming to have really made the lessons work. She dug into the coven's storage, and pulled out huge reels of tape that had been sitting around, gathering dust. She started her own video channel, and posted the high quality original footage. The ones made before the quality was compressed down to VHS standards.<br /> <br /> When she had posted the entire original run, the fans expressed sadness that there would be no more. Deciding that her work wasn't finished, she bought a digital camera, and started a new series of videos. At first what amounted to vlogs where she talked about magic, then actual productions. One crowd-funding campaign later - helped by some Virtual Adept friends, who made sure to keep the Technocratic Union from pulling more chicanery - and the witch had started up her program as a regular show. Years of experience (and a little help from more tech and media savvy friends) made her videos even better; less awkward, more punchy, with better production.<br /> <br /> Many in the Verbana became embarrassed anew...but, secretly, they smile at the resurgence of old passions amid young faces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T17:01:44-07:00","id":1232253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1232245#post1232245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">107) Straight to VHS Verbena</div> </div> </div> </div>I ADORE THIS.<br /> <br /> This is just... I love it. It's perfect.<br /> <br /> The video recordings themselves could be a virtual foundation. Subtle Mind and Entropy effects are layered into the recordings to heighten their effectiveness. Entropy helps the tapes fall into the right hands, and has people watching them in the right mood. Mind has them paying attention, and means that the intended emotional ideas are communicated clearly; comfort and understanding stemming from a humble &quot;good luck&quot; ritual made before each recording.<br /> <br /> This sort of character could make a great NPC in a chronicle. The PCs never actually meet her, but recovering all of the VHS tapes could form an important plot point. Perhaps this witch had possession of something dangerous and important which needs to be found and recovered. Perhaps one of the tapes, by fluke, acts as a Primer, meaning that the Verbena (or Union) desperately want to keep control of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-03T19:01:22-07:00","id":1232274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1232253#post1232253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I ADORE THIS.<br /> <br /> This is just... I love it. It's perfect.<br /> <br /> The video recordings themselves could be a virtual foundation. Subtle Mind and Entropy effects are layered into the recordings to heighten their effectiveness. Entropy helps the tapes fall into the right hands, and has people watching them in the right mood. Mind has them paying attention, and means that the intended emotional ideas are communicated clearly; comfort and understanding stemming from a humble &quot;good luck&quot; ritual made before each recording.<br /> <br /> This sort of character could make a great NPC in a chronicle. The PCs never actually meet her, but recovering all of the VHS tapes could form an important plot point. Perhaps this witch had possession of something dangerous and important which needs to be found and recovered. Perhaps one of the tapes, by fluke, acts as a Primer, meaning that the Verbena (or Union) desperately want to keep control of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It being a Primer is unlikely, as one of the qualifiers for Primers is that they can't be passive experiences, like music or films. They require active effort to comprehend the material. On the other hand, I've toyed with the idea of a Primer that is a film, but requires the viewer to study and analyse the contents of the film - frame by frame in some cases - before they can gain the full effects. Like a Primer created specifically for film buffs.<br /> <br /> Another idea could be that some event occurred during the filming of one episode. It wouldn't even need to have been at the film set; whatever it was just sent out waves of interference on the electromagnetic spectrum. So that, for a few frames of footage, a clue was captured on the film stock. Its presence wasn't recognized until years later, when a mage saw the distortion on their copy of the VHS tape. But because it's VHS, the quality of the footage is too poor to make out what the interference was.<br /> <br /> Only the master copy of the actual film stock would be high quality enough to analyse for clues. And if it's on the last episode made, the witch may not have had the original film returned from the distributor before her show got canned, and it got lost in the confusion. Meaning the PCs have to go track down wherever that master copy is stored or who has it.<br /> <br /> That even could be anything, but would presumably be something affecting a wide area, and noticeable on the electromagnetic spectrum. It would also be quite an old event, to be picked up by that tape. I'm imagining some kind of Technocracy or Virtual Adept experiment, sent out by broadcast. Or maybe a call for help, with information about a person's whereabouts, or the whereabouts of something important they wanted known. The Technocracy might even have scrubbed all other sources of such things after the fact, but missed this witch's tape because she was a relative unknown, and/or because of the delay between filming and release on VHS. There are many ways this could go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 07-03-2018, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-18T06:29:13-07:00","id":1236388,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">&quot;The wavelength gently grows,</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">Coercive notions re-evolve,</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">A universe is trapped inside a tear,</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">It resonates the core,</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">Creates unnatural laws,</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">Replaces love and happiness with fear&quot;<br /> -Muse, &quot;MK Ultra&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> 108) Formerly a soldier in the US military, this Ecstasy Cultist volunteered for a secret research project. They told him he could serve his country by putting his mind on the line. So when they pumped psychedelics into his veins and strapped him to a chair with flickering lights on his eyes, he thought he could take it. He'd been waterboarded as part of training, so he thought he could handle anything. The government lab, for their part, wanted to see if they could foster psychic powers.<br /> <br /> They succeeded. Pity they and the rest of the lab didn't survive long enough to appreciate it.<br /> <br /> The explosive Awakening left him stranded in a crater that used to be a military base. After wandering back to civilization, he discovered that the destruction had been covered up, with official reports blaming a gas leak with &quot;No Survivors&quot;. After a few close calls from shadowy assailants and men in black suits, he realized that someone knew about him. He abandoned his life, eventually falling in with the Cult of Ecstasy.<br /> <br /> He studies psychic powers now, using combinations of drugs, sensory deprivation, and sensory overload, as well as various mental exercises, thought forms, and headgear cribbed from the notes of Etherites he knows, to channel mental ability.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the mental trauma - combined with being hunted and lingering questions about that secret research project - has also done a number on his psyche. He's more than a little paranoid, and puts great stock in conspiracy theories. Now of course, in the World of Darkness, many conspiracy theories are true. But others aren't, or aren't quite as many know them. He's lucid enough to know that, but can't rule out any theory for sure, no matter how outlandish. What if the Technocratic Union is simply a front for Lizard People? What if those Lizard People are simply fronts for an even more esoteric set of hidden masters? He does know not to trust the government, because they took advantage of his patriotism and got him into this mess with their secret project. He wants to know who was behind that research, and who they are really working for.<br /> <br /> He'll astral project across the planetary mindscape, if it means finding answers. He'll also work to decode the riddles and signs hidden everywhere. It's not like the Technocracy is a stranger to implanting memetic effects into media and the like. Why can't the REAL conspiracy do the same?<br /> <br /> Currently, he spends a great deal of time on message boards, and selling brain health products on the side. Since he's a military vet, he's also not above making money by teaching other mages and/or their consors how to fight. The Traditions need to be ready to fight the real war, now that the distraction war against the Technocracy is on hold. Of course, the Traditions are also almost certainly pawns in someone's game. He'll stay on the inside, in order to get a better chance to see who or what they are.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 07-18-2018, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T21:22:28-07:00","id":1237403,"title":"","content":"109) A flamboyant and narcissistic stage magician, inducted into the Cult of Ecstasy by The Man in the Mirror.<br /> <br /> Centuries ago, a master illusionist belonging to what then was known as the Seers of Chronos, the Man in the Mirror used his great powers to retreat into a mirror pocket dimension, in order to evade danger. Unfortunately for him, the Scourge twisted his magick, trapping him in his mirror refuge. He could survive indefinitely in his prison and act through reflections to a limited capacity, but could not leave. (Or perhaps he CAN leave, but some persistent threat keeps him holed up. He's not terribly forthcoming about his situation). So there he remained, for hundreds of years.<br /> <br /> That is, until a vain fool found a hand mirror in an antique store, buying it for a song.<br /> <br /> As it happened, the ornate mirror was the old master's Talisman. When the young narcissist - a cocksure individual of a gender-fluid persuasion - managed to make the item's magick work, it intrigued the old master, and the Man in the Mirror appeared in the reflection. Unaccustomed to seeing someone else's face staring back at them, the Fool adapted surprisingly quickly. When the Man in the Mirror offered to teach them True Magick, they feigned aloofness, but secretly longed for such power. So, after much posturing, passive aggressive hostilities, and exasperation, the Fool became the Man in the Mirror's apprentice. Not too long after, they Awakened fully, allowing them to grasp subtleties of illusion, prophecy, and apportation, in addition to the finer points of mundane stage magic and the Art of Desire.<br /> <br /> The Ecstasy Cultist travels the world, performing stunning displays for the benefit of audiences. Off the stage, though, the narcissist acts as the agent of their Mentor, who uses the modern fool to enact broader schemes. Seducing people here, whispering magically charged ideas into ears there, and tracking down mystic artifacts along the way. If they find useful magical items or research, they either use it themselves, or trade them off to other mages (the Man in the Mirror, despite his exile, seems to remain fully in contact with quite a few old mages, who are interested in swapping such things for favors). It's only recently, though, that the fool has shrugged off their incurious habit, and begun to wonder what the Old Man is playing at. If any of the tasks directly or indirectly take them closer to freeing him, the Man in the Mirror doesn't share the logic. He brushes off the subject, even, as if his egress is less important to some other, more pressing tasks. Sooner or later, if the Fool is going to get out from under the thumb of their Mentor and pursue their own interests, they're going to need to figure out what the Old Man wants.<br /> <br /> For now, though, the young magician finds their current arrangement comfortable, profitable, and personally gratifying. They always did love strutting around like a peacock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T00:47:27-07:00","id":1237909,"title":"","content":"&quot;I've got a secret I've been hiding under my skin<br /> My heart is human, my blood is boiling, my brain IBM<br /> So if you see me acting strangely, don't be surprised<br /> I'm just a man who needed someone and somewhere to hide<br /> To keep me alive, just keep me alive<br /> Somewhere to hide to keep me alive&quot;<br /> <br /> -Styx, &quot;<a href=\"https://youtu.be/14LAAU8H4Rc\" target=\"_blank\">Mr. Roboto</a>&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> 110) Agent Kilroy (an assigned designation he now considers bleakly ironic) was an Iteration X Bio-Mechanic who, in contrast to many of his Methodology peers, eschewed cybernetic augmentation for himself to the most part. Save for some brain implants, taken as a matter of workplace efficiency, and then only with great reluctance. In the end, though, that implant ended up saving his life. By chance, he discovered one of his high-ranking Iteration X superiors speaking with a mysterious individual - as Kilroy came to understand, they were two individuals of different factions in a united organization that was attempting to infiltrate the Technocratic Union (later, Kilroy's contact within the Void Engineers begrudgingly revealed who they were: Threat Null). Near the end of the conversation, Kilroy discovered that these individuals worked directly for Control - the lost super AI that held the Convention in thrall before the Dimensional Anomaly - and that it wanted to see the whole Union dominated, and in totality. When Agent Kilroy tried to escape, he made too much noise, and was found. They tried to silence him, but the tussle resulted in an explosion that wrecked the lab. The two infiltrators departed, citing an &quot;industrial accident&quot;, and wrote off the eavesdropper for dead.<br /> <br /> Except Kilroy survived. He lost all fours limbs and much of the rest of his anatomy, but Void Engineer doctors weren't slouches, and he was saved.<br /> <br /> Not that he was out of danger, though. When he came to, he heard doctors arguing with that same Iteration X superior, who rushed over as soon as it became clear Kilroy was alive. &quot;I demand to see Agent Kilroy, immediately&quot;, the infiltrator said. Luckily, the doctor refused entry, citing the patient's need to recover. The Iteration X superior departed, but Kilroy knew the man would simply return as soon as he could and...eliminate Kilroy as a threat. The Bio-Mechanic was under no illusions that he'd be killed, or worse: subsumed into whatever domination Control would have for him. Knowing he'd suffer either physical or ego death, Kilroy desperately worked to formulate a plan of escape. That's when he realized that a &quot;Mr. Roboto&quot; had been left by his side, to service his needs.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The RURX series robots were first developed by Japanese Technocrats in the 80s, to provide cheaper human-like labor around labs. Because of their national origin, they were informally dubbed &quot;Mr. Roboto&quot;, and the name stuck ever since. They aren't combat models or specialized machines, but rather generic drone bots of humanoid shape, designed for all-purpose work, and with options for modular modification. They are relatively cheap to produce, by Technocracy standards, so the Union often keeps a few dozen units on hand at any given location. Moreover, they look, to the laymen, like a lean person in a robot costume; this is by design, as it cuts down on &quot;Paradox Interference&quot;, rendering them usable even in labs or Constructs that haven't been &quot;Paradox Shielded&quot;. For this reason, the Union will often employ them to fill out ranks in personnel, or to do labor in areas or situations too sensitive for most lower-level Extraordinary Citizens (who may not be cleared for secret projects or &quot;high Science&quot; locations). And because they are generic and easily repaired, many used models get shuffled around from Construct to Construct as needed or convenient.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, Roboto class robots are even lost track of - many discarded, salvaged, or stolen during the waning years of the Pogrom - and end up in the hands of non-Union personnel. Many Virtual Adepts hack them into leaving bases on their own, while Etherites salvage their parts to act as lab assistants (after installing their own tech). Even non-mages can be found with them; many lay in the hands of Glass Walker werewolves, or populating the havens and warrens of Nosferatu or True Brujah technologists (who go to great lengths to achieve the mundane Hypertech Ability sufficient to maintain them). Others can be found wandering urban environments, providing aid to random people as part of their programmed need to be of service. Most such units get picked up on the Union's radar eventually, but others are hidden (by owners who know enough to not advertise what they have) or simply fall through the cracks. So Roboto class robots winding up &quot;out in the wild&quot; is not unheard of.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Working quickly, Kilroy ordered the Roboto to bring in automated manufacturing equipment. Once in place, he hacked them using his brain implant, using their flexible armatures to take the Roboto apart, so its chasis could be used for his own purposes. Then, he used the arms to lift him into position, though the movements caused his injured body great pain. After much tedious work and discomfort, he accomplished his rushed, insane plan: graft parts from the Roboto onto himself, until he used its robot limbs and frame as a new cyborg body. He finished by retrofitting the head casing and face plate into a concealing mask. So that, when his new limbs propelled him from the sick bay room, he looked for all casual examination like a Mr. Roboto.<br /> <br /> Then he boarded the next cargo vessel back to Earth (forging digital records of a transfer manifest), with no one knowing where he'd gone.<br /> <br /> Kilroy - or &quot;Mr. Roboto&quot; as he's called - remains in his disguise, even now. Knowing the amount of pull his enemies possess, he cannot risk being up and about with his own face on display. Any electronic surveillance would pick up his true visage on facial recognition software. So, to protect himself from capture, he maintains the Roboto facade, acting variably as a committed cosplayer or a simple automaton, though he lets slip when necessary that he's more than he appears to be. He forges contacts within the Union - especially among Void Engineers - in his crusade to root out Threat Null infiltrators. He can even sometimes walk about low-security Union Constructs - blending in with other Roboto units - though obviously not without risk and precaution. He's developed Rotes for disguising his electronic and mechanical signature, so he appears like a regular robot, instead of a cyborg.<br /> <br /> As such, the Union at large is aware only of a rogue Roboto unit, that may be possessed of some advanced AI or be under someone's remote control. They aren't sure whether &quot;it&quot; is a superstitionist tool, a rogue bot, or the agent of some Union power player with their own agenda. Given how byzantine and cold war-esque Union politics can be, no one is willing to rule out the latter. Few, if any, seriously consider that someone would actually make their cyborg body look like known Union hardware. The Roboto has caused minimal disruption; &quot;it&quot; has even seemingly worked to expose corruption among Union personnel. Leading some to question whether it might be a tool by Special Agent John Courage. In any case, the matter is seen as being of limited importance for the moment, though one to be investigated where practical.<br /> <br /> Kilroy himself remains loyal to the Union's cause, at least in principle. He has, however, also become disillusioned about the utopian ideal ascribed to technology. He's seen Control, and what can happen if man becomes a slave to tech, rather than the other way around. For now, his survival depends on obscuring his true identity and nature. At least until he can provide proof of Threat Null's presence in the upper ranks. On that day, when the parasites on the Union's insides are unmasked, will he be free to remove his own mask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 07-23-2018, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T07:11:00-07:00","id":1240026,"title":"","content":"111) A Templar knight trained in the old arts of creating holy relics and reliquaries. As a young man, he encountered one such object in an abandoned church in Mexico. Upon touching it, he received a divine vision of Saint Dunstan, patron saint of smiths. Awakened and inspired, he set out to praise God through artistry, and to bring lost relics back to the people, where they could do the most good.<br /> <br /> A craftsman as well as a priest and warrior, he forges and shapes art objects that will attempt to capture divine aspects into material forms. The heyday of the reliquaries has largely passed, but he believes it can return again, to inspire the common people towards piety and awe. And of course, as a member of the Knights Templar, he hopes to eventually create relics potent enough to effect miraculous change (read: Wonders). He knows, however, that the greatest of all relics are literally reliquaries: items that house body parts or treasured items belonging to saints. For this reason, therefore, he is prepared to play the part of graverobber, digging up the graves of latter-day saints and taking samples to empowered his work. These he takes with the utmost respect, to atone for the transgression made for the greater good.<br /> <br /> He has also not forgotten his origins. His Awakening happened as a direct result of finding a lost and forgotten holy artifact. The world is full of such things - the reliquaries of many saints having been misplaced, stolen, discarded, and hidden over many centuries. These items can be put to use, whether it be by presenting them to the masses, by privately studying them to improve his own work, or to use directly against the forces of evil (when the items have power of their own, as Wonders or objects of True Faith). He works closely, therefore, with detectives, antiquarians, and treasure hunters. One never knows when a significant item sits, unused, in an attic or crawl space or abandoned warehouse. Where necessary, he will abscond with an item if others would exploit or squander it, or when the object is too dangerous to be left in unknowing hands. Otherwise, though, he's okay allowing &quot;proper parties&quot; (like the Catholic Church, museums, or even the Celestial Chorus or Society of Leopold) to hang on to relics. To everything there is a season, and a proper place for every tool of the divine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 07-30-2018, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T20:20:42-07:00","id":1248287,"title":"","content":"112) A magical gold digger, this Orphan user of Chaos Magick learned every trick in her magical arsenal by seducing it out of a string of mage lovers.<br /> <br /> She began as a bright but shallow young woman. Ever since puberty, she was accustomed to using her sex appeal to get what she wanted. As such, she coasted through her schooling up to year 2 of university, by ingratiating herself with people more learned and diligent than herself. It's not that she didn't have the intelligence to make her own way; she just considered applying herself to be a waste of effort, when her natural charm could get her through. While at university, though, she hooked up with a guy who turned out to be a Verbana witch. When she discovered his power, she plied him with seduction until he taught her a few magical tricks. Restless by nature and unfocused by habit, she eventually dumped him, finding his more advanced lessons and lectures about nature spirits and the Wyck to be too much effort.<br /> <br /> By this point, of course, Magick had sunk its claws into her, and she craved more. So she sought out other magical practitioners, creating a cycle of romance, sex, taking knowledge on offer, and finally abandonment. Some of her partners (she long ago learned not to discriminate based on gender, to get what she wanted) were mere Sorcerers - hedge wizards and cunning folk - while others were outright charlatans. She almost came under the fangs of a vampiric blood sorcerer once, as well, though she was experienced enough with people to read when the moment was going somewhere she didn't want, and she bounced. And some, naturally, were True Mages. Somewhere along the line, she Awakened herself. Throughout her &quot;education&quot;, she picked up bits and pieces of occult lore, Rotes, and types of Instruments to use. She became a perennial Jill of all trades, master of none. Her teacher-lovers tended to be on the inexperienced side - more established magicians tended to be wise to her advances and intent. Younger or inexperienced mages, meanwhile, tended to be easier to seduce, and moreover were proud enough of their meager studies that they seemed to actively WANT someone to regurgitate knowledge to, as if they were the learner turned master.<br /> <br /> All easy rides must come to an end. She never really learned restraint; she only avoided critical social failure due to her promiscuity during high school because she graduated, and moved to a college where no one knew her. Inevitably, jumping from lover to lover, sponging magic off the impressionable and leaving them high and dry when she grew bored, caught up with her. Mages can be insular, but they do, on occasion, exchange notes. Word gets around, perhaps all the easier because of the smaller community of magical practitioners. Masters and compatriots started warning young mages and sorcerers about her, and her reputation soon preceded her. Suddenly, no one was interested in taking her up on any offers or reciprocating her advances.<br /> <br /> Which means now her preferred - heck, ONLY - method of gaining arcane knowledge was cut off. Moreover, she left quite a few broken hearts and wounded prides in her wake, which earned her cold shoulders everywhere the magically inclined congregated. For the first time in her life, using her natural talent to coast through life no longer worked, and indeed had landed her in a worse situation than when she started. Nor did she have much more than a vague Paradigm of her own. She just accepted that the tricks and Rotes she was taught worked; her understanding had a distinct lack of Theory. This would not do.<br /> <br /> So, it was time to rectify that deficiency. Which meant actually applying herself. At the moment, she's got half-remembered lectures and a host of New Age books on the occult to work from. It's frustrating, going back to square one and learning the basics. Trawling through material from the Golden Dawn to the Golden Bough, and everything in between she can get her hands on. Nonetheless, she has that itch. The itch that all magical practitioners of magic feel. The desire to learn and amass power, that motivates above and beyond other concerns. That drive, at least, is profoundly her own, not borrowed, begged, or stolen.<br /> <br /> Now, if only she could dodge the machinations of ex-lovers who were particularly broken up about their break ups. Hell hath no fury like a magus scorned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 08-20-2018, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T13:35:10-07:00","id":1248887,"title":"","content":"113) The Fatal Addiction<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;The blood, it always comes back to the blood. &quot;This is my blood, which is poured out for you.&quot; It is the blood which gives us life, and it is <i>vitae</i> which leads the way to eternal life. I hold the holy grail, the alpha and omega, and I am dance among immortals, I move with the heavens and...&quot; <i>he takes a deep sip from his cup</i> &quot;I will uncover its secrets.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Imagine discovering the secrets of the universe while sipping from a cold, dead arm. Imagine devouring a star. The sweet and heady taste of vitae is not to be underestimated; it is my salvation and my curse. I know so much, but I depend on a self-centered corpse to survive. In time I will control him, but for now I am vulnerable... my jugular is exposed.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Oliver was lured into the service of a Tremere Apprentice while studying Classics at Oxford University. Upon entering ghouldom, he began to understand the world in ways he hadn't before. Blood magic, Thaumaturgy, were will made manifest, controlling the world through the blood. His first experiments in blood magick were dangerous, hurting his body, burning through his limited supplies of human blood, but in the end he fully Awakened, knowing himself and the power held within his blood.<br /> <br /> Oliver studied for years, learning as much as he could about Thaumaturgy simply by being useful. Assisting in every experiment, befriending every Apprentice, becoming integral to the Chantry's nightly activities. Eventually he realized that this place was a chain wrapped around his neck, as suffocating and limiting as the blood bond itself. Possessed by dark intent, Oliver received blood from his &quot;master&quot; one last time before torching the chantry while his master and the others slept. It took a phenomenal amount of willpower to resist the urge to save his master, but his tears were thin and pale, while the blood within him was everlasting, strong. They burnt up like kindling, and Oliver escaped with various tomes and tools, ready to experiment further.<br /> <br /> Arriving at the doorstep of the only Tremere within the domain who didn't reside within the Chantry, he spun a tale of hunter arsonists, weeping for his master. He offered his services to this lone survivor, safe in the knowledge that any thought that might betray him was now protected by his magick, a power that far surpassed any sanguine sorcery...<br /> <br /> Magick:<br /> <br /> Paradigm: All power comes from the blood; when we understand that, we turn the keys to reality<br /> <br /> Practise: High Ritual, Blood Magick<br /> <br /> Instruments: Blood, Cups and Vessels, Circles and Designs, Numerology, Ordeals and Sacrifices, Gems and Stones, Meat and Remains<br /> <br /> Oliver performs magick using his blood; to him, the vitae within him, and even his own human blood, is the ultimate focus for Will. He uses other tools to heighten the power of his magick, from the blood and remains of animals, to specialized vessels and ritual designs, but everything comes back to blood.<br /> <br /> Since Oliver has Path of Blood 1 he is able to identify important elements in any blood he touches, smells or tastes using his Willpower alone. This is a useful tool upon which his magick is built.<br /> <br /> Roleplay:<br /> <br /> Nothing is more important than knowledge and magickal growth. Any esoteric tome might hold the next key in your path to apotheosis, so inquire. You come across as a useful lackey, a helpful assistant, and you hide your sharp genius. Instead you present a level of intelligence which reflects and complements those around you; you talk like a smart student who is aptly understanding the things their teacher explains, making interesting suggestions in response. In reality you are far superior in might to your domitor, but the less he knows about that the better.<br /> <br /> You take great pains to hide your thoughts and aura using Mind and Spirit; to you the risk of being discovered is intolerable. You always have contingencies in mind; for example you have committed a few kindred contacts of your domitor to memory on the off chance that you ever need a new domitor.<br /> <br /> You are addicted to vitae, but have moved beyond personal attachments to the vampire feeding you. Some spiritual resilience (an element of your Avatar perhaps?) has pushed you beyond being a simpering obedient ghoul. Do not neglect your fierce and burning addiction however; you are more dependent than any alcoholic or drug user could ever be, since drinking vitae has become an addiction on many levels. Your body needs it to remain strong, healthy and young. Your Avatar craves it, for reasons which are unclear to you. Emotionally you need to taste that bliss which melts away stress and fear.<br /> <br /> Mechanics:<br /> <br /> - Arete 3, Mind 1, Life 1, Prime 1, Spirit 1, Forces 2<br /> <br /> - You are a Ghoul, and experience all of the typical benefits and drawbacks as explained in V20. These include, but are not limited to, a pool of vitae (up to 10 points) which can heal damage, buff your physical attributes and fuel Disciplines, a dot of Potence, no aging, the ability to soak lethal damage with Stamina, the risk of Frenzy, an addiction to blood and a pale aura (somewhere between that of a human and that of a Vampire).<br /> <br /> - Your Avatar itself has an addiction to Vitae which has been inherited from a past life. This is why becoming a Ghoul triggered an Awakening; the previous owner of the Avatar dabbled in blood magick. You are Unbondable but suffer a severe addiction.<br /> <br /> - Your Disciplines are Potence 1 (a simple one dot bonus to Strength; this can also be activated with a point of Vitae to give one automatic success on all Strength rolls for a turn) and Thaumaturgy 1, with Path of Blood 1. Path of Blood 1 is a simple power which allows you to determine supernatural and natural qualities of blood with your senses. Many of the advantages of this power are covered by Life 1, but some aren't. For example you could recognize if Vitae is Tremere or &quot;something other than Tremere&quot;, and you could recognize if some blood was from a supernatural source (a Mage, a Demon, a Werewolf). Identifying blood as something specific (this is Brujah/Tremere/Ventrue blood, this is potent/weak blood, this is the blood of a powerful Werewolf) relies on experience. You also know at least one level 1 Thaumaturgy ritual, likely one that is useful to your Domitor, such as Communicate with Domitor (allows telepathic communion with your Domitor, and them only) or Purity of Blood (purges supernatural and natural corruption, from infection to poisons, from blood).<br /> <br /> - Your magick tends to be largely internal, and typically coincidental (reading surface thoughts in those around you, seeing magickal ebbs and flows), but your &quot;showier&quot; effects are largely Vulgar. Nothing will sell a person spitting out blood which turns into sanguine flames as coincidental, at least in most settings.<br /> <br /> - Quintessence is the energy held within vitae, simply removed from its physical &quot;host&quot;. Vitae simply acts as a stable and natural container for energy, one which can last for 1000s of years. Paradox is the burn or mental instability which results from improperly manipulating your own blood, and the &quot;blood-stained strings of natural order&quot;. Of course when you botch an attempt to transform your body into something greater you begin to see things that aren't really there; people see all sorts of crazy things when they've lost a lot of blood.<br /> <br /> Future Developments:<br /> <br /> - If vitae is simply blood enriched with Quintessence, then using Prime and Life to extract &quot;vitae&quot; from humans the way Vampires do should be a cinch. And by the same logic, fusing blood and Quintessence to make Vitae should be simple. Oliver may eventually reach a point where he becomes like a Vampire himself, forging his own unstable immortality out of a predatory lifestyle, fusing his magickal power with stolen blood to create a heady elixir which will keep him immortal forever... or at least until he misses a step.<br /> <br /> - Eventually Oliver will discover the similarities between himself and the first Tremere. Will he see the Embrace as the apotheosis of his mystical path, or as a betrayal of magick and of human nature? Are kindred to be emulated, or parasitized off of?<br /> <br /> - How will Oliver integrate into the Order of Hermes? Will his nature be discovered?<br /> <br /> - What could Oliver achieve with an object like the Cup of Vaddhartha (a cup which holds the blood of Ventru, one of the third generation, which Ventru's child Vaddhartha used to embrace many other Ventrue of the fourth generation), or a similar relic? Are there powers within his grasp that no other mage could conquer, or is he a deluded addict?<br /> <br /> - Will his addiction ever get in the way of his development a Mage, or has he successfully married the two? Will he be able to live as a Mage whilst also fulfilling his duties as a Ghoul? Will he eventually evolve beyond his Domitor and destroy or abandon him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-25-2018, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-25T16:39:27-07:00","id":1248894,"title":"","content":"Example Effects (CW for self harm and blood, as you can imagine):<br /> <br /> - Realizing that his aura and spiritual scent are going to attract negative attention among Lupines (both as a Mage and a Ghoul), Oliver decides a disguise is in order. He washes himself carefully, and applies various perfumes. Once this purification is complete he creates stigmata in each palm and bleeds into a bowl, taking a point of bashing damage to fuel the effect. He heals this damage by spending some of his precious vitae.<br /> <br /> With the focus in place he rolls his Arete for a Spirit 1 effect to alter how his aura is perceived. This change is coincidental since nothing is happening from the viewpoint of a bystander outside of some bizarre and unhealthy activity. 3 dice, difficulty 3 (Level 1 effect + 3 for Coincidental - 1 from the damage inflicted onto his body). This results in his aura becoming less pale, similar to that of a normal human.<br /> <br /> - Oliver decides that someone needs to die. Flicking open his lighter and biting his tongue hard, he exhales a mist of blood into the flame and then breathes in rapidly. Turning to face his foe(s), he breathes out a great plume of blood red flames.<br /> <br /> This is naturally vulgar (hopefully without witnesses), and is using a Forces 2 effect since there is no transmutation or creation. The damage inflicted to his body could reduce the difficulty, depending on whether biting his tongue causes damage. 3 dice, difficulty 6 without modifiers.<br /> <br /> - Oliver jolts awake when he hears a bell ringing. Realizing that some kind of spirit is disturbing his master's haven (the bell is charmed with static magic to ring is a spirit passes nearby), he quickly grabs a shard of glass from a broken mirror and pricks both of his eyelids. Pointing the shard over his shoulder, as the blood trickles down it, he looks around the room searching for any ghosts (or other spirits).<br /> <br /> Standard Spirit 1 effect to see nearby spirits, and any influence they are exerting.<br /> <br /> - Inspired by the act of Diablerie, Oliver hopes to strengthen himself with a kindred sacrifice. With his sacrifice laying staked on an altar, he prepares a ritual circle with white ash around the altar, drawing hermetic runes and lighting wax candles. Adorning white robes he stigmatizes his hands and feet, and does the same to his sacrifice. He draws designs on the staked vampire in his own blood, and runes on his white robe in the sacrifice's blood. He continues by dousing his sacrifice in purified oil, and eventually setting him alight with one of the candles.<br /> <br /> What Spheres are needed here depends on exactly what the player thinks this &quot;diablerie&quot; will result in. A boost to permanent Willpower, a full replenishment of the wheel with Quintessence, a permanent increase in an Attribute... I'd assume that these sorts of effects require level 3 and 4 spheres generally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T04:46:15-07:00","id":1248938,"title":"","content":"nice. was thinking something along the lines of 'fake' other supernaturals myself, but nothing like this neat bloodmage. Great job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T05:54:29-07:00","id":1248942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1248938#post1248938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nice. was thinking something along the lines of 'fake' other supernaturals myself, but nothing like this neat bloodmage. Great job.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanted to be a &quot;fake vampire&quot;, then you could get the upperhand of your domitor once you're powerful and then use the Flatline ritual (it's level 1, very doable) to get rid of your vital signs. Have your domitor fight for you to be allowed &quot;the embrace&quot; and then arrive at Elysium as a fledgeling, with no heartbeat etc. thanks to Flatline (a Life effect could also do this of course).<br /> <br /> Now you're a member of Vampiric society who is secretly an Awakened Mage. Enjoy the tightrope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T08:36:56-07:00","id":1248961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1248942#post1248942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you wanted to be a &quot;fake vampire&quot;, then you could get the upperhand of your domitor once you're powerful and then use the Flatline ritual (it's level 1, very doable) to get rid of your vital signs. Have your domitor fight for you to be allowed &quot;the embrace&quot; and then arrive at Elysium as a fledgeling, with no heartbeat etc. thanks to Flatline (a Life effect could also do this of course).<br /> <br /> Now you're a member of Vampiric society who is secretly an Awakened Mage. Enjoy the tightrope.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> man, you have thought about it. Maybe also get fangs and vitae pool with bio-grafts?<br /> I was thinking more of a werewolves and ghosts. First is doable with high level fetish/wonder tattoo, arcane and spirit magic, the second is just projection + aura modification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T12:34:10-07:00","id":1248995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1248961#post1248961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> man, you have thought about it. Maybe also get fangs and vitae pool with bio-grafts?<br /> I was thinking more of a werewolves and ghosts. First is doable with high level fetish/wonder tattoo, arcane and spirit magic, the second is just projection + aura modification.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Life effect, using Vitae as a perfect focus, could grow you some fangs. Then again some young Kindred in modern times, especially those of higher generation (12+) have no fangs at all. As for the vitae pool, Ghouls get that automatically. Your vessels and heart and tissue fluid hold the vitae, much the same as the storage in a Vampire. The most likely way you'd get caught out is being cut in some way; Kindred don't bleed the way humans do, and you can't cast an effect reflexively to stop a spurt of blood.<br /> <br /> With Werewolves... to imitate one in terms of perception you'd just need to use Spirit to change your Aura. To pass as one to other Garou you'd probably need more successes since they have specialized gifts for the purpose of identifying Gaians in some cases. To imitate all their abilities you'd need a lot of Spirit/Prime/Life and the Paradox would destroy you quite quickly. Much easier to imitate Kinfolk I think... and more believable, since Kinfolk *can* be Mages regardless.<br /> <br /> That would be a clever way to imitate a ghost, agreed. Entropy + Spirit combined with Mind could give you astral projection with wraith-like qualities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T15:53:55-07:00","id":1249025,"title":"","content":"114) The Abomination<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;When we awaken, taking that first breath and opening our eyes, we inherit something special. A fragment of Creation, of God, of the Universe. It isn't always very powerful, most don't come with a grand destiny, but it's the greatest mentor you'll ever have. A force pushing you towards enlightenment and apotheosis. A warmth that keeps you company when all seems lost. It breaks my heart though... some magi inherit a poison, a darkness, a corruption. There is no crueler jest, and nothing makes me question my faith more. Innocent and weak, they embrace this new power and are lost before they have any chance whatsoever. Pray for them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Nothing pisses me off more than listening to ecstatic types talking about their awakening. How they found it at the peak of a guitar solo, or when they first got laid, or the first time they danced in front of a crowd... how special and intimate and scary it was. They can't even begin to understand &quot;Scary&quot;. Finding out that your new &quot;friend&quot; is a demon gnawing at the very core of your soul is scary. Jesus wept...&quot;</b><br /> <br /> When Addison's awakening began, the situation was already far from pleasant. Wracked with chronic painful illness and a bitter seething anger, an idea resonated in his head. &quot;Life really is shit.&quot; And that idea stuck...<br /> <br /> Opening his eyes for the first time, properly, his view became more and more pessimistic. Look at these people. How vapid and selfish they are. Isn't it a mercy that within 60 years most of them will be dead? It was only an abnormal force of will that stopped him from falling prey to his own Avatar (as most widderslainte do), that stopped him from becoming a Nephandus. Resisting descension came with a price; Addison is wracked and haunted by his own Avatar, and finds it opposing his growth and ascension at every turn. Practising magick is a painful and dangerous business for him, and he knows that he walks a dangerous tightrope. His avatar attracts all sorts of unsavoury spirits, and eventually he might just slip...<br /> <br /> Magick:<br /> <br /> Paradigm: Creation is deeply flawed, and we're on a One Way Trip to Oblivion, but I'm taking the devil <i>with </i>me! Addison may have a dark paradigm, but he entirely blames the Nephandi as a collective for his situation, rather than reality itself. Whoever fell and created this cursed mess of a soul is to blame, and he can use his curse to put that right.<br /> <br /> Practise: Gutter Magick, Maleficia; Addison's magick is cruel, but this cruelty is generally targeted at those who deserve it, or at the environment and animals. When all else fails the cruelty may be targeted at Addison; the only thing Addison really shares with his Avatar is a negative view of himself, so such a focus can act as a rare case of them working in harmony.<br /> <br /> Instruments: Ordeals and Exertions, Runes and Symbols, Blood and Fluids, Meat and Remains, Weapons, Animalism, Social Domination<br /> <br /> Addison applies his effects through a variety of stereotypically dark means. He might attack someone with a swarm of insects or vermin, command fate to curse someone by consuming a sacrificial animal or call upon the aid of a bane.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying:<br /> <br /> What matters to you is destroying Nephandi and their pawns. You are skeptical of those around you, and skeptical of yourself. You struggle to open up to people or trust them, and you resent other Mages for having a special connection with the universe. You hold no hope for a cure, and have no real faith in a higher power; you have faith in your own resolve and grit.<br /> <br /> If you were to learn to trust another person, you'd have an unconventional friendship. The greatest intimacy you're currently capable of is trusting another person to watch over you and do what needs to be done if you lose your footing.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Promise me that if I go off the rails, you'll try to capture me rather than kill me. I don't want some poor kid to inherit this mess.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Mechanics:<br /> <br /> - Arete 3, Entropy 2, Spirit 1, Life 1, Forces 2<br /> <br /> - Advantages (M20) or Powers (Fomori: Freak Legion) to reflect the limited upsides of your body being warped into something monstrous. Lethal vomiting, a hardened body, warped teeth and fingernails... These may end up being mechanically very powerful (with the right combination of Powers a character can be incredibly tanky), however the social and mechanical downsides of being a widderslainte are huge; many important Arete rolls will be +1 difficulty due to the Avatar opposing the action, and Seekings will be nearly impossible without extreme preparation and outside help. On top of all of that, you look incredibly evil and dangerous at a glance...<br /> <br /> - Flaws which reflect all of the problems that arise from his condition. You are monstrous at a glance and suffer from chronic pain, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-26-2018, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T00:39:46-07:00","id":1249075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1248995#post1248995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Life effect, using Vitae as a perfect focus, could grow you some fangs. Then again some young Kindred in modern times, especially those of higher generation (12+) have no fangs at all. As for the vitae pool, Ghouls get that automatically. Your vessels and heart and tissue fluid hold the vitae, much the same as the storage in a Vampire. The most likely way you'd get caught out is being cut in some way; Kindred don't bleed the way humans do, and you can't cast an effect reflexively to stop a spurt of blood.<br /> <br /> With Werewolves... to imitate one in terms of perception you'd just need to use Spirit to change your Aura. To pass as one to other Garou you'd probably need more successes since they have specialized gifts for the purpose of identifying Gaians in some cases. To imitate all their abilities you'd need a lot of Spirit/Prime/Life and the Paradox would destroy you quite quickly. Much easier to imitate Kinfolk I think... and more believable, since Kinfolk *can* be Mages regardless.<br /> <br /> That would be a clever way to imitate a ghost, agreed. Entropy + Spirit combined with Mind could give you astral projection with wraith-like qualities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are correct, but I meant non-ghoul 'vampire' with starting character abilities. So you graft fangs with additional effects if needed (retractable, narcotic saliva, etc.) and simulate vitae pool with biological pariapt that can refill from human blood. Will need to take LIfe+Prime+Mind for beginning spheres.<br /> <br /> For a werewolf - level 5 tattoo wonder with powerful totem to imitate shapeshifting and gauntlet breach, spirit+mind to mask aura and talk your way through, maybe predator gland biograft to imitate smell and Arcane to raise difficulty of investigation and detection gifts. Of course it won't stand to <i>really </i>detailed scrutiny, but I can see some powerful spirit having goals that would require such masquarade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T07:50:12-07:00","id":1249135,"title":"","content":"[This one is inspired by fairy tales in general, but more specifically by works like the anime <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Tutu\" target=\"_blank\">Princess Tutu</a>, and the upcoming game <a href=\"https://youtu.be/iOzW1INWIb0\" target=\"_blank\">The Liar Princess and the Blind Prince</a>.]<br /> <br /> <br /> 115) In the Renaissance, Little Mouse was just what it sounds like: a mouse. Until, however, a beautiful prince showed her kindness, and Little Mouse fell in love with him. Because in those days, sometimes wild animals were not only intelligent and aware, but could be moved to human passions. Desiring to just be with the prince, Little Mouse sought out a fairy of the forest. It was an epic quest, by mouse standards, since she had to travel all the way from the prince's castle to the deep forest. Little Mouse came to emulate the courtesans and nobles of the royal court, and wielded a sewing needle to defend herself from threats.<br /> <br /> Impressed by her bravery, the fairy of the forest granted Little Mouse a boon, and changed the rodent into a girl. The fairy taught Little Mouse how to speak and employ witchcraft, and transformed the mouse's sewing needle into a fine human rapier, called Shirt Piercer. But the fairy also gave Little Mouse a weakness and a geas, as was common in fairy enchantments. The weakness: the old fear of cats could not be overcome; Little Mouse was as powerless in the face of felines as she ever was as a rodent. The Geas: Little Mouse would only ever have one chance to confess her love to the prince, and she must reveal her true nature when she does so. If the prince rejects her feelings, Little Mouse will return to being a mouse, forevermore. She would only have one opportunity to get him to love her. With determination, Little Mouse returned to the prince's castle.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for her, getting a member of royalty to love her is easier said than done. Getting through the front door was the first challenge, as guards don't let just any...peasant?...see members of the nobility. Second, even when she finds him, he is hardly impressed by a girl who is short, unkempt, uneducated, of ignoble birth (which can't even be determined), and possessing of a &quot;mousy&quot; look. It doesn't matter how much she claims to know of the blade, or of magick.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there's that matter of Little Mouse being, for all intents and purposes, a witch. In Renaissance Europe. She was lucky to escape the castle with her life.<br /> <br /> But the winds of fortune shift, and Little Mouse got her chance. Political turmoil rocked the land, and the castle came under threat from without...and from within. The prince only dodged the blade of treachery most foul, by the intervention of Little Mouse. Fleeing the country, the prince and mouse sneak across wilderness and scattered villages, hoping to gain asylum from the prince's distant relatives. Mayhaps they gain assistance from other mages along the way, but Little Mouse is the prince's first and foremost protector. She guards him with her life. Hoping against hope that, when she finally confesses her love, the prince will reciprocate her feelings.<br /> <br /> Will her dreams come true? Or will she be reduced to a rodent once more, heartbroken and alone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-02T07:50:42-07:00","id":1250746,"title":"","content":"Note: this one isn't appropriate as a PC for two major reasons. Firstly, she works best as a villain due to her genocidal paradigm and warped vision of Ascension. Secondly, her concept demands traits and advantages which lie outside of starting PC territory in most games.<br /> <br /> 116) Concept: The Plague Bringer<br /> <br /> &quot;There's this old Iterator motto... &quot;What intelligent creature would choose its flaws over perfection?&quot; I couldn't agree more. If the homo genus is going to survive, it must adapt. The strong must survive, and humanity must be shepherded into a bright future under a program of rational and benevolent eugenics. I only wish that the progenitors and iterators had stayed their course, and not backed down from the cusp of human excellence...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;If you were thinking about escaping and 'saving the day', you're too late. The pandemic has already begun. Patient zero is on his way to a seminar... &quot;Facing the Future&quot; I believe. A load of overpaid academics and politicians pontificating about saving the world. The great irony is that simply by gathering together, they have. The infection will spread virulently, with the strong acting as carriers, angels of death, spreading my magnum opus into the blood of the weak as they travel back to their home countries. Within a few weeks, only the strong will remain. Most Magi will be spared, don't worry about that. The Revenant families, the lycanthropes, and the strongest homo sapiens, they'll all live. And I'll never be thanked for this, but I *have* saved the human race from itself, trust me on that. I've tried to make the course of illness as painless as possible, but I prioritized virulence and selectivity above all else. Those destined to die from their infections will exhibit a highly aggressive and irrational state, perfect for spreading the gift.<br /> <br /> In two days time you'll be free, and you can see for yourself the wonderful world I've created.&quot;<br /> <br /> Name: Katarina Obertus (and various aliases)<br /> <br /> Ostensible Affiliation: Euthanatos, Progenitors<br /> <br /> True Affiliation: Herself, her family's dark vision of Ascension, and (in her view) the human race<br /> <br /> Katarina Obertus, like many Mages, is excellent. A starred first class degree in biomedical sciences, a masters in genetics, and a lauded PhD dissertation focused on biological anthropology and evolutionary biology, all achieved by the time she was 20 years old... or so it would seem. Katarina looks like an ordinary woman in her early 20s (officially being 23), but she is actually 52. Like all of the members of her family, a vestigial link to the Cainite race has left her to age gracefully from puberty onwards, at 1/4 of the rate.<br /> <br /> Before she reached the appearance of adulthood, she cloistered herself away in the family's libraries, studying works on physiology and eugenics. Inspired by the philosophy of her family's patron clan, she began to focus attention on Azi Dahaka, the &quot;perfect form&quot;. Rejecting the idea that she would find some enlightenment in fetishizing the form of a dragon, she began to Awaken as she imagined humanity freed from weakness and sickness, brought into a modern age of enlightenment and strength.<br /> <br /> Katarina's main inspirations are the philosophy of Clan Tzimisce and Family Obertus. The Tzimisce believe that ascendance can be found in the flesh and the mind, through constant alteration and reinvention. Changing appearance, ability, preference, personality, obsession, memory. The Obertus believe that homo sapiens is simply a precursor to homo obertus, and that humankind will naturally give way to the stronger Revenants. In recent years she has learned about the philosophy of the Euthanatos while undercover; this has simply fueled her resolve. She believes that she is bringing the great cycle into balance, and that there is no sin in what she is doing. All those who die will return stronger in the next cycle thanks to her work, so in the long run any &quot;evil&quot; she commits is moot, and the ends more than justify the means.<br /> <br /> As she emerged into the world, she used her many advantages to secure phenomenal qualifications, and was eventually approached by the Technocratic Union. Making a name for herself among the Progenitors, she gradually grew in power and influence, eventually reaching a point where she could form aliases and use them to gain a presence in various sects and key groups. Making use of Vicissitude, she became a master of disguise, creating doubles who could stand in for her when necessary, and changing identities as most people change clothes.<br /> <br /> Magick:<br /> <br /> Paradigm: We Are One Flesh, Might is Right, Humanity must Evolve; Katarina believes that natural selection is a natural law, and this guides her magick and her entire philosophy. Humanity is like a single organism, and it must self-regulate. As her Arete improved, she gained a greater understanding and began to see past the illusory separation of flesh, seeing more and more clearly that humanity must be reshaped in her vision if it is to become healthy and strong.<br /> <br /> Practice: Enlightened Science, Mad Science<br /> <br /> Instruments: Organisms (especially pathogens), Lab Gear, Calculations and Projections, Blood and Fluids, Eye Contact, Surgery and Vivisection, Brews and Concoctions<br /> <br /> Roleplaying:<br /> <br /> Katarina's aliases are intentionally unassuming and don't attract much attention. She is skilled in making people rely on her, and winning their trust.<br /> <br /> When she is herself, Katarina is friendly and honest; she's no Nephandi, and her vision is one of Ascension, simply a terrible and dark one. She argues for her beliefs as convincingly as possible, and is well read in terms of utilitarian philosophy. There's no superficially obvious hatefulness or malice in her; she is &quot;doing what must be done&quot;. To her, the only path to humanity's survival and success is the path she offers. This prediction is backed up by various statistical models she has produced using Time, however it's likely that her obsession and personal belief in this genocidal ascension have biased the results.<br /> <br /> Katarina places a lot of emphasis on politeness and being a good host. She has a great deal of respect for other magi, and exceptional human beings. If she were to talk to a player character, she would discuss their goals, their beliefs, and the significance of magick in their eyes. How they see humanity's future, as things stand.<br /> <br /> Mechanics:<br /> <br /> Arete 6, Life 5, Time 2, Entropy 2, Forces 2, Mind 4, Correspondence 4, Prime 4, Matter 1, Spirit 1<br /> <br /> - Katarina is an Obertus Revenant, and she has 1 dot in Vicissitude; this allows her to disguise her face and her voice as she desires, given plenty of time and a few Intelligence + Medicine rolls. She also has 1 dot in Auspex, which allows her to reduce the difficulty of a mundane Perception roll by 1 when she wishes.<br /> <br /> - Katarina's &quot;magnum opus&quot; is a viral pathogen, the work of someone who could rightfully be called an Archmage, which reads the code of the host's DNA and chooses different regulons (large overarching groups of genes programming different kinds of &quot;modes&quot; into a single virus, which are activated in different contexts) depending on the target's nature. Individuals with supernaturally enhanced bodies or abilities (sensed with Life and Spirit), exceptional abilities (sensed with Life and Mind), a special &quot;cure&quot; she has prepared for those she has promised to keep alive in exchange for their help (sensed with Matter 1) or amazing health (sensed with Life and Mind) will act as carrier hosts, simply spreading the disease at an alarming rate through sneezing, coughing, skin contact and all bodily fluids. Those who are both mundane and have notable flaws in their health (carriers for serious genetic disease, for example) will experience total organ failure. Her predictions indicate that 1.3 billion individuals will survive this pandemic, bringing an end to global warming. Her attempts to steal the necessary materials to bring about this great plague and introduce it to the population (samples of a certain viral pathogen which she needs to steal from a Technocracy stronghold, samples of tass she needs to acquire from the Verbena, the expertise of several leading virologists, and other requirements) will form the basis of a chronicle in which she acts as the villain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-03-2018, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T04:30:51-07:00","id":1251021,"title":"","content":"117) Concept: Unknown<br /> <br /> Name: n.a.<br /> <br /> &quot;Invisibility is a mixed blessing. When I was homeless I would go days without anyone speaking to me. People would rather have some blissful ignorance, and avoid confronting society's failures. When I opened my eyes for the first time, I found I could do anything without anyone noticing me. Walk through a fancy gala, help myself to champagne, sit next to the string quartet... you know I've been staying at this chantry for 3 years now, and none of you know my name? It's like I slide out of people's minds. I've tried dying my hair, but within a few minutes I'm &quot;that girl, you know, the one... well she looked sort of...&quot; and before long I'm gone, invisible again, forgotten.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We got through a lot of candles and twine. I mean I could swear I'm the only one who uses them, but we don't keep too close an eye on ritual gear. And the Apprentices are all useless; when I come into the high ritual chamber it's always in a state, salt and wax left out, and they all claim they left it tidy. Otherwise you should find everything is in order.&quot;<br /> <br /> Magick:<br /> <br /> Paradigm: Perceived Reality is an Illusion; what we experience, the &quot;sensory reality&quot; we construct, is far from total truth. We add and remove things. We approximate. We fill in gaps. That's why optical illusions work, and it's also why we don't always get the head count right... some people just blend into the background. There's something quiet about their presence, they don't give off that &quot;I Am Here&quot; signal the way everyone else does. And sometimes that is taken to an extreme...<br /> <br /> It's possible that this illusion can be changed by thought and will, reshaping the perceptions of others to create a new reality.<br /> <br /> Practice: Shamanism, self-taught, with elements taken from constant observation of Mages of many practices<br /> <br /> Instruments: Books and Scrolls, Runes and Writing, Circles and Designs, Thought-Forms, Transgressions, God-Bonding and Weapons<br /> <br /> Unknown is a Shaman since it brings the company of ineffable spirits which she feels are like her kin. Unobserved, impersonal, observant, quietly powerful. She is naturally used to her own company, favouring solitary pursuits such as reading, writing poetry, creating art and committing petty crimes against those around her, with all of these forming the basis of her magick. Her own Avatar is personified as the Quiet One, a silent mentor which guides through an ambiance and cryptic clues, giving a sense of companionship to a deeply lonely woman.<br /> <br /> Roleplay: if you're part of a group of Mages, then you know a lot about them. Since they can't perceive you unless you directly grab their attention, your relationships with them are stuck in the first stages (at least for now). Over time through familiarity they may have developed a weak sense of your identity, recalling you vaguely each time you grab their attention.<br /> <br /> You're a relatively quiet and introverted person, but when you do have a conversation with someone you've been observing you enjoy having a chance to use your voice. You're generally good-natured but have little respect for privacy or boundaries. You know that any transgressions you commit will slide out of people's memories over time.<br /> <br /> Your goal is to form true and lasting relationships with other Mages using Mind as a crutch to overcome your natural tendency to slip out of people's memories.<br /> <br /> Mechanics:<br /> <br /> - Arcane 5, Dexterity 5, Stealth 5, and possibly a totem animal relating to camouflage or stalking like Tiger or Mantis. The net result is that unless you are deliberately grabbing attention, or are in a room with a fiercely observant person, you will almost always go unobserved. Furthermore, your Arcane rating means that you slide out of people's memories over time, becoming more featureless and vague as they try to hold onto the memory. Mundane and Magickal rolls to try and sense or investigate or learn about you are opposed.<br /> <br /> - Arete 3, Mind 2, Spirit 2, Forces 2; Forces forms the basis of illusions (from total invisibility, to avoiding tripping laser detection systems), Spirit forms the basis of Shamanism, and Mind forms the basis of her control and her limited relationships; by using Mind 2 she tries to plant enduring memories of herself in other people (this can be taken for the sake of RP). She still has a lot of control over what is remembered and what isn't however (unless the other Mage were to use Mind and Time to try and remember absolutely everything about her, however her Arcane rating would oppose these attempts for good and bad).<br /> <br /> - No Backgrounds, and 2 in each of the Social Attributes. She once tried to store some money in a bank, but somehow her application process didn't end up going through; being inherently forgettable makes such processes very difficult. So she simply borrows from other people, staying in empty spare rooms, taking what she needs, using magick to make up for it (curing a minor mental funk with Mind, bringing good luck upon a household with the help of a spirit).<br /> <br /> &quot;Even talking about her is difficult. I remember us going to great pains with some sort of ritual, and I can just about hold her in my mind. I'm worried that she might be some kind of Marauder living in our midst, driving us all insane... I mean how would I even know?! When I go to check on the chantry's security system, I can see her plain as day, but when I look away she kind of... fuzzes. I mean this has to be some sort of insanity right? She thinks she doesn't exist, and she's projecting that onto every mind in the vicinity...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-03-2018, 07:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T05:55:01-07:00","id":1251036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas#post893464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it would be fun to do one for Mage (all factions and the Sorcerers) as well. Please, no more than two at a time.<br /> <br /> 1) A Cultist has discovered a way to help people who've lost certain senses (taste, touch, etc) feel again through him. Example: A person who lose their sense of taste can enjoy a candy bar with the Cultist eating it and then mentally passing his feelings to them via the Mind sphere. Interestingly, this talent has gotten the attention of members of the local Vampire community who would like the &quot;Pleasure Dealer&quot; to help them feel again.</div> </div> </div> </div>1.1) Concept: Pleasure Dealer, Sensual Collector and Librarian<br /> <br /> Magick:<br /> <br /> Paradigm: Reality exists in the Mind; Consciousness is the only true experience.<br /> <br /> Practice: Sensual Magick; lots of tools and behaviours that heighten and alter the sensory experience.<br /> <br /> Instruments: Sex and Sensuality, Bodyforms, Thoughtforms, Eye Contact, Food and Drink, Vocalizations, Gems and Stones, Symbols, Aromatherapy...<br /> <br /> Using Mind and Life, this Mage collects and shares experiences. With a vast mental library of experiences taken from his own mind/body and the minds and bodies of others, he is a sensual zenith. These can be used to help or to harm, from inducing the sensation of euphoria to bringing about the deepest dread.<br /> <br /> He is a great believer in the idea that sensation and feeling should be diverse, and that a bit of pain or sadness can be good, that these are useful feelings.<br /> <br /> His idea of Ascension is becoming omnipotent through the recollection of All Sensation, to know through personal and borrowed experience what it is to be anything and everything, to know the beginning and the end of sensation, and to move past it into godhood.<br /> <br /> His Demesne, a great mind palace, is a space within the maya which stores millions of experiences, and will store many more as time passes...<br /> <br /> - Arete 4, Mind 3 (Mind 2 extends senses to others, Mind 3 extends them to those who are unwilling), Correspondence 3 (allowing sensation to be shared across great distances), Spirit 2 (opening up a whole new realm of sights, sounds, ideas), Time 3 (extending sensation, shortening it and recalling past sensations), Prime 2 (controlling the flow of energy, bringing it to great peaks, merging it, draining it, gifting it), Forces 1 (adding new sensory experiences), Life 3 (physical experiences, sharing the physiological experience along with the mental one, heart rate, peripheral sensation...), Matter 1 (adding new sensory experiences), Entropy 1 (giving a sense of destiny and significance, drawing him towards important experiences).<br /> <br /> - The Cult Background, to reflect his acolytes who go forth and seek new experiences to add to the library. If he has taken his quest far enough, or he has warped those who follow him too much, then he might be considered a &quot;villain&quot; by some players. His personal belief is that the whole breadth of human experience should be accessible to all, and that will inevitably lead to him trying to open the eyes of the masses if he is left unchecked...<br /> <br /> - The Demesne Background, and the Lucid Dreaming skill.<br /> <br /> - The Dream background, to represent his ability to pull abilities he doesn't possess from the many memories he has collected. He can only do this with one ability per scene, but it opens up many rare talents and a lot of flexibility, making him a terrifying villain or adversary, or a powerful ally.<br /> <br /> Roleplay: You've heard better, you've tasted better, you've seen better. Digging through every experience you can find, in the minds of sleepers and mages and wraiths and vampires, you've experienced so much that everyday enjoyment is lost to you, unless it is heightened through use of magick. The extremes that the dealer can offer will ruin people given time, himself included.<br /> <br /> His clients include the celibate, who wish to know what it feels to experience the most potent embrace. The occultist, who wants to know how it feels when a Lupine goes through &quot;the change&quot;, or how a Cainite feels when they are embraced or feed or commit diablerie, who wants to know how Glamour tastes to a Fae or how Passion tastes to a Wraith. The Setite who wishes to feel the rush that his clients feel when he makes love to them or feeds them his blood, or gives them narcotics or alcohol. The dying woman who wants to experience that beautiful evening where her first husband proposed to her in Paris, all those years ago. The addict who wants to kick their addiction but needs to feel something. The ancient supernatural being that wants to recover its memories. The historian who wants to examine the sights and sounds and people of times past.<br /> <br /> He charges in money and favours, but also in experiences. The memories he brings back, the feelings he transfers from the Vampire's ghoul to the Vampire, and the odd experience he finds in a client's memories... he keeps them. Locks them away. No need to mention that to those who use his services; they might not be happy knowing that their experiences will be blended into the experiences he offers his other clients.<br /> <br /> Most of his cultists were once clients, and they are truly devoted to him, including a few supernaturals and people of significance. To them he is the core of all experience, and they have few memories which trump those he has gifted them with.<br /> <br /> While he cannot make Wonders himself, with the help of another Ecstatic he has created Charms and Wonders which give a certain experience either once (in the form of a small vial of fluid that you drink to experience the sensation or memory) or many times (each time you touch it, for example; these are given to those who have earned it). The cult is very much like a real cult, with levels and hidden teachings and demands that you give up resources to the great leader...<br /> <br /> His enemies may be unfortunate enough to experience how it feels to be harmed in the worst ways imaginable. How it feels to go through the Torment or Oblivion, or how it feels to be warped by a Tzimisce or a creative Nephandi. Alternatively, they may experience terrible pain on top of each sensation.<br /> <br /> Ultimate Goal: he could create his own Realm with mastery of the Spheres. This realm could be a paradise of perfect sensations, stitched together from memories and experiences and emotions. He would exist there mostly, and his followers would bring new experiences to the realm. Alternatively, &quot;Paradise&quot; could be a lie, and those who &quot;go to paradise&quot; are being destroyed, their Quintessence and memories being absorbed by their master. This would solve the problem of the cult becoming too big, or anyone becoming too senior or experienced and therefore threatening. Or &quot;Paradise&quot; could be a testing ground, and those who are sent there are trapped and put through situations which are so extreme that they elicit new emotions and experiences which he can harvest, with Time flowing differently so that he may gather new experiences more quickly as they are tortured (among other things) for eternity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-03-2018, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T09:24:00-07:00","id":1251079,"title":"","content":"Note: playing this one could be really divisive at some tables. Whether this character *is* spiritually related to the High Umbral Spirit of Christ, or simply *thinks* she is, will likely depend on the taste of the storyteller and the players.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, this might stray into uncomfortable territory since a key part of her concept is &quot;what if a person running a cult, and acting as a Televangelist, were actually supernaturally gifted and virtuous, and not a huge con artist&quot;. Considering that there are people who perform and &quot;cure&quot; people of their cancer on-stage in real life, and those people are abusing people and committing theft, it's possible some players might not want a PC at the table to be doing that &quot;but for realsies&quot;.<br /> <br /> 118) Concept: The Pop Messiah<br /> <br /> &quot;My faith is a big part of my work. And faith evolves. I know a lot of you have been hurt by the church, and that's why I want to lead people into a new kind of faith. One that's fit for the modern era, and one which preaches to the marginalized, as Christ did.&quot;<br /> <br /> Tradition: Choristers, Ecstatics, loose affiliations.<br /> <br /> A potent pop idol carrying what she sees as a messianic secret; she thinks she is the second coming of Christ. She might also be a functional Marauder with some subtle quiet, and she might be turning her biggest fans into an international cult. Who knows.<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course I'll be called a false prophet. Most of the other Choristers will never believe me. But I am growing into my power, and in time I will have my own chorus singing along with me. They'll Awaken, and be my apostles. I'm revealing this secret to you, Andrew, because you will be my first true follower, like your namesake.&quot;<br /> <br /> She's enigmatic, she's inspirational, she practices what she preaches. Big donations to the needy, a relatively modest lifestyle considering her income, advice which helps dysfunctional people to fix their lives. She presents herself as both a musical and style icon, and she mixes her faith with everything she does. A lot of what she does could be labeled as &quot;Christian Pop&quot; and &quot;Self-Help Pop&quot;. Lots of empowerment, faith, political and personal messages.<br /> <br /> &quot;All of you are capable of it. You can change the world. I had nothing when I started out except a god-given talent for singing. And I'm doing what I can to help people with it. You all need to find that special gift and do what you can with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Magick:<br /> <br /> Paradigm: Creation is Divine and Alive, It's All Good; Have Faith, I am the Saviour, I am a God in Disguise<br /> <br /> For her, magick flows from the divinity of the universe, of certain acts, and from her own divinity. Through living her life she is essentially writing a new testament, a third testament. As Jesus came to fulfill and rewrite the old laws, she has come to do the same. She believes that Christ was limited by the time he preached in, and that the world wasn't ready for certain teachings. Christ's message was deeply controversial already (turn the other cheek, love all humanity, accept those who are marginalized) and including ideas that would still be controversial in the 21st century would have hampered his central message.<br /> <br /> Practice: God-Bonding, Social Engineering, Faith<br /> <br /> Instruments: Voice and Vocalizations, Dress and Style, Dancing and Bodyforms, Prayers and Invocations, Eye Contact, Symbolism, Ordeals and Exertions<br /> <br /> Mechanics:<br /> <br /> - Arete 3, Spirit 1, Forces 1, Mind 2, Correspondence 2<br /> <br /> - Avatar 5, True Faith 1<br /> <br /> - Resources 4, Cult 2 (aides, groupies, stylists, backup dancers and vocalists), Fame 3<br /> <br /> - Potentially, the Nephilim Merit to represent being the spiritual child of some High Umbral representation of Christ or the Christian God. Alternatively, she's a Marauder and has a Permanent Quiet rating of 1, with her central deviation from reality being the belief that she is the Messiah, including a Sanity Sink which makes those she has prolonged contact with believe it too (if not explicitly). Or... both. There's no reason that she couldn't have a legitimate link to Christ in the High Umbra and also be a tad insane; it's possible that a paranoid schizophrenic could believe that MI5, the CIA and the KGB were watching them and also be correct (if very unlikely) after all.<br /> <br /> If it's the latter, then she has some weak protection from Paradox (detailed rules in M20) and she also extends her personal reality to those she spends a lot of time around; if any of her fans were to Awaken, they would likely do so as Marauders with the intense belief that she is some kind of prophet or messiah.<br /> <br /> If it's the former, then she gets the benefits of Nephilim as described in M20. 7 points of Quintessence every 24 hours (and can store 7 points as personal quintessence), easier to command using rituals or spells which are designed to work on high umbral spirits (say, the ritual of an infernalist who was used to capturing and destroying Angels), capable of physically entering the High Umbra with the right spheres (normally impossible, most Mages use astral projection), has an easier time commanding spirits of all kinds (from asking for an angel's aid to casting out demons or ghosts who have possessed mortals), may have Advantages (from angel wings to rapid healing), may have a Derangement (from paranoia to megalomania), -1 difficulty to rolls relating to the High Umbra, including Mind and Spirit effects, a burning powerful aura, several points in physical flaws to reflect how unstable the form of a half-spirit human is...<br /> <br /> - Enchanting Feature, Voice. Her voice, in singing and speech, is a Unique, Personalized Instrument. This means -2 difficult to mundane and magickal rolls involving her voice.<br /> <br /> Roleplaying:<br /> <br /> An embodiment of positive and kind faith. Warm, nurturing, thoughtful. Somewhat holier-than-thou; when she is rebuking another person (say a hateful pastor) she adopts the kind of tone someone would if they were absolutely certain that they were right and the other person was wrong. Certainty characterizes a lot of her behaviour; she is *certain*.<br /> <br /> She uses live performances as an opportunity to perform rituals (which are typically coincidental thanks to a local Reality Zone generated by the performance), and to ask for miracles with True Faith. Praying that someone in the crowd will recover from a serious illness, praying that someone in the crowd will rediscover their passion for life, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Example Effects:<br /> <br /> - Examining the crowd, she uses Mind and Spirit, along with Correspondence, to try and quickly single out a person in need of help. Finding a person who has been deeply unhappy for a long time, she invites them to speak, with an aide bringing them a mic. Using Mind 1 she gleans information about what's wrong in their life, and gives vague but helpful ideas about the changes they could make. Using Mind 1 to reduce the difficulty, she attempts a Charisma + Expression roll to inspire them to improve their life (with bonus dice from Fame and the situation), and gets many successes.<br /> <br /> - During a performance, she uses Forces 1 to perfect her command of her voice through listening to the tones and using this feedback to perfect her singing technique temporarily (reduction to the Performance difficult). She then begins to perform, using a song as a focus for an effect to create religious hysteria and devotion in the audience (this is an out-of-character description; she wouldn't describe what she was doing this way at all, and she would be being entirely honest... she is potentially delusional remember) using Mind 2 to heighten existing feelings, and Correspondence 2 to spread it across a wide area. With the support of her Cult she has an Arete pool of 5, and she can attempt the roll several times before her Stamina becomes a limitation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-03-2018, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-06T09:28:45-07:00","id":1251929,"title":"","content":"119) An Order of Hermes Mage who is such an outcast and who tries to innovate so much that he was denied entry into House Ex Miscellanea despite his desire and wish to belong to it. He does have a grudgingly accepted place in House Tytalus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-06-2018, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T17:14:03-07:00","id":1254882,"title":"","content":"120) An unorthodox Dreamspeaker, this family man carries on the legacy of ancient Roman animism. His family line has dutifully paid respect to the <i>numina</i> (spirits) in all things, including the &quot;greater numina&quot; (the Roman gods of the imperial cult), and to the numina of the household. With the death of his uncle, this father is now the eldest male in the family, making him host to the family's <i>genius</i>. Being the embodiment of the ancestral numina of the bloodline itself, he has both great power and great responsibility. Not just to protect the family, but to see it continue. His greatest fear is that he'll fail to pass on the devotion to the old spirits to his children.<br /> <br /> His magic involves the ancient rituals and offerings of the Roman household, in order to gain the favor of numina in the world. The man's prized possession is a short sword from the Roman legion, passed down through generations, and possessed of an aware and potent numina. He rounds out his ancestral knowledge with experience is divination, via the method of interpreting omens and the flight patterns of birds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 09-16-2018, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T03:18:32-07:00","id":1256674,"title":"","content":"121) A Virtual Adept gone Marauder who believes that the world is a videogame. He spends a lot of his time &quot;speedrunning&quot; things in the most vulgar ways imaginable, clipping through walls and abusing the effects of Wonders, hacking reality as if it were a game...<br /> <br /> &quot;The lore is so fucking deep... I'm trying to romance a Vampire on this playthrough, wish me luck!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 09-23-2018, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T06:47:15-07:00","id":1256703,"title":"","content":"122) A real mind-hacker, this Virtual Adept prefers to operate from a distance. Skilled in Data and Mind, he acts as a kind of mission control for Tradition groups. Hacking electronic devices gives him access to the 3D space of distant locations, from security or phone cameras where possible. If he needs to, though, and when he's familiar with the subject, he can hack their phones or other devices, then pivot to the wetware computers they call brains. Allowing him to see through the eyes of others. During many ops, he keeps in mental contact with his team-mates, coordinating their efforts like a cyber-psychic relay. When they spot an enemy, he can then use them to pivot again, into the enemy's head. He's working his way up to being proficient in mind control.<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly, his forays into directly dictating thoughts, feelings, experiences, and actions has given him more than a budding superiority complex. He likes the feeling of control that mentalism gives, and his 360 degree view of distant locations is gratifying in a manner that worries his allies. Except the Celestial Chorus ones, who are offended by his repeated, gleeful shouts of &quot;BECOME AS GODS!&quot;<br /> <br /> Hopefully, his arrogance and power madness will be tempered the first time he faces a mentalist more powerful than himself. Double hopefully, he'll be able to walk away from that encounter with all his limbs and an intact psyche. At the moment, his allies learn to not put too much stock in his high opinion of himself, when it comes to risk taking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T07:12:09-07:00","id":1256705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1250746#post1250746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When she is herself, Katarina is friendly and honest; she's no Nephandi, and her vision is one of Ascension, simply a terrible and dark one. She argues for her beliefs as convincingly as possible, and is well read in terms of utilitarian philosophy. There's no superficially obvious hatefulness or malice in her; she is &quot;doing what must be done&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those characters and NPCs who &quot;are not as bad as the Nephandi&quot; ( this is not the first time I see this term/idea used ) seem to me more ruthless, uncaring and focused on making others suffer than the Nephandi are. In fact, if there would be any ranking to make, then such persons are worse than the Nephandi - because they are very delusional in that they think they are not doing any evil, unlike the Nephandi Mages ; who are keenly aware of this in regards to their philosophy and their deeds and who are honest - to themselves and to other persons - about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-23-2018, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-23T07:52:06-07:00","id":1256712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1256705#post1256705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those characters and NPCs who &quot;are not as bad as the Nephandi&quot; ( this is not the first time I see this term/idea used ) seem to me more ruthless, uncaring and focused on making others suffer than the Nephandi are. In fact, if there would be any ranking to make, then such persons are worse than the Nephandi - because they are very delusional in that they think they are not doing any evil, unlike the Nephandi Mages ; who are keenly aware of this in regards to their philosophy and their deeds and who are honest - to themselves and to other persons - about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the Nephandi but I think the Mage books should be super duper clear that most Evil Mages aren't Nephandi, and that you can cause more damage as a normal Mage in some cases. Good or bad intentions can cause a lot of harm when you're fighting for reality itself. Example villains should include plenty of completely sane Mages who are just bad in the way normal humans are bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T15:34:33-07:00","id":1258277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1256712#post1256712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I love the Nephandi but I think the Mage books should be super duper clear that most Evil Mages aren't Nephandi (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, I think that what is written in the books makes it to a great extent clear that it is the opposite - that the Nephandi influence and capabilities are so far-reaching and have such varied, practiced and unique recruitment methods that most radical and/or evil Mages do eventually join the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> First off, it has to be noted that the Nephandi are one of the three primary factions / organizations of Mages - it is the Traditions, the Technocracy, and the Nephandi. The Disparate Alliance, the Crafts, the Marauders, and Mages who aren't in any group or faction - they aren't mentioned in the same way as those three.<br /> First, it means that the Nephandi have organization, logistics, established rules, resources. The Prelati are their generals and rite leaders. The Adsinistrati are dedicated tempters. Between the Nephandi Mages of those two ranks, there is a definite inclination - ideological, pratical, and organizational - towards recruitment of new Mages into the Nephandi.<br /> Second, it means that the Nephandi have a sense of pride, comraderie, and agenda that has a lot of potential to convince and draw Mages into joining the Nephandi. Including those who are on the outs in their respective factions or groups ; and might be feeling and considering that they need an alternative for being in their current or previous Mage faction / group.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi certainly have some sure means and experience of finding persons, considering that they regularly search for and find young Widderslaintes to recruit them.<br /> <br /> Also, where are the evil, radical, outcast, or ostracized ( not that these are the only reasons to join the Nephandi, of course ) to go but the Nephandi ? The Nephandi have such a reputation and opinions about them, that I think many for example radical and ambitious Mages are likely to feel a definite temptation to at least contact the Nephandi if they are, for example, on the outs with their factions, when in a bad and problematic situation, or when in need of advice, or if they need or want help with a plan or an undertaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-05-2018, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T03:31:34-07:00","id":1259038,"title":"","content":"123)<br /> It could be said that every Enlightenment of each Technocrat is unique and exceptional ; however, it is a rarity among newly recruited Technocrats that a person chooses focus almost solely on the activity or the epiphany that was responsible for the circumstances that led to the person becoming Enlightened. This Technocrat Operative of the New World Order is such a person, choosing to focus on interviews as her principal activity, method of action, interest, and Foci for her Procedures.<br /> <br /> A successful and satisfied journalist, she interviewed a Technocrat of the Syndicate Convention for a business magazine, and noticed that it was not possible at all to get a second interview. In fact, using her contacts, trying to contact him, or using official channels only seemed to make it harder - as his reputation, his time schedule, and even his paper trail and digital footprint all worked in various ways against both unwanted attention and acquiring more information about him. Suspicious and interested, the journalist opted to include references that she was somehow certain only he would notice. She started including in her interviews, as much as she could while keeping it sensible, conclusions to talked about issues that were made in a similar way to how he did it when he gave her the interview - through short, half serious, seemingly unrelated anecdotes and made-up stories.<br /> After she did this in six interviews for magazines and newspapers, he proved her point - that he was more than he let on - by appearing at a restaurant she dined in regularly. There he was, sitting with an almost finished course at a table right next to the one she reserved for that day. In a few moments, they agreed that he will order another course for himself - and pay for hers - and sit with the journalist at her table. She Awakened after the first thirty minutes of the hour long dinner, which the Syndicate member did notice. She was introduced into the Technocracy after he called in for a car ( driven by an agent of the Technocracy ) and asked for them to be taken to the shared Syndicate and New World Order Construct that he worked and lived at. Wanting a hands-on approach, she chose the New World Order Convention and the Operative Methodology ; this was confirmed by psychological and statistical evaluations of the N.W.O Technocrats present as a right and appropriate choice for her.<br /> <br /> <br /> So far, she has managed to make interviews central to the majority of her Procedures ; through her own inventiveness and efforts, and with the help of other Technocrats, she has developed the application of interviews and interview analysis in various field of Technocratic Inspired Science.<br /> <br /> When being able to sync with the Primal Field at the Construct via a cybernetic eye that she replaced her left eye with, she is able to store Primal Energy it in her body. To do this, she needs to activate and synchronize the implant with the Primal Energy - for this she does a short fifteen minutes interview, and the implant is acted by the feelings of familiarity, elation, and relaxation. She can do those interviews with any other Technocrat or with an Extraordinary Citizen. She does them relatively mundane topics, like politics of countries or the most recent cinema movies ; this is a preference, and not a necessity. ( This is Prime 1 Store Quintessence , useable a Technocratic Construct. )<br /> <br /> Through specialized cameras and recording technology she sets up to be active during an interview, she is able to gain a Connection for her variant of Correspondence : Data for the person she is interviewing. The devices register the voice, gestures, posture, eye movements of the person being interviewed ; this data is later used to gain information and to link to a given person so that Correspondence : Data Procedures can carried out more easily. ( This is Correspondence : Data 2 or simply Correspondence 2 )<br /> <br /> Through her interviews and analysis of those interviews, she is able to carry out Mind 1, Mind 2, and Mind 3 Procedures. Knowing what a persons thinks ( including about topics not related to the topic(s) of the interview ) , suggesting to a person what to think, and implying what not to think about ; this is all possible for the young N.W.O Technocrat . At the same time, she can direct and set-up an interview so she is able to, in various and superlative ways, affect and boost her own moods and lead her thoughts to new and novel avenues. ( This is Mind 1 Empower Self . )<br /> She is capable of carrying out some of the standard Mind Procedures known by Operatives of the N.W.O .<br /> <br /> <br /> She is currently content to be an N.W.O Operative who works mainly through acquiring and analyzing information, and manipulating persons through subtle ways while using her cover as a journalist ; and while still being a journalist, if only to a small and limited extent compared to the fact that she is a Technocrat.<br /> <br /> [ For this Technocrat Mage and for the purpose of her Procedures, an interview is not just a conversation, of course. The topic must be stated to the other person, permission asked, she and the person must sit at a quiet enough place, and she must inform that she will be noting down and/or recording what will be said, and do this. ]<br /> <br /> [ This Mage has Mind 3, Prime 1, Correspondence : Data or Correspondence 2 . ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-05-2018, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T11:34:40-07:00","id":1259627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1249025#post1249025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">114) The Abomination<br /> <br /> It was only an abnormal force of will that stopped him from falling prey to his own Avatar (as most widderslainte do), that stopped him from becoming a Nephandus. Resisting descension came with a price; Addison is wracked and haunted by his own Avatar, and finds it opposing his growth and ascension at every turn. Practising magick is a painful and dangerous business for him, and he knows that he walks a dangerous tightrope.<br /> <br /> - Arete 3, Entropy 2, Spirit 1, Life 1, Forces 2<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Did you start creating this character concept by first deciding to base the character around the &quot;abomination&quot; concept, and then later made him a Widderslainte ? Or was it the other way around - did you start with wanting to write up a character who is a Widderslainte, and afterwards you decided to create him around the &quot;abomination&quot; concept ? Or maybe it was neither of these two possibilities ?<br /> <br /> I don't think that an Avatar of a Mage who is a Widderslainte would oppose her or him if the Mage would not join the Nephandi and would not act like a Nephandus. I haven't read anything in any M:tA book that said or implied that this is what happens in such a situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-08-2018, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-08T13:51:47-07:00","id":1259659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1259627#post1259627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you start creating this character concept by first deciding to base the character around the &quot;abomination&quot; concept, and then later made him a Widderslainte ? Or was it the other way around - did you start with wanting to write up a character who is a Widderslainte, and afterwards you decided to create him around the &quot;abomination&quot; concept ? Or maybe it was neither of these two possibilities ?<br /> <br /> I don't think that an Avatar of a Mage who is a Widderslainte would oppose her or him if the Mage would not join the Nephandi and would not act like a Nephandus. I haven't read anything in any M:tA book that said or implied that this is what happens in such a situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that if your Avatar had gone through the Cauls, it would guide you towards Descension and working alongside the Nephandi, or working as a Nephandic individual at least. If you refuse to start descending or working with Nephandi, surely the Avatar (especially if it's Avatar 5 and therefore a highly self-aware, demanding and powerful one) will oppose you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-09T13:09:00-07:00","id":1259865,"title":"","content":"124) A Syndicate woman who hasn't left her home in thirty years.<br /> <br /> A trauma sufferer, she developed agoraphobia early in life, leading her to become a shut-in. When her parents died, she used her meager inheritance to play the stock market. A well-educated and savvy woman, she became very good at it. In order to ensure her financial stability - and simply out of boredom and a desire to have an effect on the outside world - she started using her money to form a network of connections and employees. Through intermediaries paid from shadow accounts, she gathered information. About people, places, plans in motion. She extorted powerful people, sometimes for money, more often for power.<br /> <br /> It was when she made the mistake of unknowingly extorting a high ranking Technocrat that the Syndicate investigated and uncovered her web of influence. The Technocracy was impressed, and offered her a job.<br /> <br /> These days, being able to run an information and financial empire from a phone isn't too impressive, unto itself. Many people do it all the time, and many not even Enlightened. She's just very good at it, and the additional powers afforded to her by the internet and telecommunications technology have only enhanced her reach. With a few phone calls to the right agents in her employ, and she can effect change on a large scale. She takes a certain pride in the fact that she's becoming a player on the world stage, despite being no one of importance. Unlike politicians, executives, media personalities, and state intelligence agents, she holds power while remaining in the dark. The intelligent and well-informed can intuit her position as a player in what she calls The Great Game, but are stymied by her lack of public presence. She merely sits on her web of influence, earning her the moniker &quot;Spider Executive&quot; among members of the Syndicate who are aware of her.<br /> <br /> These younger members sometimes even receive orders from her, but always over the phone or in emails. Few Technocrats have met her in person.<br /> <br /> The chink in her armor - the fault in her web - is that she didn't always have the benefit of Technocratic telecom technology. Ergo, her earliest operations were done on the grid, with known accounts. Some of the records of her activity persist in physical form, where they can't be easily hacked and altered or expunged. Despite all her power and the Technocratic support, she has never moved since first withdrawing from the world. Meaning it's entirely possible for a persistent investigation to find out who she is and where she lives. There's a reason her home is surrounded, at all times, by Technocrat guards and agents in disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T23:53:55-07:00","id":1260400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1259659#post1259659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) If you refuse to start descending or working with Nephandi, surely the Avatar (especially if it's Avatar 5 and therefore a highly self-aware, demanding and powerful one) will oppose you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it ever happens that an Avatar goes so far in opposing a Mage to the extent that you are suggesting it can happen for a Nephandus. Where and what in M:tA books did you read that would suggest that this can happen for Mages who are Nephandi ?<br /> From what I read in the M:tA books about the Nephandi, I think that what the Nephandi initiation does to the Mage and her or his Avatar only goes so far in regards to any ( for example ) tendencies or perspectives that a Mage later has due to the initiation ; and the Nephandi initiation only goes so far in regards to changes to the Mage's relation with her or his Avatar. A Mage who is a Nephandus does not have to act in a nephandic way due to her or him being a Nephandus ; though due to how the Nephandi initiation works - and due to other reasons, like actions of other Nephandi Mages or the way the Nephandi faction functions - they will most likely be predisposed in various ways to think and act in a nephandic way, and it will be to an extent natural and ordinary ( in various ways ) for a Nephandus to act in this way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-30-2018, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-21T00:17:17-07:00","id":1261894,"title":"","content":"125) This Technocrat Mage of the Iteration-X Convention - a PC gamer and designer and a programmer from the period of his life before he Awakened and was recruited by the Technocracy - has found a viable way to be able to keep playing and modifying PC games within his actions, duties and development as a Technocrat. Through recording, cataloging, and analysing his brain activity during playing PC games while setting up intricate and complex self-limitations and challenges within the gameplay for himself , he has developed means to alter, catalyse, and adjust his thinking and feelings through a personal energy field that he has developed. This gives him the capability to carry out very potent, flexible, and efficient Mind Shield Procedures of the Mind Magick kind. Currently it is only in regard to himself that he can carry out these Procedures; but he is undertaking research that would enable him to use those Mind Shield Procedures on other persons, as well.<br /> <br /> His other Magick capabilities are Correspondence 2 and Prime 2 . He has established and defined himself as long-range information gatherer, and support for other Technocrats - both those in the field and those in their laboratories. His Mind Shields capabilities enable him to keep his intentions, plans, and actions hidden ; and to assure that any information he receives or gathers also won't be accessed by those that shouldn't know it. This safety and assurance enables him to act independently efficiently and in a significant variety of ways ; and also to aid other Technocrats more reliably , with his Correspondence 2 and Prime 2 capabilities ; and also through giving suggestions and advice, and passing important and vital information from person to person.<br /> <br /> <br /> [ This Technocrat Mage of the Iteration-X Convention has Prime 2, Mind 2 with speciality in Mind-Shielding , and Correspondence 2. ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-01-2018, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T03:29:39-07:00","id":1264000,"title":"","content":"126)<br /> <br /> Back before he Awakened and was recruited into the Technocracy, this Technocrat of the New World Order Convention wouldn't think that his theories about philosophy, the point and the goals of existence, and the universal similarities and themes woven through both the human mind, and inanimate matter and energy would contribute to changing his life to such a large and significant extent. Yet his zeal and persistence in following and delving into what might have seemed at times like obscure and irrelevant topics and ideas have truly paid of, as due to this that his eyes and mind were opened during this one day, as he was able to recognize a Technocrat he met while studying late in the library at the university he attended back then.<br /> <br /> He still remembers as he noticed a slight, but deeply characteristic quality in her gaze, and her eyes, as she gave him a cursory look while he took a place at a table next to where she was sitting. Putting aside his work, he studied this woman as she was writing notes while reading through notebooks and sheets of paper. He tried to apply his philosophical theories and ruminations to who he was seeing and what it could have meant, both in itself and in relation to what he lived through. He noticed a slight, but very distinctive soft glow around her pen as she used her Primal Energy modulator to enhance her comprehension and focus. His years of studying philosophy and thinking have prepared him to not being surprised at all, and thus he was able to keep observing the white-blue glow until it faded as the Technocrat woman expanded the Primal Energy from the battery inside the pen. This observation was the final trigger that led to him Awakening and becoming a Mage ; within five minutes of this, he mustered the courage to talk to the woman, who quickly recognized another Enlightened person. She invited him into her apartment for the night and the next few days ; and during the course of the next few weeks initiated and recruited him into the Technocracy, and the New World Order Convention.<br /> <br /> This Technocrat's background, knowledge, and insights in regard to philosophy has provided a good enough basis in regard to him comprehending the knowledge, and the practice, of Mind Procedures. What matters more to him is how philosophy has tied into his understanding of, and the ability to create and use, technology that enables him to perceive and manipulate Primal Energy. With it, he has been able to call upon Primal Energy to provide him an edge in regard to carrying out Mind Procedures, and to stabilize the results of his Mind Procedures. He also developed technology that gives him other capabilities related to Primal Energy. He is also able to perceive Primal Energy, store it in an apparatus create an idealized image of himself, energize his body, transfer Primal Energy to other Technocrats or to their apparatuses, and receive Primal Energy from other Technocrats through various means.<br /> <br /> Currently he is researching practical applications of Inspired Psychology and Inspired Philosophy in regard to resolving conflicts and disputes - those internal inside the Technocracy, and those occurring between Technocrats and other groups or individuals ; and also those that occur between individuals or groups without Technocrats being involved.<br /> <br /> <br /> [ This Technocrat Mage of the New World Order Convention has Arete 3, and Prime 3 and Mind 3. ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-01-2018, 06:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T15:46:17-07:00","id":1264506,"title":"","content":"[We never have enough Sorcerer's Crusade characters here.]<br /> <br /> <br /> 127) A priest in the ranks of the Cabal of Pure Thought, his duty often calls him to thwart sorcerers and heretics. Unbeknownst to his Convention, he carries out a heresy of his own. A small one, he swears.<br /> <br /> See, his father was a scholar and copyist working for the Catholic Church, working every day of his life to preserve humanity's stock of lore. Ever since the mage was a child, his father stressed to him the utmost importance of preserving knowledge. Especially classical texts, and written copies of oral traditions. &quot;The Lord giveth wisdom upon all folk, according to His design. Even pagan words carry a wisp of truth, if wheat be sorted from chaff. Never allow a codex or scroll or note succumb to rot or flame. For all knowledge is a gift from the Almighty. To squander it is to spit on His kindness.&quot;<br /> <br /> Such lessons the mage took to heart. Even now, when protocol demands he capture the books of Tradition mages and set them to fire, he cannot bring himself to the task. To set page to flame goes against everything he was taught. So when he takes the possessions of a felled sorcerer or loots their libraries, he does not build a pyre for them. Instead, he quietly commands secret hirelings to take these texts away. He retrieves them at his convenience, and stores them in a private property he retains, just beyond the limits of a certain city in which he's based. A stone building, covered in ivy and moss, with a secret library hidden in the basement. He even learned a few tricks from allies in the Craftmasons, so he could employ them for disguising his private storage.<br /> <br /> The Order of Reason would not understand his reticence; they consider wrong knowledge categorically harmful, and thus in need of immediate destruction. This mage disagrees. Mayhaps one day, some useful scrap of data can be derived from a Verbana witch's book of herb lore, or from a Hermetic wizard's codex of demonology. The priest is no sorcerer, and definitely no infernalist. He has no interest in their spells or blasphemies. He just supposes that it's better for the Order of Reason to have the books and not need them, rather than need them and not have them.<br /> <br /> Moreover...though his allies are loath to say so, are their mechanisms and natural philosophy not bordering, even now, upon the truly fantastic? And it would be so much easier to combat a hostile sorcerer's blandishments...if he understood them. He is a faithful man, and loves God...but the temptation to read the books is strong. God give him strength, to resist the allure of sorcery...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T11:00:39-08:00","id":1264760,"title":"","content":"128)<br /> <br /> Usually Technocrats experience working with and learning from members of their own Convention before they take part in cooperative efforts with Technocrats of Conventions other than their own. This member of the Iteration-X is an exception to this, as she took part in joint effort of Technocrats of different Conventions ( The Iteration-X and the New World Order ) in the very situation that she Awakened ; and has kept doing this since her recruitment into the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> She still remembers it clearly and vividly. After finishing university with Ph.D. s in physics and materials science, she started working in a superconductor and magnetic materials research facility; that unbeknownst to her was used by Technocrats as a base of operations and testing facility. At the end of her work shift she, due to tiredness, absent-mindely went into a room where two Technocrats were observing results of latest tests and tuning the machines and aperture to the new results and calculations based off them. Her entering this Technocratic facility was only possible because the Technocrats, due to tiredness, left the automatic door on a let-in-anyone setting.<br /> Upon seeing her they, also due to tiredness, assumed that she was a research assistant knowingly working for the Technocracy, as only such person would be let in by the doors on the usual setting. Immediately after her entering the Technocratic facility a situation - a little crisis - presented itself.<br /> Due to mistakes made by the member of the New World Order Convention in accessing the new data, the resonance regulators and chronoscopic sensors at the facility become desynchronized. This caused appearance of chronal anomalies - ghostly images and voices of the two Technocrats from the five previous minutes ; and also resulted in a rapid loss of data from the data storage servers. The member of the Iteration-X sought to stabilize the situation, but she needed another person to operate the technology. Not only was the member of the N.W.O unsuccessful in helping his fellow Technocrat ; his actions actually hastened the ongoing loss of data and caused further desynchronization of the aperture ; resulting in a disruption of overall functioning of the technology in the little Technocratic research facility.<br /> <br /> At the same moment, both Technocrats looked at her, as if expecting her to do something - while at the same time realizing that they don't have an idea of who she is, what is her expertise or skills, and how she can help. The member of the New World Order gave her a long look, then went back to unsuccessfully trying to bring a semblance of order to the fluctuating settings of the technology in the facility. Maybe it is true to a large extent that the Technocrat of the Iteration-X Convention is responsible for her Awakening, as she encouraged the young scientist to take actions with a slight smile - as she realized that the young researcher was an uninitiated scientist from the larger mundane facility - and an amused sum-up.<br /> -Well, by the rate it is going, and as far as I know him, this is going to take more than one person to sort out and fix what he did.<br /> Followed by words spoken in a more serious tone.<br /> -Will you help with this? If you only stand next to me, listen carefully, and observe what is happening, I can get you through the basics. If you have any questions in regard to the matter at hand, do ask.<br /> <br /> The trust given to her by a senior scientist, the blue-and-green glow of data screens, the slight, clean humming of technology, the clearly defined task ahead, and the mystique of the situation to her - all of this combined into her becoming Enlightened during the next fifteen-or-so minutes. The young scientist's Enlightenment occurred as he Iteration-Xer explained to her how to operate devices and technology for carrying out Matter 1 and Forces 1 Procedures ; so that the machines could be monitored, in order to identify and prevent any malfunctions and problems, while the technology was adjusted and set back into the usual configurations. Not only was the newly Awakened scientists able to understand and carry out Matter 1 and Forces 1 Procedures ; much to the Iteration-Xer's surprise, she was able to quickly grasp the analysis, assumptions, and calculations required for carrying out Time 1 Procedures. This made it possible for her to monitor the situation of chronal technology in the facility while she calculated and inputted the correct data and settings to deal with the desynchronized premature and the chronal anomalies ; the Iteration-Xer also managed to restore the entirety of lost data. Meanwhile the member of the New World Order was literally taking notes, trying to both comprehend and memorize how to operate the technology in the facility.<br /> The crisis in this Technocratic facility was dealt with easily within a few minutes. Within the next few hours, the two Technocrats brought out food and drinks, and were well into convincing, fact after fact, of the existence, capabilities, and influence of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Three months haven't passed, since her Awakening and subsequent recruitment into the Technocracy, and this novice Iteration-Xer is already cooperating with members of the New World Order, in regard to development of Enlightened Science and in regard to resolving situations ; using primarily her skills in regard to Time Enlightened Science. While doing research and work within the Iteration-X Convention, she focuses on Matter Enlightened Science and Forces Enlightened Science. She hopes to be able to keep aiding the N.W.O in the future, without this ever being a problem in regard to her achieving her goals and presenting satisfactory results as a Technocrat of the Iteration-X Convention.<br /> <br /> <br /> [ This Technocrat Mage has Arete 3, and Time 2, Matter 2, and Forces 1. ]<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1264506#post1264506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> [We never have enough Sorcerer's Crusade characters here.]</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, more Dark Ages characters - and from time periods other than the modern one - would be good additions to this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-19-2018, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T17:56:17-08:00","id":1264843,"title":"","content":"129) He is called the Sleep Buster, for he is the enemy of all slumber.<br /> <br /> A Marauder, he began as a psychologist in the early 20th century. His Awakening occurred when an obsessive patient at his asylum whispered his madness into the doctor's ear. Or perhaps the Marauder <i>was</i> the patient. He is too far gone, now, to adequately recall. All he knows is that the inmate feared to sleep, for he had dreams. Dreams of...things, from the realm of sleep. Things that wanted to break him. To make him the servant of their dreaming lord. And to use him as a gateway through which their kind could enter the waking world. These maddened ramblings brought the doctor - or the patient - to an Awakening, and to a Quiet from which he has never recovered.<br /> <br /> Whether he was a doctor to begin with, or picked up the knowledge later, the Sleep Buster wanders the world, maintaining a series of hidden laboratories. He believes fully in the ramblings of that raving lunatic, from that asylum, long ago. There is another world - a world of sleep and dreams - filled with beings that desperately want to gain access to the material plane. He believes they use sleeping people as bridges to cross over, in addition to means of contacting and corrupting sleepers. To him, a sleeping person looks as though a strange, unearthly smoke rises from them, bearing an unnatural hue not of the waking world.<br /> <br /> As such, the &quot;good doctor&quot; has not slept in decades, keeping himself alive and conscious with a steady and regular cocktail of drugs, chemical baths, self-hypnotic procedures, and sonic influence. He wears a breathing mask when he is out and about, that feeds him a steady stream of gas, formulated to keep him alert. He is also armed with a selection of geometric and mathematical formulas and designs. For he believes that the anti-logic of the dream beings cannot abide the rigid order of the waking world; numerical and geometric complexity confounds them. He believes this is why humanity - almost subconsciously - designed their cities with rigid order in mind. The better to protect themselves from the dream things, so they may achieve restful sleep...if there is such a thing. Nonetheless, there is power to be derived from the dream logic the other world operates on, and in imposing such logic on the waking world. In controlled doses, of course. Hallucinogens are useful for this purpose, he finds, for they give a person a measure of dream madness, while keeping them safe and awake.<br /> <br /> This is ultimately his purpose, and his mission. To use his research to solve the bane of slumber, and protect mankind from the dream world for good. To accomplish this, though, he needs test subjects. He often stalks the homeless and mentally ill (often times, they are the same), for they are persistent and vivid dreamers. If he can cure them of their addiction to slumber, helping the rest of humanity do the same should be a simple matter. If a few people must perish, that is the price of progress. If nothing else, the dead cannot dream.<br /> <br /> He is greatly distressed by seeing anyone asleep in his presence, and will attempt to wake them, and keep them awake, if at all possible. Humanity has been sleeping for millennia - collectively and frequently - so he has much progress to make up. A great deal of ground to cover, to stymie the efforts of his dreamworld foes and their abominable sleeping lord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 11-05-2018, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T03:22:21-08:00","id":1264914,"title":"","content":"130)<br /> <br /> This young Technocrat of the Iteration-X chose to specialize in Primal Field Theory, and uses Correspondence Procedures almost exclusively to lend her skills and expertise in regard to this ; and also to find new contacts and situations where her skills are needed. Other than providing Primal Energy for other Technocrats, she also helps them stabilize and prolong the results of their Procedures ; and aids them in regard to detecting and identifying the involvement of Mystic Mages, and of other Technocrats who don't make themselves known.<br /> It has been suggested by other Technocrats to her that she should develop knowledge and skills in regard to the more common Matter and Forces Enlightened Sciences. However, she seeks to first achieve the highly sought after expertise of Prime 5. It is her goal and aspiration because of a variety of reasons : she will be able to deal effectively with a much wider range of situations and issues ; she will be capable of developing novel means and methods of action ; and she will the competence and the ability that will enable her to explore intricate and little known avenues in research.<br /> <br /> <br /> [ This Technocrat Mage has Arete 3, and Prime 3 and Correspondence 3. ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T11:40:56-08:00","id":1268929,"title":"","content":"131)<br /> <br /> This Technocrat is a former Verbenae Apprentice who left the Traditions to join the Progenitors because he saw the intricacy of their ordered, systematic approach to unlock the myriad potential of the biological body. Or, as members of the Traditions put it - sold out to the Progenitors because he couldn't bring himself to muster the faith and the devotion required in the practices of the Verbenae. The Technocrats that know him are glad that he chose the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> The young Progenitor has benefited from his short membership in the Traditions ; his insights into Mystical Time and Entropy Magicks somehow enabled him to easily and smoothly understand the theory and comprehend the practice of little known sections ( at least to the other Conventions ) of the Progenitors' Enlightened Sciences. Thus even though the mysticism of Time and Entropy as seen by Traditions seems faded to him now, he has lost nothing of what he was capable - and in fact, through the Progenitors' methods, he has further developed his Time understanding and capabilities.<br /> <br /> This Technocrat, in addition to having the usual capabilities of a Progenitor with Life 2, also has Time 2 and Entropy 1. As part of Entropy 1, after a prepared injection of a substance he can perceive - through the senses of sight and touch - outcomes of random events ; and he can also enter a trance state which enables him to discern whether someone is being truthful. As part of treatments he gives himself periodically as part of Time 1, he can sense chronal phenomena and anomalies through touch and hearing ; he has also gained awareness of the precise internal clock that a person's own body can be. As part of his Time 2 Procedures he drinks a dose of chronal serum ; this has so far enabled him to predict the outcomes of events up to around thirty minutes into the future ; or to realize what happened in the past up to around twenty minutes before.<br /> <br /> The Technocrat is currently seeking to achieve the expertise of Life 3, in order to be able to better aid his newfound friends and colleagues at the Technocracy. Through setting this goal for himself he also seeks to focus himself, as a member of the Progenitors Convention, on a more standard course ; though after achieving the knowledge and the methods of Life 3 he might very well delve more deeply into the the Time and Entropy Enlightened Sciences.<br /> <br /> [ This Technocrat Mage has Arete 3, and Time 2, Life 2, and Entropy 1. ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-21-2018, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T05:54:45-08:00","id":1269525,"title":"","content":"132)<br /> <br /> A member of the Syndicate whose stated goal is to use his resources and capabilities to establish contacts, logistics, and resources in as many varied places in the economy, and in as many economically-involved social groups, as he reasonably can. Thus he tries to gain influence and contacts in multiple and varied business sectors, and to have a working knowledge how every part of a given industry works ; and to be involved, directly or indirectly, with the persons responsible for each branch. The reasons behind his choice is his view point that such an approach will enable him to better aid other Technocrats ; and also to be able to sort out uncommon issues and problems, and to perceive and take advantage of unusual opportunities.<br /> At the same time, he is aware that in the future he might decide \u0096- or the circumstances might force him -\u0096 to be more focused in his efforts and approach. He is slowly but steadily gathering knowledge and information in regard to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-21-2018, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T21:39:07-08:00","id":1269999,"title":"","content":"[And now for something completely different.]<br /> <br /> <br /> 133) Following the Renaissance, in the evolution of the Order of Reason into its modern incarnation - the Technocratic Union - it slowly, one by one, began to prune away the parts of itself that it no longer saw as necessary. The populist and ritualistic Craftmasons fell first, followed thereafter by the faithful of the Cabal of Pure Thought. Those members who resisted change were eliminated, while those who could be &quot;salvaged&quot; were broken and rebuilt in line with the Union's modern, secular vision. The least discussed of the Conventions who &quot;fell&quot;, however, were the Ksirafi, the &quot;Razors&quot;. The knives in the dark, that once watched Daedaleans for betrayal, gathered knowledge, and performing the dirty deeds necessary for the greater good. Those at the top of the transformed Order of Reason saw these perennial spies and closet mystics as a liability. Naturally, the Razors knew their time was up, and were accustomed to fading into the night. Their libraries were burned (save the extra secret caches). Some allowed themselves to be absorbed into what would become the New World Order, while the more mystical obtained positions in Hermetic House Janissary. The rest perished (sometimes willingly, for the sake of their secrets), or went to ground for good, in order to guard what they had for the rest of time.<br /> <br /> One Ksirafi, however, would not allow himself to simply die. He was one of their masters, and held vast stores of knowledge and experience. He went into hiding, of course, but only so long as was needed to finish his last great work. A volume of text that acted as combination biography and treatise on the Ksirafi's philosophy. Weaved into the text was an enchantment of staggering complexity. A memetic agent that, when the text was read and understood, would imprint a personality overlay on the first person to do so. The plan was to place the text in the charge of his most loyal and secret agents, who would guard it, for centuries, if need be. Until, long after the Technocratic Union had given up on finding any more Razors, they would find an initiate who displayed a personality close to the old master's. And who would be prepared to give everything - even the sanctity of his own ego - to protect the world, through any means necessary. The two persons - old master and new initiate - would become one, and rebuild their order.<br /> <br /> Naturally, no plan survives contact with the enemy. In this case, the enemy was time itself. The vagaries of age and fortune took their toll. The text was lost, the servants dying and not being replaced. Or else &quot;lost the plot&quot;, along with his resources.<br /> <br /> We pick up the &quot;plot&quot;, as it were, in the most unlikely of places: modern Japan.<br /> <br /> Among the more enthusiastic otaku circles, a young woman sat at her computer, working as a contributor to an anime fan site. Her passions included cosplay and magical girl shows, but her hidden specialty was in identifying and compiling texts the anime studios would appropriate in their productions. If a fan needed to know what the arcane glyphs being used in a show were, she was the person to go to. She'd poured over medieval European documents and familiarized herself with esoteric lore. Not because anyone asked her to, but because it provided a potent intellectual exercise.<br /> <br /> So when the anime studio got their hands on a western document for cheap - one they clearly neither understood nor cared about - they stuck the text in the show, as backdrops and space filler. Such things lent an air of sophistication to shows (not to mention were cheaper to anime than actual activity). For the sake of completion, our otaku poured over the show, frame-by-frame, in order to compile the text's contents and identify their meaning. She managed to gather enough to make sense of the text, and you see where this is going.<br /> <br /> The old master Razor never intended such a...different vessel for his knowledge and personality. The result was not so much an overlay adding itself to a like-minded vessel, so much as two radically different personas being jammed into the same head, and left to integrate as best they could. They did <i>not</i>, as one might imagine, resolve by breaking into separate personalities via dissociation, but it wasn't a clean mixture either. The sheltered young lady was inundated with visions of complex symbology and real memories of having <i>killed people</i>. Many of them. The old master, meanwhile, was baffled by modern technology, cultural trends, and the...<i>complexities</i> of being a Japanese high school girl.<br /> <br /> Indeed, it's only because she had the benefit of his experience that she didn't completely fall apart or reveal what had been done to her. If nothing else, the newly minted Razor knew how to hide her feelings and intent behind a mask. Everything was fine, she'd say. Everything was not fine, of course, but she knew to just smile and nod. She was very used to smiling; she may have been an otaku, but she loved to get into character when cosplaying at conventions. As far as she was concerned, she was just cosplaying. Full time. <i>As herself</i>.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, the amalgam of two people is quietly wrestling, not just with the cognitive dissonance between the two life experiences, but between vastly different personalities. She doesn't <i>want</i> to be playing a role all the time, just to get by. It's just that no matter how much fun she's having with friends or family, she can't help keeping a running mental record of everything they say or do around her, and making detailed notes of it later. What is he - sorry, she - supposed to do? <i>NOT</i> diligently maintain the shadowy, spy-like lifestyle honed over two centuries of life in the Order of Reason? On the other hand, she finds herself emotionally confused all the time, as the Ksirafi's detachment from interpersonal investment is challenged by her genuine, youthful desire for friendship, love, and validation? How is that old man supposed to react to the desire to get with boys?<br /> <br /> For that matter, why does their Daemon - the grim and warlike angel - now appear in visions as positively...<i>bishonen</i>!?<br /> <br /> On one matter, however, the two sides of this coin agree. They do not like the Technocratic Union. She finds their dismissal of magic and wonder to be repellent, and their abuses of common people to be obscene. He, meanwhile, still holds a grudge against the group that abandoned their roots and disregard the angels of their better nature, not to mention cast out their most loyal members when they were not longer convenient.<br /> <br /> So recently, the Tradition chantries of Japan have a new arrival. An orphan with a strangely broad - if inconsistent and archaic - understanding of Hermetic praxis. Out in Japan, no Order of Hermes members in the region are intimately familiar with the works of the now decimated House Janissary, so they presume she's a mere self-taught magician. A magus with some potential, perhaps, if educated in proper Hermetic forms. She's certainly bizarre, though, for a Hermetic. Then again, chantries throughout the world are no strangers to oddballs.<br /> <br /> Exactly what she's counting on. She may appear like just an otaku who learned all her praxis from anime, but that's only because she keeps all her deepest arts - and more subtle Ksirafi tricks - in her back pocket, to be employed in secret and at a time and place of her choosing. She observes her new colleagues - old habits die hard - but is really interested in learning about the Technocrats in her city. As well as making sure that no infiltrators from the Union can act unnoticed within the Traditions's ranks. That she's a flamboyant and, shudder, cute personality is just one more tool in her arsenal. No one would suspect the chantry member that comes in wearing cat ears and tail to be observing anything, let alone be an actual <i>threat</i>.<br /> <br /> In short, she's an emotionally conflicted magical girl, who just happens to be knowledgeable in centuries old techniques of subterfuge and assassination. Her cosplay costumes all come equipped with places to hide blades, potions, poisons, lockpicks, and grappling hooks. She's compassionate and loving, unless provoked, where she can dispatch a foes with cold, detached efficiency...and then cry about it later. It would almost be funny, if she wasn't the most dangerous otaku this side of the Virtual Adept hacking scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 11-23-2018, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T18:05:58-08:00","id":1271644,"title":"","content":"134. A Hermetic graffiti artist. Most of his effects involve spray painting occult symbols disguised as graffiti. An example is his &quot;Break-neck Tag&quot;. When he's being chased he quickly sprays it on the ground. The next person to pass over it will trip and fall badly. Perfectly coincidental, they must have slipped on the wet paint.<br /> <br /> 135. There were witchcraft traditions that focused on fairies. And fairies are nothing but the European equivalent of nature spirits. Let's forget about C:tD for a moment, how about Dreamspeaker based in Western fae folklore? One of her main foci is a garden gnome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T13:31:30-08:00","id":1271834,"title":"","content":"136)<br /> <br /> This Verbenae Mage has been spending much less time delving into the intricacies of Life Magick than she intended to spend when she Awakened, less than two months ago. But this is not due to her losing interest or encountering difficulties. She just didn't have the time to do it, as the recent weeks were completely taken by her experimenting and discovering how much potential, in regard to opening up her perception and senses, is in potion making. During the past weeks, every few days, she was amazed how through following intuition and through careful considerations, she could devise new methods to make mixtures in order to achieve the results that she had in mind.<br /> <br /> The concoction with which she started as a Mage is one of herbs and flowers gently boiled in her small cauldron, and it allows her to perceive Life Patterns. By adding a few herbs to this potion, she can access the possibilities of Life 2. The next potion one that the Mage devised opens up her sight to the Patterns of Matter, and it is made by heating, each one separately, selected gems and random stones picked up in the forest ( the gems are kept and reused in each potion, while the stones are not ) , and putting them one by one into slowly heated water of her cauldron. Her sense and perception of Time is due to a mixture that is made from roots of obscure plants handpicked by her ; the roots are kept in very cold water in strict intervals of 58 to 62 seconds ; this is done multiple times to properly release the roots' essence. The witch channels Prime Magick through an elixir made by boiling ripe fruits - a slightly different selection each time - in a fire fueled by wood into which runes devised by her are carved. Her Correspondence Sense is stimulated through a potion made of herbs and old branches found on the ground ; the water and the ingredients are slowly heated as the cauldron is moved to nine separate places in her Sanctum during the process.<br /> <br /> She can cast Conjunctional Magick either through creating a mixed concotion, or by mixing potions made separately. The Verbenae usually drinks her potions at the start of the day, and this allows her to use her Magick for the next few days.<br /> <br /> [ This Verbenae Mage has Arete 3, and Life 2, Prime 1, Time 1, Matter 1, Correspondence 1. ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 11-29-2018, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T14:04:29-08:00","id":1272041,"title":"","content":"137)<br /> <br /> Sometimes a passionate romance between lovers leads to a quick marriage ; and sometimes a passionate romance leads to a young Technocrat ending up doing more assignments for other Conventions, than he does for his own Convention. This young member of the Iteration-X, due to insistence from his paramour ( she is from the Syndicate ) has volunteered for field assignments and directed his progress as an Enlightened Scientist towards practice and theory pertinent to the field work he has been part of. This way, the two lovers will be able to spend more time together. For this it was certainly worth going off the previously planned track - in order to learn Prime and Correspondence Enlightened Sciences, and to specialize his expertise in Forces in regard to electricity. The young Technocrat's current priority in regard to Enlightened Science is to reach Prime 2.<br /> <br /> The assignments are almost entirely about sabotaging - and much less often, repairing - electrical systems and technology. Sometimes the Iteration-Xer is also asked to also perform observation and reconnaissance of a location and it's technology. The sabotaging is done through Forces Procedures, and his basic knowledge of Matter and Correspondence Procedures greatly helps him in this. The sabotages have so far been requested by members of two Conventions - the New World Order and the Syndicate. They find them very useful as an event to happen at a location, in order to aid in accomplishing specific goal(s) . The Iteration-Xer either does the sabotages ( and repairs ) while under a cover identity, or he enters or breaks in into a location in secrecy while it is closed.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the point of an arranged technology malfunction or failure is so that a repair crew consisting partly or entirely of Technocracy's agents, or Technocrats, will be called. Once they are at a location, they can perform a number of actions - installing and placing technology for future use, performing preparations for carrying out Procedures later, industrial espionage, establishing contacts, sabotage, data retrieval, data removal, observation. There is a variant in this option, in which the technology malfunction is caused in such a way so that a regular repair crew will be at a loss what to do ; thus an opening is created for a repair crew sent or influenced by the Technocracy to arrive, deal with the issue, and right at start have an established positive opinion. Sometimes the point of a malfunction is to cause ( or contribute towards ) a removal or a demotion of a specific person ( or persons ) in a company ; this is sometimes done so that a person working for the Technocracy will be put in a particular position. Sometimes a malfunction is needed so a person or a company will need money, or some service done or materials delivered, that will lead them to contacting and meeting Technocrats from the Syndicate ( or their agents ) who will &quot;just happen to have&quot; an offer or a suggestion. Sometimes it is very simple - a malfunction is requested so that a location will be closed for a time ; or so that the time or attention of specific persons will be taken away from other matters. The methods and means of the Technocracy are intricate and varied ; the expertise of this young Technocrat is excellent in regard to creating openings through which other Technocrats can then act.<br /> <br /> [ This Technocrat Mage has Arete 3, and Forces 3 ( Speciality: Electricity ) , Prime 1, Matter 1, Correspondence 1. ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-04-2018, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T02:11:05-08:00","id":1277469,"title":"","content":"138) A Verbenae Mage who has decided to spent equal amount of times in the city, and in forests and the countryside. Sometimes she changes it day to day, and sometimes it is patterns of for example three days, four days, four days, three days. She reasons that this will teach her a lot about appriaciating the nature; and also in regard to persons who live in the cities, and about how to convince persons from the cities to spend more time being closer to nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-30-2018, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T19:52:37-08:00","id":1278231,"title":"","content":"139) In his childhood, he nearly drowned when his family's boat was caught in a storm. The experience gave him a long-abiding fear of water, persisting into adulthood. To the point where his sleep was often plagued by nightmares, bringing him back to those moments of violent, crashing waves and suffocating submersion. But there always seemed like a malign, Primordial will behind the water that haunted his dreams, and that he felt inhabited the waters of the waking world. A force alive and aware of him, hidden in the crushing depths.<br /> <br /> Until one day, when he was an adult, that someone he loved was cast into the water, in danger of drowning. Despite his terror, he cast himself into the drink, to save them. In those moments, completely immersed in the water, he felt strangely one with it. It spoke to him. Not in words, but in a profound awareness that registered in his core. For indeed, was his body not mostly water? He sensed the currents around him, and felt the vibrations of his loved one thrashing in the deep. When they emerged to land again, he was changed. Awakened. That night, he dreamed of the ocean again, but this time a calm one. The still sea spoke to him, and he was at last ready to listen.<br /> <br /> An Elementalist who specializes in water, he traveled around as an Orphan for a time, learning what he could from communing with water, until he met and joined the Verbana. They, too, had a long history with the elements, and counted him as another of their kind. A person who retreated from the world, to learn from nature. He learned how to shape and control water. How to heal with it...and how to destroy. He even learned how to use it to focus his mind, making it as still as a pond or as mighty as a torrent. And he learned that all water is connected, and that these connections can be exploited across distance. His implements are simple and primal. Bodily fluids. Cups and containers. A staff, hollowed out like long straw. Meditation fully immersed in water. And all manner of uses for water, from sprinkling and washing to drinking and splashing.<br /> <br /> He has taken to the task of combating the Consensus. Not merely to smash it, but to erode it. A pragmatic man, he does not limit himself to any one method of undermining Technocratic control, but flows in where opportunities present themselves. Even a small crack can let the water in, which can widen the hole over time. Some of his preferred tactics are to enter facilities dressed as a worker there to restock drink machines or water coolers. Or to trip fire alarms, so automatic sprinkler systems go off and cause both havoc and distraction. Why blow up buildings, when breaking a pipe and letting water damage do the work in a more subtle way? If pressed into a fight, he prefers to emulate the waves; employing hit and fade tactics, he will crash and recede, minimizing harm to himself while wearing down his opponents. Obscuring mists help greatly for this task, and &quot;fog machines&quot; are a known quantity, that make the trick Coincidental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T14:56:59-08:00","id":1291974,"title":"","content":"[How about one for The Sorcerer's Crusade?]<br /> <br /> <br /> 140) A strange mix of Explorator and Grand Financier - or rather a renegade member thereof - this pirate uses the Art of Desire, along with a couple of trinkets bought, borrowed, salvaged, or stolen from various native tribes (because heck, it worked for them, so there's probably something to it). Adept with a cutlass and fleet of foot, he's a more or less typical example of a swashbuckling mage. Charming his way through life and around the law, with a pleasant smile, a witty retort, and a stylish set of clothing (long coat, wide-brimmed hat, knee-high boots).<br /> <br /> What sets him apart is his particular fixation on money. Treasure is not merely a means to an end, with him, but an end unto itself. Not merely because of greed - though he'd say he had a &quot;healthy&quot; appreciation for coin - but because he measures his mystical might by the size of his hoard. Like an exploration age dragon gone sailing, he ties his material wealth to some greater, immaterial quality like magic. He doesn't need to keep all his treasure on him, though he keeps no few coins on hand at all times. But they must be claimed and stashed by him. For the sake of protecting the wealth (and the power that follows with it), he avoids putting all his eggs in one basket. Spreading his hoard out in chests buried throughout the Caribbean, so it cannot all be claimed by happenstance or mutinous crew.<br /> <br /> When he needs to perform a big rite, he guides his ship to one of these sites, hauling the chests up and incorporating the treasure in the ritual somehow. Whatever strikes his fancy, or from wisps of occult practice he witnesses from other mages. Sometimes, a &quot;Ritual&quot; for him might take the form of that classic High Guild staple: meticulously counting coin. If he's so inclined, he can spend the coin, which can serve its own magickal function. A coin slipped into the pocket of a crew member can embolden them to work harder. A coin under the table can sway a guard or colonial governor. A coin may even carry a potent hex, that sticks to the target so long as he hangs on to it. He's loath to part with treasure unnecessarily, though he's more attached to his skin than to any loot. After all, he can just steal it back later if he must.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T04:02:11-07:00","id":1300793,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\">141) Agent Charlotte Miles, Psionic Union Operative</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sect: Technocratic Union</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Convention: New World Order</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Paradigm:</span><br /> <br /> Consciousness is the only true reality, so we must transcend our limits.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Practice:</span><br /> <br /> Psionics, Martial Arts<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Instruments:</span><br /> <br /> Eye Contact (mind control, emotional control, sensory rolls directed at other people, projecting psychic interference and attacks, emphasis on Mind)<br /> <br /> Meditation (mental self-improvement, access to mind palace, emphasis on Mind)<br /> <br /> Social Domination (standard NWO fare; intimidation, showing off licenses and warrants, &quot;the office I work for doesn't even exists as far as you're concerned, just give me what I need officer&quot;)<br /> <br /> Thought-Forms (the core of her practice; used for everything from Forces attacks to altering outcomes of dice rolls)<br /> <br /> Weapons (used as part of her psychic focus when attacking someone; everything from tasers to guns)<br /> <br /> (Dances) and Movements (martial art techniques; her understanding of the nervous system and psychic reality is holistic. We're not &quot;just our minds&quot;, at least not in a way that discounts our bodies. Our bodies, our senses, and our movements are a very important part of our mental reality. Therefore martial art techniques play a key role in her practice, allowing her to focus her mind. Emphasis on Forces)<br /> <br /> Drugs and Poisons (empowering herself with Union-approved psychostimulants; when she develops Prime 2 these will be how she makes Charms/Gadgets; emphasis on Mind and Life)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Spheres:</span><br /> <br /> Mind (Affinity, will always be higher than her other spheres, and forms the justification for many of her effects in and of itself, from psychokinesis to pyrokinesis and mind-reading)<br /> <br /> Forces (emphasis on movement and temperature because of 'psionic hypernarratives' in the public consciousness (mythic threads), but she is only limited here by her own understanding; as she improves she'll realize that she could just as easily turn sound into light as she can make particles vibrate)<br /> <br /> Prime (never higher than 2; emphasis on making Gadgets which are mental stimulants and awaken her full psionic potential. Also the source of pyrokinesis, naturally, along with other aggravated forms of attack. Prime 1 senses allow her to &quot;see&quot; deviant effects with her powers)<br /> <br /> Spirit... maybe (this is where things start getting slightly deviant; what do you do when your agent starts seeing &quot;Ghosts&quot; that don't fit into Union practice? Fear of being unmutual because of what your powers let you sense can always lead to good conflict)<br /> <br /> Correspondence (psionic 'scrying', eventually even understanding that a person's position in the universe is a matter of subjective thought that is open to mental editing)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Merits, Backgrounds and Stuff:</span><br /> <br /> Set Willpower high, maybe even up to 10, since it's so important in psionic practice.<br /> <br /> Clear-Sighted merit; simply melt through all illusions. Very fitting for the concept.<br /> <br /> Enchanting Feature merit; eyes. -2 difficulty to all effects using Eyes as the focus since they're a Unique/Specialized instrument.<br /> <br /> Acute Senses merit, the 3 point version. Hyper-alertness is a good talent for a psychic.<br /> <br /> Mental merits can always be purchased later as required; Concentration and Iron Will might be especially useful.<br /> <br /> Avatar 3+, Demesne 1+, Node 1+.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Attributes, Abilities:</span><br /> <br /> Mental Primary, invest abilities into Alertness, Awareness, Empathy, Intimidation, Martial Arts, Meditation, Esoterica or Science (Psionics), Technology, Computer, Drive, Enigmas, Investigation, Law, Politics, Medicine, Firearms... There are a lot of dots to go around. Priority should be 1 dot in each, with 3 in things like Esoterica/Science and Martial Arts and Meditation if possible.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Roleplay:</span><br /> <br /> Things got weird when you started having the strange dreams. You'd wake up only to find half the objects in your room in a pile, or thrown up into every corner. You saw a therapist over your &quot;sleepwalking habit&quot; and it didn't get better; one night you turned the stove on, and it was only found in the morning. This persisted even after the use of sleeping restraints; the only conclusion your parents could reach is that you were putting them back on before going back to sleep. Eventually your claims that you could make things move if you concentrated hard enough drew the attention of a consultant psychiatrist specializing in children with abnormal delusions... officially. From this moment on you were a Union interest, and a good deal of work was put into justifying, quantifying and rationalizing your power. No, no, not a Deviant. Simply a type of Science which is poorly understood. Psionic powers in a latent state, expressing themselves randomly since they lack a proper channel of use. Your powers were trained until you reached adulthood and became an agent.<br /> <br /> In terms of personality, you're a very optimistic and friendly servant of the Union. Your experience with the Union has been very positive, and you believe everything you've been told (both true and untrue). You're discreet with your powers since you fear being labeled as &quot;unmutual&quot; by more closed-minded colleagues. You are rarely still or totally silent, and invest a lot of time in solving puzzles and playing with fidget toys (a crutch you were taught as a child, to minimize the risk of psionic activity by keeping your mind occupied).<br /> <br /> To you, a gunshot is a warning, not an attack. A threat of arrest or legal trouble is a tool to get compliance. There are ways of applying your own psychic manifestations (SURRENDER, NOW) without scaring or confusing the masses. You'd be completely devastated if you were forced to kill someone, and when it comes to lethal violence you're still relatively untested... essentially you're a slightly naive idealist who has only seen the good side of the Union. Now, enter whatever plot the ST has in mind and allow that idea to slowly decay and perhaps even shatter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-29-2019, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T04:05:34-07:00","id":1300794,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\">&quot;Curious, is the trap-maker's art. His efficacy unwitnessed by his own eyes.&quot;<br /> - The Ancestor, <i>The Darkest Dungeon</i></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> 142) This Artificer comes to be known as the Trapmaster, for his expertise in setting ingenious traps and installing them in creative ways. He's not only learned in mechanisms, but in poisons and other chemical arts. If there's a clever (or ridiculous) trap installed in an Order of Reason building, it's either his handiwork or someone emulating/copying his work.<br /> <br /> Chests that open up to reveal spring-loaded crossbows or knock-out gas canisters. Doorknobs or latches that jut out envenomed needles when not correctly opened. Letters coated in fine, toxic powders that come off on fingers or get inhaled to foil interception. Pressure plates that activate all sorts of mechanisms embedded in the walls/floors/ceilings. Valuable objects coated in a dye that is clear on its own, but which takes on a hue when it contact with skin oils; thieves often get caught <i>literally</i> red handed. And countless, countless death traps, primed and waiting to catch the Order's enemies unaware.<br /> <br /> The Trapmaster travels from city to city, across Europe and some parts of Africa and the Holy Land, at the request of Daedaleans looking to beef up their security. The Craftmasons, in particular, are always happy to see him appear. Asking him to teach their architects how to build and hide such traps in their structures.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the Trapmaster is a consummate professional, with a high personal standard of quality. He considers a trap that cannot stand the test of time a failure. His mastery of Matter allows him to create mechanisms that can wait, primed and ready, for years without degrading. Indeed, even in modern times - long after his death - certain lost and forgotten Order of Reason objects and locations harbor deadly hazards.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T23:26:24-07:00","id":1310935,"title":"","content":"143) A certain Master Mage, coming upon a point in his life where (presumably) he would either Ascend, become an Oracle, or die, bid a hasty farewell to his apprentice and his Cult. The cult - a group of adherents to Winter, called the Silent Circle - were informed that their leader's apprentice would come to shepherd them in the master's absence. A man who knew their ways and could lead them farther along the path to knowledge and enlightenment.<br /> <br /> This character is not that apprentice. Rather, he's an accidental impostor who stumbled into the role.<br /> <br /> The character in question was an Orphan, whose primary experience was in metal and fire, both literal and figurative. As such, his current arts, while fairly Elemental in practice (and Practice), lent themselves more to Craftwork and practical Effects, rather than the contemplative esoterics of the Silent Circle. Merely their elemental affinities were at odds - fire and metal versus cold, darkness, and silence - leading him and them with little in common.<br /> <br /> How, then, did he become their leader? Well, the craft-mage was an old friend and correspondent to the master's apprentice. The craft-mage knew the winter arts existed, but not much else. When he visited the apprentice's home, he found his friend murdered, his cold hands still clutched around a letter from the master and a pendent by which the Silent Circle would identify their new leader. Realizing that he could do nothing for his friend, the craft-mage left, not wishing to become embroiled in a forthcoming police investigation. Making his way to the lair of the Silent Circle - intending to brief them on the tragedy - his brandishing the pendant instead gave the cultists the impression that he was the man they waited for. The &quot;emissary and voice of he who became as one with the silence&quot;. Not the most adept at using his tongue, the craft-mage could not clear the misunderstanding, and it would soon be too awkward to correct (not to mention dangerous, if he was seen as a murderer and charlatan). So, an Emissary-And-Voice he would have to become.<br /> <br /> Naturally, he knows barely anything about the rites and ethos of the cult. He is a stranger to their ways. As such, his current preoccupation is in tracking down as much as he could about winter magic, to sell his role as expert. His old friend's collected notes might have helped, if the man's property hadn't been taken by the bank and sold off piece-meal. Even just tracking down where all the books went will be difficult enough, let alone keeping one step ahead of his cultists in studying them. He must, also, become very adept at faking his expertise, lest the cultists revolt or, worse, give and scatter to the four winds.<br /> <br /> Perhaps he feels partly responsible for his friend's death. Or perhaps he just doesn't want to see harm come to these poor people. Whatever the case, he wants to live up to their expectations and keep the Silent Circle together. That, and to find out who killed his friend and why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T11:37:15-07:00","id":1312609,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">&quot;Fire and water, earth and sky</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\">Mysteries surround us, legends never die&quot;<br /> -Blackmore's Night, <i>Locked Within The Crystal Ball</i></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> 144) Attend the tale, if you please, of the Knightess Io, Saga-Born. Again. And again. And again.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Tragic History of Io Four-Coloured&quot; is a saga hidden from Sleeper history, but known to the Awakened, if only in reference. The story was a poetic account of the life of the titular Io of Four Colours, a witch-knight from the time after the fall of the western Roman empire. Bards carried the story from land to land, and it was even written down a few times. Whether through simple misfortune or concerted effort by this or that Mage group, the original saga was lost to history. Elements of the tale persisted only through fragmentary retellings and references recorded by scholars in the Order of Hermes and Choir Celeste. Notably, the conclusion of the saga remains lost, hinting at a climactic battle with Io's great nemesis and occasional consort, Thomas the Black (although &quot;Thomas of Dusk&quot; is considered a more accurate translation).<br /> <br /> Eventually, authors here and there took what they knew of Io's story and created their own versions, filling gaps and interpreting as fit their vision. Church writers painted Io with a Christian brush. Her traits as a passionate lover were scrubbed off, depicting her as a chaste and virtuous maiden. Io made into a holy saint rather than a elemental witch, her retinue of nature spirits that followed her into battle reinterpreted as an angelic host. This vision of the Io - now called the Brilliant - became the basis of centuries of further retellings, each time drifting her characterization in whatever way fit the purposes of the day. The story of Io was never as famous as the Arthurian Cycle, but authors and playwrights who looked to obscure sources could find inspiration in this Knightess.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to the present day, where a modern fantasy author took her own crack at portraying Io. The trilogy of novels became popular enough to spawn a quadrilogy of films (naturally, the third book was split in half). Audiences ate up the fantasy series. Critics took note of the Feminist interpretation of a &quot;classic story&quot; (that barely anyone had heard of outside literature circles and theater nerds). LGBT circles praised the bold move to turn &quot;Black Tom&quot; into &quot;Black Tam&quot;, while firmly emphasizing the oft-neglected romance between Io and her erstwhile foe. Traditionalist mages merely shrugged, seeing another populist fantasy that is both an effort by the Syndicate to profit off mysticism AND another gateway for new traditionalist recruits.<br /> <br /> It took a while before Mages realized that this latest incarnation seemed to spawn a flesh-and-blood Four-Coloured Io. The Legend lives again.<br /> <br /> Io arrived on the scene, profoundly confused about who she was and how she got there. Was she a Sleeper whose memory of her former life got washed away in the chaos of a harsh Awakening? Or did the magnitude of popular imagination about the character cause Reality to, somehow, spit her into existence ex nihilo? What IS known is that she came equipped with a Focus from the outset, one that emulates but doesn't copy the popular conception of Io Four-Coloured's magic. Her powers were both holy - that of Faith - but also pagan - Witchcraft. Combined with Martial Arts, and she was a Saint-Witch-Knight. A profoundly confusing Paradigm and Practice to be sure, especially for her.<br /> <br /> Moreover, Io seemed bound by a strange destiny. One in line with her Legend. Scholars of the character she emulates/is an incarnation of point out that events surrounding her since her appearance hew closest, thematically, to what is known of the original saga. Her life is playing out her Legend as it was first told.<br /> <br /> While in general she studies the many versions of herself that have existed in story, her specific goal is to find all she can about the first saga. Chasing down leads, picking up fragments, and trying to see if somewhere, out there, exists a complete transcription of the sage. If Io is truly Saga-Born, as she supposes, knowing how that story ends will help her understand where he life is headed. And whether it's possible to avert tragedy. In the meantime, she looks backward, peeling back layers of interpretation to find her &quot;core essence&quot;.<br /> <br /> But she's not alone in the world. Io the Brilliant - the Four-Coloured - had a supporting cast. Friends, allies, lovers, and enemies. While these roles fit into her Legend on a fluid basis, she has her own Black Tom...or, rather, Black Tam. Is this a fangirl of the modern story, looking to force herself into Io's life? Or is she a true reincarnation of Thomas of Dusk? In the world of Magick - where symbols and stories have as much or more power than anything else - is there even any difference? More troubling, some Awakened scholars posit that Thomas of Dusk (the historical figure) might have been a Nephandus. Is this true, and if so does this mean &quot;Black Tam&quot; cannot be redeemed? Does Io Saga-Born even want to try? Could she resist doing so, even if she wanted to? Or is Io doomed to play out their ill-fated romance and rivalry, before it comes to an unknown but tragic end?<br /> <br /> What is clear is that Io Saga-Born has complex feelings. About her life. About her story. About (and FOR) Black Tam. Even about the force of Destiny itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 05-16-2019, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-06T02:46:41-07:00","id":1316786,"title":"","content":"[Haven't done a quick-fire list of career Sorcerers in a while. Let's rectify that.]<br /> <br /> <br /> 145) A high class escort, this user of Fascination uses her magic to leave a lasting impression on clients. That way, they leave generous tips (and not the sexual kind; she's strictly Escort only), and hire her again. Not because she's money-grubbing, but to support her child as a single mother. The father - a mysterious stranger from what seems like a lifetime ago - taught her magic, before disappearing as suddenly as he came. Before taking a job, she uses Divination, reading an antique deck of Tarot cards for signs of danger. It's perilous out there, for a person in her line of work. It pays to know the score.<br /> <br /> <br /> 146) A wandering mask salesman, who carries a bulging backpack full of his wares from location to location. Few have ever seen his face, behind the masks he wears; fewer still advertise what they know. These days, he gets much of his business during festivals, masquerade parties, and holidays (like Mardi Gras and Halloween). Using Enchantment, he endows the ornate masks with a little magic, usually related to the mask's design. A gazelle, for nimble-footedness. A craggy stone, for endurance. A grinning clown, for comedic ability. A nondescript face, to blend into the crowd. Believing every mask has a destined wearer, he rolls dice for Divination, to track down those people who need his most special wares. When situations go south - many folk fail to appreciate the roles their new masks let them play - he uses Shapeshifting to assume the forms more fully. To others, his lion mask might make hunting easier; on his face, he <i>becomes</i> the lion.<br /> <br /> <br /> 147) A professional, itinerant gambler, using Fortune to push his luck in the right direction. He heavily varies his choice of gamble, to avoid notice. Anyone can tell when a poker player seems to win too much for just skill to explain. When he works horse races one day, football the next, and some dice after that, it's hard to get a handle on a pattern. He uses both sides of Fortune, depending on the situation. Boosting luck or laying a curse, either works. If there's one bet he loves to make, though, it's about whether it will rain. His preferred tactic is to sidle up behind someone at a public place (bar, diner, etc) where the weather forecast is displayed on a TV, or else someone is checking on their phone. Whatever the forecast says will happen, he bets the opposite will happen. Not many take the bait these days, but some are so sure of the forecast that they think they can make easy money. They don't realize the stranger making the bet is learned in Weathercrafting, and so <i>makes</i> his bet come true. He just pockets the money, and everyone else assumes the strange man was just lucky.<br /> <br /> <br /> 148) Grandmother to a rich extended family, this old lady is a wizard with knitting needles. Literally. Drawing upon many folk spells gathered over years, she weaves Enchantments into the articles of yarnwork she produces, muttering a chant under her breath to tie up the bonds of fate and Fortune. Members of her family all regularly receive the products of her labors, which they have slowly learned to cherish. A sweater that seems really good at keeping away even the most bitter cold (yet doesn't seem too warm, either). Scarves that give good luck, or that aid in memory retention (great for students about to take tests). Oven mitts that, when worn, seem to make food taste all the better. Socks decorated with tree patterns, that seem to root the wearer in place and keep them from falling over (her football-playing grandson never plays a game without them). A set of baby's clothes, that the baby always seems less prone to accidental harm when wearing. Even a tiny dog's sweater, that is so precious, people seem compelled to dote on and feed the canine when they're wearing it. Speaking of food, the grandma loves to send baked goods along to her family. Goods that carry with them a subtle magic of their own. When asked, she always says that she knows a great many recipes, that call for a variety of herbs and other special ingredients. They are always delicious, and always coveted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T18:41:13-07:00","id":1320189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1316786#post1316786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">146) A wandering mask salesman, who carries a bulging backpack full of his wares from location to location. Few have ever seen his face, behind the masks he wears; fewer still advertise what they know. These days, he gets much of his business during festivals, masquerade parties, and holidays (like Mardi Gras and Halloween). Using Enchantment, he endows the ornate masks with a little magic, usually related to the mask's design. A gazelle, for nimble-footedness. A craggy stone, for endurance. A grinning clown, for comedic ability. A nondescript face, to blend into the crowd. Believing every mask has a destined wearer, he rolls dice for Divination, to track down those people who need his most special wares. When situations go south - many folk fail to appreciate the roles their new masks let them play - he uses Shapeshifting to assume the forms more fully. To others, his lion mask might make hunting easier; on his face, he <i>becomes</i> the lion.</div> </div> </div> </div> This sounds uncomfortably similar to the <i>Happy Mask Salesman.</i><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-22T19:28:10-07:00","id":1320191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/893464-1001-interesting-character-ideas?p=1320189#post1320189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This sounds uncomfortably similar to the <i>Happy Mask Salesman.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This person gets it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T01:29:48-07:00","id":1396625,"title":"","content":"149) Victorian Children of Knowledge mage, a neurotic woman trying to balance her pursuit of the Great Work with the duties of being a good, middle class wife and mother.<br /> <br /> Born to a family with a noble history (now gone stagnant and fallen on relatively hard times), she grew up a sickly child. Unable to go out and play like normal children, she spent much of her youth reading from her family's extensive library. These included alchemical texts, and by the time she came of age, she had Awoken. Her understanding of Life allowed her to finally improve her chronic health - if not her nervous disposition - and her parents used her miraculous improvement to put her &quot;on the market&quot; for a husband. Knowledgeable in deeper mysteries though she was, decorum demanded she be married.<br /> <br /> To her relief, she eventually found a suitor she connected with. A young man who shared the young lady's interest in history and plants, and alone among his fellow suitors knew how to sooth her anxiety. The two fell in love, and were soon married. He's one of the only people who know her secrets.<br /> <br /> Moving to the city of London, she tries her best to blend in and adjust to the busy city life. She fell in with a circle of women her age, for it was seen as proper to have friends. Truthfully, while social situations made her uncomfortable, she found it stimulating, if not entirely interesting. She'd much rather be discussing esoteric formulas, rather than Victorian fashion. She's got her ears to the ground for other Mages.<br /> <br /> As a new mother, she has her hands full. Not that she begrudges the little miracle. She'll make sure the child grows up big and strong. Even if she has to concoct all manner of alchemical solutions.<br /> <br /> What gives her great concern, these days, is just how dangerous Victorian life is becoming. Inventions and products are churned out on assembly lines and marketed to the middle class, far faster than such things could ever be tested. Her magickal senses - particularly of Life and Matter - make her acutely aware of these hazards. Arsenic in the wallpaper, lead in the paint. Corroding natural gas pipes, poorly ventilated smoke, and infected baby bottles. Her friends think she's silly for refusing to feed with a bottle or stay too long in a poisoned room. They couldn't possibly understand the deathtraps surrounding them, even if she revealed her enhanced senses (which she dare not). Instead, she needs to navigate a minefield situated in the homes of herself and her social circle.<br /> <br /> She's slowly coming to realize that unregulated industry is to blame, and will probably need to be stopped. But that would bring her in direct conflict with the Technocratic Union, who have considerable to gain from their businesses and innovations being allowed to run unmolested (even when it directly harms the public the Union swore to protect). It's almost enough to drive a poor woman to nervous breakdown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T22:49:22-07:00","id":1407086,"title":"","content":"150) Chaos Magician with Impostor Syndrome.<br /> <br /> Started as a bit of deception. He learned about the existence of Mages, and started walking in their circles. To fit in, he started dressing as a wizard, taking on eccentric mannerisms, learned new age lingo, and started practicing stage magic. Maybe some of the Awakened knew he was fraud, maybe they didn't. He was tolerated, especially since his mundane skills and sleight of hand were useful. He himself always knew he was putting on a front. It was all a trick.<br /> <br /> Until one day he Awakened, and started doing Magick for real.<br /> <br /> Evidently, his disguise was good enough to fool the universe. Or at least that's his conclusion for how his Magick works. Indeed, he often has trouble believing it. As he grows in power and confidence, his ability to affect the world around him will expand. For now, his Effects tend to be Coincidental, if for no other reason than because he doesn't have the confidence to push into the Vulgar. In the pit of his stomach, he's convinced that he's only able to do what he does because he's kept the illusion going. That he has everyone fooled, including Reality itself.<br /> <br /> He thinks he's a fraud. But it seems he'll fake it until he makes it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}